(48115,80,'2025-04-17 15:45:37','2025-04-17 21:45:37','Now that renovations are complete, the Big printers are once again available. Come join our workshop to learn how to use the large format machines, advanced materials, and multi-material systems. The workshop is also open to any previous attendees to brush up on any updates and collaborate on our latest, most challenging projects.','Advanced 3d Printing Workshop (Large Format Printer Training)','','publish','closed','closed','','advanced-3d-printing-workshop-large-format-printer-training','','','2025-04-17 15:46:57','2025-04-17 21:46:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=48115',0,'event','',0),
(50027,80,'2025-06-18 11:48:16','2025-06-18 17:48:16','Carrot, our large-format printer, is finally online again! And with all-new upgrades!\r\nThis class will cover the large-format printers, as well as other advanced topics.\r\n\r\n<strong>Prerequisite</strong>: This class is open to all members who have completed the standard 3D Print class.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Advanced 3d Printing Workshop (Large Format Printer Training)','','publish','closed','closed','','advanced-3d-printing-workshop-large-format-printer-training-2','','','2025-06-18 11:51:15','2025-06-18 17:51:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50027',0,'event','',0),
(50028,80,'2025-06-18 11:50:29','2025-06-18 17:50:29','The Mk4S kits are in for our Prusas!   Come help install the upgrades, learn how to maintain and troubleshoot the machines, or just hang out and watch.','Prusa Mk4S upgrade workshop','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-mk4s-upgrade-workshop','','','2025-06-18 11:50:29','2025-06-18 17:50:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50028',0,'event','',0),
(50273,80,'2025-06-26 18:33:22','2025-06-27 00:33:22','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-31','','','2025-06-26 18:33:22','2025-06-27 00:33:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50273',0,'event','',0),
(50274,80,'2025-06-26 18:34:24','2025-06-27 00:34:24','Carrot, our large-format printer, is finally online again! And with all-new upgrades!\r\nThis class will cover the large-format printers, as well as other advanced topics.\r\n\r\n<strong>Prerequisite</strong>: This class is open to all members who have completed the standard 3D Print class.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Advanced 3d Printing Workshop (Large Format Printer Training)','','publish','closed','closed','','advanced-3d-printing-workshop-large-format-printer-training-3','','','2025-06-26 18:34:24','2025-06-27 00:34:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50274',0,'event','',0),
(50275,80,'2025-06-26 18:37:03','2025-06-27 00:37:03','Our Prusa XL is almost here!   We need volunteers to come help build and test the new machine, and learn how to use it.\r\nCome join the fun','Prusa XL build party','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-build-party','','','2025-06-26 18:37:03','2025-06-27 00:37:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50275',0,'event','',0),
(61732,109,'2026-05-08 17:07:58','2026-05-08 23:07:58','<p class="mb-ds2-10">Have you ever heard that Macs don\'t get malware? Well that\'s not true. Bad Brew was a click fix malware campaign that tricked users into downloading and running malware by imitating the homebrew package manager. I will compare an earlier and a more advanced malware sample that shows how the threat actors tactics changed over time</p>\r\n<p class="mb-ds2-10">Location: denhac classroom, denhac, 700 Kalamath Ave, Denver CO\r\nDate &amp; Time: May 22nd @ 7:00 p.m.\r\nNote: Bring a laptop and ethernet cable if desired.</p>','DC303: Reversing Bad Brew','','publish','closed','closed','','dc303-reversing-bad-brew','','','2026-05-08 17:07:58','2026-05-08 23:07:58','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61732',0,'event','',0),
(39083,199,'2024-05-28 13:17:17','2024-05-28 19:17:17','Learn how to use our CO2 lasers and get authorized.\r\n\r\nThis class is for members only.\r\n\r\nPlease read the wiki for more details:\r\n\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Laser Training','CO2 laser training & authorization','publish','closed','closed','','laser-training','','','2024-05-28 13:50:43','2024-05-28 19:50:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=39083',0,'event','',0),
