(69000,199,'2026-10-20 19:26:53','2026-10-21 01:26:53','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @CraigMurray','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-56','','','2026-10-20 19:26:53','2026-10-21 01:26:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69000',0,'event','',0),
(69003,199,'2026-10-20 19:29:31','2026-10-21 01:29:31','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @EvanRobertson','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-58','','','2026-10-20 19:29:31','2026-10-21 01:29:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69003',0,'event','',0),
(40935,460,'2024-08-02 13:03:39','2024-08-02 19:03:39','Learn to use the industrial sewing machine and get authorized to use it.\r\n\r\nThis class is available at no charge to denhac members only.\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Industrial Sewing Machine <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/kingmax-gc-8700d-industrial-straight-stitch-sewing-machine">read the wiki</a>.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-class-2','','','2024-08-02 13:10:48','2024-08-02 19:10:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=40935',0,'event','',0),
(42401,418,'2024-09-18 16:54:04','2024-09-18 22:54:04','Learn to use the Serger sewing machines and get authorized to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Sergers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/serger-sewing-machines&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2opdkSLiWhz_x4n9JVQkL9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Serger Sewing Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','serger-sewing-machine-authorization-class-2','','','2024-09-18 16:54:04','2024-09-18 22:54:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42401',0,'event','',0),
(43798,434,'2024-11-08 19:55:16','2024-11-09 02:55:16','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on plates of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with CAD, CAM, and CNC before using this tool.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-10','','','2024-11-08 19:55:16','2024-11-09 02:55:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43798',0,'event','',0),
(43820,418,'2024-11-09 18:02:11','2024-11-10 01:02:11','Learn to use the Single Needle Embroidery machine and get authorized to use it whenever you\'d like. The embroidery machines are perfect for adding a high quality stitched image onto fabric but can only embroider one color at a time before needing to be swapped manually.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Single Needle Embroidery machine, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/single-needle-embroidery-machine">read the wiki</a>.','Single Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','single-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-class','','','2024-11-09 18:02:11','2024-11-10 01:02:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43820',0,'event','',0),
(45898,434,'2025-01-28 13:22:14','2025-01-28 20:22:14','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>HOMEWORK:</strong></span> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-16','','','2025-01-28 13:22:14','2025-01-28 20:22:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45898',0,'event','',0),
(47739,434,'2025-04-07 12:32:42','2025-04-07 18:32:42','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-20','','','2025-04-07 12:36:14','2025-04-07 18:36:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47739',0,'event','',0),
(56824,238,'2026-01-04 13:47:36','2026-01-04 20:47:36','Open door meeting for the computer museum and retro technology.\r\n\r\nThese are low-key, open-door sessions to explore the vintage tech at denhac, share knowledge, and work on developing the computer museum. Whether you\'re new to retro computing or already into the hobby, this is a place to learn, collaborate, and help shape the next phase of the denhac computer museum. Drop in anytime. For the moment these will be free-form meetings with no set agenda. We can teach, game, chat, plan, code, repair, improve, build, solder, or anything of the like.\r\n\r\n<strong>Room:</strong> Fishbowl\r\n\r\n<strong>Slack:</strong> <em>#project-computer-museum</em>\r\n\r\nDon\'t forget that denhac also has Laserdiscs and vintage video game consoles. And the museum has a software PBX and some older networking tech.\r\n\r\nFeel free to reach out to <em>@joseph</em> or our channel on slack for questions/comments regarding this event.\r\n\r\n[caption id="attachment_53753" align="aligncenter" width="800"]<img class="size-full wp-image-53753" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/computer-museum-office-hours-event-image.jpg" alt="Computer Museum Office Hours" width="800" height="600" /> Computer Museum Office Hours[/caption]','Computer Museum Office Hours','Open door meeting for the computer museum and retro technology.','publish','closed','closed','','computer-museum-office-hours-2026-09-17','','','2026-03-05 18:17:15','2026-03-06 01:17:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/computer-museum-office-hours-2026-01-15-2026-01-22-2026-01-29-2026-02-05-2026-02-12-2026-02-19-2026-02-26-2026-03-05-2026-03-12-2026-03-19-2026-03-26-2026-04-02-2026-04-09-2026-04-16-202-10-2026-09-17',0,'event','',0),
