(57049,303,'2026-01-09 11:48:06','2026-01-09 18:48:06','Have you been to a locksport night (second Tuesdays from 8-10pm)? This event will show an expanded look at locksport topics in a casual, flexible environment. Topics not formalized, but may include varieties of locking mechanisms, picking techniques, tool fabrication, research and history, as well as a "book club" for locks ;)\r\n\r\nThis event is an adventure in building the ship as it\'s pushed out to sea. Hope to see you there!\r\n\r\nThis workshop is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. If you\'re interested in becoming a denhac member you should join us at a Tuesday night open house from 8-10pm.','Intermediate Locksport','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-locksport','','','2026-01-09 11:48:57','2026-01-09 18:48:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57049',0,'event','',0),
(57471,238,'2026-01-21 13:11:03','2026-01-21 20:11:03','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-42','','','2026-01-24 21:56:09','2026-01-25 04:56:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57471',0,'event','',0),
(57474,238,'2026-01-21 13:40:57','2026-01-21 20:40:57','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-43','','','2026-02-06 23:13:08','2026-02-07 06:13:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57474',0,'event','',0),
(57553,238,'2026-01-21 17:58:02','2026-01-22 00:58:02','Special interest group meeting for stained glass and glass working.','SIG Glass Monthly Meeting','','publish','closed','closed','','sig-glass-monthly-meeting','','','2026-01-21 17:58:02','2026-01-22 00:58:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57553',0,'event','',0),
(57555,238,'2026-01-21 17:59:28','2026-01-22 00:59:28','Show off your glass projects, toast/roast your experience working on glass at denhac, and get mentally prepared for the glass SIG meeting at 7pm.','Glass SIG pre-meeting Show-Off','','publish','closed','closed','','glass-sig-pre-meeting-show-off','','','2026-01-21 17:59:28','2026-01-22 00:59:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57555',0,'event','',0),
(59017,303,'2026-03-01 17:07:44','2026-03-02 00:07:44','Come learn and practice "float picking," a lockpicking tensioning technique necessary to pick many high-security locks. Some tools and materials will be provided -- you are encouraged to bring a bench vise and your own tools if you have them.\r\n\r\n<br aria-hidden="true" />(Please note this is *different* than the Lockpicking 101 class; you are very welcome to come to this event regardless of experience or skill level, however no 101 lecture is planned during this event.)','Intermediate Locksport - Float Picking','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-locksport-float-picking','','','2026-03-01 17:07:44','2026-03-02 00:07:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59017',0,'event','',0),
(60833,238,'2026-04-18 13:50:57','2026-04-18 19:50:57','<p data-path-to-node="5">We are initiating a formal effort to improve our shared space! We\'re focusing on organization, floorplan flow, and upgrading our member storage system.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6">As many of you may know, we have some projects already in motion, including planned upgrades scheduled for April 25th. Our goal for this meeting is to begin building out an actionable plan and budget for our new member storage.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7">With the next board budget proposal deadline on <b data-path-to-node="7" data-index-in-node="48">May 4th</b>, this is our window to solidify these plans into a concrete proposal.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="10">Agenda</h2>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="12,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="12,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Lava→Fish Shelf Project:</b> Finalizing execution details for the work currently in motion.</li>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="12,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="12,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Member Storage:</b> Turning long-standing ideas into a formal plan for new shelving.</li>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="12,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="12,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Budgeting:</b> Outlining costs to ensure we are ready for the May 4th board submission.</li>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="12,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="12,3,0" data-index-in-node="0">Volunteer Coordination:</b> Identifying project leads and establishing a build schedule.</li>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="12,0,0"><strong>Future Planning:</strong> Brainstorm ideas for the next meeting (chairs, tables, drawers, boxes, layouts)</li>\r\n</ol>\r\nWe\'ll have a Google Meet session open for remote attendance.\r\n<p data-path-to-node="14">Otherwise, we want this to be a space-wide effort, so your input is vital even if you cannot attend. Please join the <b data-path-to-node="14" data-index-in-node="106">#help-storage</b> channel on Slack to stay in the loop, view the meeting notes, and contribute to the build schedule as it develops.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="15">We look forward to seeing you there and moving toward a more organized, sustainable denhac.</p>','denhac Storage & Organization','','publish','closed','closed','','denhac-storage-organization','','','2026-04-19 13:07:34','2026-04-19 19:07:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60833',0,'event','',0),
(61230,336,'2026-04-28 23:11:23','2026-04-29 05:11:23','With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-22','','','2026-05-26 10:36:10','2026-05-26 16:36:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61230',0,'event','',0),
