(40763,546,'2024-07-27 20:04:58','2024-07-28 02:04:58','Learn to use the 7-needle embroidery machine and get authorized to use it.\r\n\r\nThis class is for denhac members only.\r\n\r\nTo read more about the 7-Needle Embroidery Machine <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/seven-needle-embroidery-machine?seq_no=2">read the wiki</a>.','7-Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-class','','','2024-07-27 20:04:58','2024-07-28 02:04:58','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=40763',0,'event','',0),
(41646,564,'2024-08-21 13:38:04','2024-08-21 19:38:04','Learn the basics of CNC machining and get certified to use the CNC Router.\r\n\r\nThis class is available at no cost and is available to denhac members only.\r\n\r\nPlease <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/cnc-training">read the wiki</a> for more details. Reading of the Wiki and watching the videos under the <strong>homework</strong> heading is a required prerequisite to the authorization class.','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class','','','2024-08-21 13:38:04','2024-08-21 19:38:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41646',0,'event','',0),
(41903,564,'2024-08-29 13:41:29','2024-08-29 19:41:29','Learn the basics of CNC machining and get certified to use the CNC Router.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no cost.\r\n\r\nPlease <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/cnc-training">read the wiki</a> for more details. Reading of the Wiki and watching the videos under the <strong>homework</strong> heading is a required prerequisite to the authorization class.\r\n\r\nThis \'class\' mostly only teaches safety. As with any kind of CNC machine the magic happens in the software, and software training is not provided in this class.','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-4','','','2024-08-29 13:41:29','2024-08-29 19:41:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41903',0,'event','',0),
(41904,564,'2024-08-29 13:43:03','2024-08-29 19:43:03','Learn the basics of CNC machining and get certified to use the CNC Router.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no cost.\r\n\r\nPlease <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/cnc-training">read the wiki</a> for more details. Reading of the Wiki and watching the videos under the <strong>homework</strong> heading is a required prerequisite to the authorization class.\r\n\r\nThis \'class\' mostly only teaches safety. As with any kind of CNC machine the magic happens in the software, and software training is not provided in this class.','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-5','','','2024-08-29 13:43:03','2024-08-29 19:43:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41904',0,'event','',0),
(41905,564,'2024-08-29 13:46:00','2024-08-29 19:46:00','This class provides training and authorization to use our fleet of Prusa Mk4 FDM printers.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize you to use the Large Format FDM printers, but this class is a prerequisite to take the Advanced FDM Workshop.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no cost.\r\n\r\nCheck out <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/prusa-3d-printer">the wiki</a> for more information.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-6','','','2024-08-29 13:46:00','2024-08-29 19:46:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41905',0,'event','',0),
(42063,460,'2024-09-05 23:59:24','2024-09-06 05:59:24','Learn to use our rug making kit!\r\n\r\nThis class is only for denhac members, and is offered at no additional cost.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our rug tufting equipment, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/tufting-gun">read the wiki</a>.','Rug Tufting Class','','publish','closed','closed','','rug-tufting','','','2024-09-06 00:00:07','2024-09-06 06:00:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42063',0,'event','',0),
(42751,564,'2024-09-29 23:05:01','2024-09-30 05:05:01','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-6','','','2024-10-06 15:58:02','2024-10-06 21:58:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42751',0,'event','',0),
(43178,564,'2024-10-16 12:20:10','2024-10-16 18:20:10','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on plywood, hardwood, and aluminum plate.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #000000;"><strong>HOMEWORK:</strong></span>\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with CAD, CAM, and CNC before using this tool.</strong> </span>\r\n\r\n<strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-8','','','2024-10-23 12:08:18','2024-10-23 18:08:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43178',0,'event','',0),
(43995,564,'2024-11-15 21:14:19','2024-11-16 04:14:19','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-13','','','2024-11-15 21:18:26','2024-11-16 04:18:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43995',0,'event','',0),
(50024,484,'2025-06-18 11:28:39','2025-06-18 17:28:39','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="-1" role="presentation" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-3','','','2025-06-18 11:28:39','2025-06-18 17:28:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50024',0,'event','',0),
(53459,477,'2025-10-01 11:48:27','2025-10-01 17:48:27','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use Table Saw Only. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~2 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "Table Saw"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-table-saw','','','2025-10-01 11:48:27','2025-10-01 17:48:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53459',0,'event','',0),
(63385,498,'2026-06-19 13:38:16','2026-06-19 19:38:16','<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Learn the fundamentals of screen printing, hands-on with Kate! All materials are provided, and you\'ll learn the tools and techniques needed to pull a clean, professional print.</p>\r\n<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">For this session, you\'ll choose from a set of pre-made designs rather than printing your own artwork, this lets us focus the class time on teaching the actual technique, which you can then apply to your own designs afterward. Please bring your own material to screen print on - we will be using the Denhac logo as an option.</p>\r\n<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">We\'ll start in the Fishbowl to gather supplies and run through the basics, then move to the garage to print, since wet projects stay out of the textiles space for cleaning reasons.</p>','Learn Screen printing at Denhac!','','publish','closed','closed','','learn-screen-printing-at-denhac','','','2026-06-23 20:16:17','2026-06-24 02:16:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63385',0,'event','',0),
(67180,498,'2026-09-11 21:00:11','2026-09-12 03:00:11','In this class, you will learn how to apply emulsion to a screen, burn an image onto it, and use it to apply ink to a shirt.\r\n\r\nFor this class, you will need to bring a blank cotton t-shirt or canvas tote bag.\r\n\r\nShirts will not be provided for you.','Screen Printing Basics','','publish','closed','closed','','screen-printing-basics','','','2026-09-18 19:15:48','2026-09-19 01:15:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67180',0,'event','',0),
(43996,564,'2024-11-15 21:17:43','2024-11-16 04:17:43','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on plates of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with CAD, CAM, and CNC before using this tool.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-12','','','2024-11-16 12:53:30','2024-11-16 19:53:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43996',0,'event','',0),
(45353,564,'2025-01-13 12:55:07','2025-01-13 19:55:07','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-15','','','2025-01-13 12:55:07','2025-01-13 19:55:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45353',0,'event','',0),
(45955,564,'2025-01-30 13:31:02','2025-01-30 20:31:02','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d printer authorization class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-18','','','2025-01-30 14:42:53','2025-01-30 21:42:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45955',0,'event','',0),
(47524,564,'2025-03-29 23:51:05','2025-03-30 05:51:05','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-19','','','2025-03-29 23:51:05','2025-03-30 05:51:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47524',0,'event','',0),
(49319,564,'2025-05-25 14:02:07','2025-05-25 20:02:07','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-23','','','2025-05-25 14:02:07','2025-05-25 20:02:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49319',0,'event','',0),
(49711,564,'2025-06-07 22:45:09','2025-06-08 04:45:09','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete.\r\n\r\nThese machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU. This class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-28','','','2025-06-07 22:45:09','2025-06-08 04:45:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49711',0,'event','',0),
(51623,564,'2025-08-08 21:32:41','2025-08-09 03:32:41','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-24','','','2025-08-08 21:32:41','2025-08-09 03:32:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51623',0,'event','',0),
(51900,564,'2025-08-16 09:46:05','2025-08-16 15:46:05','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-4','','','2025-08-16 09:46:05','2025-08-16 15:46:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51900',0,'event','',0),
(52712,564,'2025-09-08 13:17:57','2025-09-08 19:17:57','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-26','','','2025-09-08 13:46:13','2025-09-08 19:46:13','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52712',0,'event','',0),
