(60173,564,'2026-03-31 15:44:10','2026-03-31 21:44:10','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-7','','','2026-03-31 15:45:37','2026-03-31 21:45:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60173',0,'event','',0),
(60630,564,'2026-04-12 11:01:47','2026-04-12 17:01:47','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-49','','','2026-04-16 09:05:50','2026-04-16 15:05:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60630',0,'event','',0),
(61788,564,'2026-05-09 21:35:08','2026-05-10 03:35:08','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-52','','','2026-05-09 21:35:08','2026-05-10 03:35:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61788',0,'event','',0),
(39004,686,'2024-05-24 13:28:59','2024-05-24 19:28:59','Join us as we work on our foundry equipment and melt some copper.\r\n\r\nTraining available/no experience required.\r\n\r\n<strong>All participants must wear non-synthetic clothes and shoes! </strong>We also recommend that you bring your own respirator.\r\n\r\nMembers only.\r\n\r\nContact <code>@uatu</code> on slack with questions.','Foundry Work & Copper Pour','Foundry Session: Copper pour','publish','closed','closed','','foundry-work-copper-pour','','','2024-06-26 15:52:57','2024-06-26 21:52:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=39004',0,'event','',0),
(39007,576,'2024-05-24 14:33:48','2024-05-24 20:33:48','<p class="mb-4">Get trained and signed off to use some of the woodworking tools at <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">denhac</a>. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading the <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/wood-working-area" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">woodshop wiki page</a> and all tool wiki pages linked below</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.</p>\r\n<p class="mb-4">This class includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="pl-5 list-disc mb-4">\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/saw-stop" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Saw Stop table saw</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/jointer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Powermatic jointer</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/dw375-planer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Dewalt planer</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><strong>Cost:</strong>\r\ndenhac <strong>members: Free!</strong>\r\n<strong>non members:</strong> If you\'re interested in this class you must first become a denhac member. First see our website: <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/howto" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">https://denhac.org/</a>. Think our organization sounds cool and interested in joining? Attend an <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://www.meetup.com/denhac-hackerspace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open house tour</a>, every Tuesday 8 - 10pm. After your tour if you like our community - you can sign up, show us your official ID, and become a member.</p>','Woodshop Training','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-training-2','','','2024-06-01 22:43:12','2024-06-02 04:43:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=39007',0,'event','',0),
(39141,657,'2024-05-29 12:40:28','2024-05-29 18:40:28','Get authorized to use our resin printers.\r\n\r\n<strong>You must bring your own respirator.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is for members only.\r\n\r\nFor more details, see the wiki:\r\n\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Resin Printer Training','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-printer-training','','','2024-05-30 20:22:50','2024-05-31 02:22:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=39141',0,'event','',0),
