(39926,576,'2024-06-25 20:15:51','2024-06-26 02:15:51','<p class="mb-4">Get trained and signed off to use some of the woodworking tools at <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">denhac</a>. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading the <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/wood-working-area" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">woodshop wiki page</a> and all tool wiki pages linked below</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.</p>\r\n<p class="mb-4">This class includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="pl-5 list-disc mb-4">\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/saw-stop" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Saw Stop table saw</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/jointer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Powermatic jointer</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/dw375-planer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Dewalt planer</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><strong>Cost:</strong>\r\ndenhac <strong>members: Free!</strong>\r\n<strong>non members:</strong> If you\'re interested in this class you must first become a denhac member. First see our website: <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/howto" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">https://denhac.org/</a>. Think our organization sounds cool and interested in joining? Attend an <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://www.meetup.com/denhac-hackerspace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open house tour</a>, every Tuesday 8 - 10pm. After your tour if you like our community - you can sign up, show us your official ID, and become a member.</p>','Woodshop Training','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-training-4','','','2024-06-25 20:15:51','2024-06-26 02:15:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=39926',0,'event','',0),
(41995,657,'2024-09-03 13:50:06','2024-09-03 19:50:06','Learn the basics of resin printing and get authorized to use denhac\'s resin printers. Resin printing can produce parts with a much finer level of detail than our FDM 3d printers, great for things like mini-figures.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our resin 3d printers <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process">read the wiki</a>.','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class','','','2024-09-03 13:50:06','2024-09-03 19:50:06','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41995',0,'event','',0),
(43147,657,'2024-10-15 15:12:30','2024-10-15 21:12:30','Learn to use the Resin 3d Printers and get authorized to use them. These machines work by dipping a plate into a vat of photosensitive resin and using a high resolution LCD screen to selectively cure layers of the print by shining black and white images onto the bottom of vat/the current top layer of the model as it prints. This method of 3d printing is much more precise and produces much higher resolution results than the typical FDM (nozzle-style) 3d printing process.\r\n\r\nAlthough the resin tent is actively fumigated, a half-mask respirator with P100 (oil based) filters is required to use the resin printers. The mask with the filters can be found as a pack online for less than $30 usually.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the resin 3d printers, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process">check out the wiki</a>.','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class-2','','','2024-10-15 21:56:53','2024-10-16 03:56:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43147',0,'event','',0),
(44092,566,'2024-11-19 00:02:27','2024-11-19 07:02:27','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-7','','','2024-11-19 00:02:27','2024-11-19 07:02:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=44092',0,'event','',0),
(45696,566,'2025-01-21 13:04:05','2025-01-21 20:04:05','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-13','','','2025-02-13 09:03:24','2025-02-13 16:03:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45696',0,'event','',0),
(46225,566,'2025-02-10 14:35:14','2025-02-10 21:35:14','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-15','','','2025-02-13 08:54:44','2025-02-13 15:54:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46225',0,'event','',0),
(62963,564,'2026-06-07 19:39:03','2026-06-08 01:39:03','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-53','','','2026-06-07 19:40:17','2026-06-08 01:40:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62963',0,'event','',0),
(62977,564,'2026-06-07 22:12:04','2026-06-08 04:12:04','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-58','','','2026-06-07 22:12:04','2026-06-08 04:12:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62977',0,'event','',0),
(63566,564,'2026-06-25 07:48:38','2026-06-25 13:48:38','Come hang out, and get some hands-on time with the 3D Scanner! Bring a small object which you\'d like to scan. We\'ll be going over basic setup, and scanning procedures, and spend some time scanning objects people bring in to experience the potential challenges.\r\n\r\n<a href="https://revopedia.revopoint3d.com/en/MetroYSeries/Usermanual">Revopoint Metro Y Pro</a>','Revopoint Metro Y Pro Workshop (3D Scanning small items)','','publish','closed','closed','','revopoint-metro-y-pro-workshop-3d-scanning-small-items','','','2026-06-25 07:48:38','2026-06-25 13:48:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63566',0,'event','',0),
(64000,564,'2026-07-06 14:43:25','2026-07-06 20:43:25','<strong>Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-2','','','2026-07-09 08:19:48','2026-07-09 14:19:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64000',0,'event','',0),
(65027,564,'2026-08-01 07:16:59','2026-08-01 13:16:59','Learn to use the Prusa MK4S and Core One+ (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-11','','','2026-08-01 07:16:59','2026-08-01 13:16:59','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65027',0,'event','',0),
(67350,564,'2026-09-15 17:19:42','2026-09-15 23:19:42','Help out, check in with projects, and have fun! No experience necessary. Come when you can, leave when you want.\r\n\r\nThanks! <img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f6e0-fe0f.png" alt=":hammer_and_wrench:" aria-label="hammer and wrench emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":hammer_and_wrench:" /><img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f383.png" alt=":jack_o_lantern:" aria-label="jack o lantern emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":jack_o_lantern:" />','Haunted House Club Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-club-office-hours-5','','','2026-09-15 17:19:42','2026-09-15 23:19:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67350',0,'event','',0),
(67351,564,'2026-09-15 17:20:05','2026-09-15 23:20:05','Time to work on projects, ask questions, or generally pitch in for this year\'s haunted house. All are welcome, no experience necessary!','Haunted House Club Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-club-office-hours-6','','','2026-09-15 17:20:05','2026-09-15 23:20:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67351',0,'event','',0),
(68599,564,'2026-10-10 17:14:51','2026-10-10 23:14:51','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-40','','','2026-10-10 17:14:51','2026-10-10 23:14:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68599',0,'event','',0),
(38943,689,'2024-05-23 21:52:02','2024-05-24 03:52:02','<p class="mb-4">The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning. <strong>This class is required to operate the denhac lathe.</strong></p>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em></p>','Wood Lathe Training','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-training','','','2024-05-30 20:25:02','2024-05-31 02:25:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=38943',0,'event','',0),
(38997,689,'2024-05-23 21:40:39','2024-05-24 03:40:39','<p class="mb-4">Get trained and signed off to use some of the woodworking tools at <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">denhac</a>. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading the <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/wood-working-area" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">woodshop wiki page</a> and all tool wiki pages linked below</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.</p>\r\n<p class="mb-4">This class includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="pl-5 list-disc mb-4">\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/saw-stop" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Saw Stop table saw</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/jointer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Powermatic jointer</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/dw375-planer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Dewalt planer</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><strong>Cost:</strong>\r\ndenhac <strong>members: Free!</strong>\r\n<strong>non members:</strong> If you\'re interested in this class you must first become a denhac member. First see our website: <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/howto" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">https://denhac.org/</a>. Think our organization sounds cool and interested in joining? Attend an <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://www.meetup.com/denhac-hackerspace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open house tour</a>, every Tuesday 8 - 10pm. After your tour if you like our community - you can sign up, show us your official ID, and become a member.</p>','Woodshop Training','Woodshop training for: Table saw, Jointer, Planer, and Router Table','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-training-2024-06-09','','','2024-05-30 20:26:05','2024-05-31 02:26:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/woodshop-training-2024-06-09',0,'event','',0),
