(57723,727,'2026-01-27 19:33:40','2026-01-28 02:33:40','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-12','','','2026-01-27 19:33:40','2026-01-28 02:33:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57723',0,'event','',0),
(57735,689,'2026-01-27 19:48:11','2026-01-28 02:48:11','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-43','','','2026-01-27 19:48:11','2026-01-28 02:48:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57735',0,'event','',0),
(57738,689,'2026-01-27 19:53:09','2026-01-28 02:53:09','<em><strong>A wood lathe authorization is required for each attendee. Do not sign up for this class if you haven\'t been certified to use the wood lathe yet.</strong></em>\r\n\r\nThis class will demonstrate the basics of (safe) lidded vessel turning. This is just a demo, and may not include any hands on experience.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Lidded Vessels Demo (Prior Wood Lathe Auth Required)','','publish','closed','closed','','lidded-vessels-demo-prior-wood-lathe-auth-required','','','2026-01-27 19:53:09','2026-01-28 02:53:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57738',0,'event','',0),
