(58567,728,'2026-02-20 08:54:11','2026-02-20 15:54:11','<h4><span style="color: #484848;">Agentic RAG: Building autonomous systems you can actually hack.</span></h4>\r\n<h5>Presenter: Subbarao Pydikondala</h5>\r\n<h1><a href="https://r5.ieee.org/denver-cs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://r5.ieee.org/denver-cs/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1771631279971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UF5NN3gsubantlbzNeiNd"><img class="CToWUd alignright" src="https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/meips/ADKq_NZaFzq1kJxUVgsH276txzT_F2Onc-ohuleknvYOC5BMJnEVl2aPgYdmVfzIVBcgUA426TJZHgHnL4qPlyFoyarDfQOkoWL49UOqDm40jWoTZFfaiSLtqrqS4bv94ogbks0UiIUd_8iOfs74J-pB__B7mCQIzXaahronnK4_T7zmVlraTQ=s0-d-e1-ft#https://r5.ieee.org/denver-cs/wp-content/uploads/sites/66/sites/66/2026/01/Subbarao-Pydikondala-March-2026.jpg" alt="" width="230" height="265" data-bit="iit" /></a></h1>\r\n<em>AI Technology Strategist</em>\r\n<em>Senior Member, and IEEE Denver Computer Society Vice Chair</em>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Mr. Subbarao Pydikondala holds a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science and Engineering from Bharathidasan University and an Executive MBA from Quantic. With over 20 years of experience, Mr. Pydikondala serves as a Principal Architect at DocuSign, leading enterprise transformation initiatives across AI, Revenue Operations, and integrated platforms such as Salesforce, Microsoft, and Oracle.\r\nMr. Pydikondala is recognized for driving innovation in the enterprise domain and has presented at industry-leading events, including Dreamforce, AI Summit New York focusing on Agentic AI, and its safe adoption in enterprise workflows. Mr. Pydikondala’s work bridges strategic vision and real-world implementation, shaping how organizations embrace AI with digital agility. In addition, Mr. Pydikondala actively contributes to the IEEE Denver Computer Society, mentoring emerging tech talent and advancing community learning.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>','AI &amp; Computer Science Club','','publish','closed','closed','','ai-computer-science-club-2','','','2026-02-20 08:54:11','2026-02-20 15:54:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58567',0,'event','',0),
(58647,689,'2026-02-22 13:11:44','2026-02-22 20:11:44','<p class="mb-4"><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong></p>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<p class="mb-4">The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning. <strong>This class is required to operate the denhac lathe.</strong></p>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em></p>','Wood Lathe Training','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-training-4','','','2026-02-22 13:11:44','2026-02-22 20:11:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58647',0,'event','',0),
(59929,689,'2026-03-24 14:37:59','2026-03-24 20:37:59','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-16','','','2026-03-24 14:38:16','2026-03-24 20:38:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59929',0,'event','',0),
(61286,689,'2026-04-30 10:22:27','2026-04-30 16:22:27','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-42','','','2026-04-30 10:59:14','2026-04-30 16:59:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61286',0,'event','',0),
(62395,689,'2026-05-26 10:51:42','2026-05-26 16:51:42','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-44','','','2026-05-26 10:51:42','2026-05-26 16:51:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62395',0,'event','',0),
(63472,689,'2026-06-22 11:38:57','2026-06-22 17:38:57','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-28','','','2026-06-22 18:30:43','2026-06-23 00:30:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63472',0,'event','',0),
(38933,745,'2024-05-23 21:27:20','2024-05-24 03:27:20','<p class="mb-4">Get trained and signed off to use some of the woodworking tools at <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">denhac</a>. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading the <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/wood-working-area" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">woodshop wiki page</a> and all tool wiki pages linked below</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.</p>\r\n<p class="mb-4">This class includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="pl-5 list-disc mb-4">\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/saw-stop" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Saw Stop table saw</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/jointer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Powermatic jointer</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/dw375-planer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Dewalt planer</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><strong>Cost:</strong>\r\ndenhac <strong>members: Free!</strong>\r\n<strong>non members:</strong> If you\'re interested in this class you must first become a denhac member. First see our website: <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/howto" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">https://denhac.org/</a>. Think our organization sounds cool and interested in joining? Attend an <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://www.meetup.com/denhac-hackerspace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open house tour</a>, every Tuesday 8 - 10pm. After your tour if you like our community - you can sign up, show us your official ID, and become a member.</p>','Woodshop Training','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-training','','','2024-05-30 20:23:19','2024-05-31 02:23:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=38933',0,'event','',0),
(38970,745,'2024-05-23 23:03:30','2024-05-24 05:03:30','<p class="mb-4">The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning. <strong>This class is required to operate the denhac lathe.</strong></p>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em></p>','Wood Lathe Training','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-training-3','','','2024-05-30 20:26:53','2024-05-31 02:26:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=38970',0,'event','',0),
