(46768,745,'2025-03-01 15:54:41','2025-03-01 22:54:41','Learn to use the pen mandrel for the wood lathe! Although this training is not required to use the pen mandrel, the instructional class will definitely help if you\'ve never used one before.','Pen Turning Class (Wood Lathe Certification Required)','','publish','closed','closed','','pen-turning-class-wood-lathe-certification-required','','','2025-03-18 18:00:19','2025-03-19 00:00:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46768',0,'event','',0),
(47060,732,'2025-03-12 14:32:38','2025-03-12 20:32:38','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">check out the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-17','','','2025-03-12 14:32:38','2025-03-12 20:32:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47060',0,'event','',0),
(47529,745,'2025-03-30 00:08:42','2025-03-30 06:08:42','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-24','','','2025-03-30 00:08:42','2025-03-30 06:08:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47529',0,'event','',0),
(43519,760,'2024-10-29 15:37:02','2024-10-29 21:37:02','Become authorized to use the denhac mig welder. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before they\'re allowed to use the MIG machine. The class will cover basic safety training regarding the MIG welder but will not be an exhaustive lesson on welding. This class is also a heavily recommended but optional prerequisite to taking the TIG welder authorization class.\r\n\r\nThe MIG welder uses a pistol-style torch to deliver current carrying wire protected by inert gas. MIG welding is easier than the TIG welding but offers less control of the weld. The difference is very akin to using an automatic (MIG) vs manual (TIG) transmission.\r\n\r\n<strong>Attendees must wear non-synthetic clothing and shoes.</strong> Welding helmets, jackets, and gloves are provided, but you’re also welcome to bring your own. We do not have shoe covers so make sure to wear some good boots or something you can drop hot slag on.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','MIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','mig-welder-authorization-class','','','2024-10-29 15:38:02','2024-10-29 21:38:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43519',0,'event','',0),
