(57730,745,'2026-01-27 19:45:12','2026-01-28 02:45:12','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-13','','','2026-01-27 19:45:12','2026-01-28 02:45:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57730',0,'event','',0),
(59928,745,'2026-03-24 14:36:44','2026-03-24 20:36:44','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-15','','','2026-03-24 14:36:44','2026-03-24 20:36:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59928',0,'event','',0),
(66182,745,'2026-08-26 23:14:35','2026-08-27 05:14:35','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-36','','','2026-08-27 10:18:55','2026-08-27 16:18:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66182',0,'event','',0),
(66203,745,'2026-08-27 10:35:18','2026-08-27 16:35:18','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\nThis class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe. This class has limited attendance and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and decide not to go, please cancel your RSVP so the next person on the waiting list can attend!\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, checkout the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-3','','','2026-08-27 10:35:18','2026-08-27 16:35:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66203',0,'event','',0),
(68409,745,'2026-10-07 00:45:01','2026-10-07 06:45:01','<em><strong>A wood lathe authorization is required for each attendee. Do not sign up for this class if you haven\'t been certified to use the wood lathe yet.</strong></em>\r\n\r\nThis class will demonstrate the basics of (safe) bowl turning and using the chuck attachment in the headstock. This is just a demo, and may not include any hands on experience.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Bowl Turning Demo Class (Prior Wood Lathe Auth Required)','','publish','closed','closed','','bowl-turning-demo-class-prior-wood-lathe-auth-required-8','','','2026-10-07 00:45:01','2026-10-07 06:45:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68409',0,'event','',0),
(68412,745,'2026-10-07 00:44:54','2026-10-07 06:44:54','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\nThis class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe. This class has limited attendance and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and decide not to go, please cancel your RSVP so the next person on the waiting list can attend!\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, checkout the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-4','','','2026-10-15 10:21:52','2026-10-15 16:21:52','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68412',0,'event','',0),
(42590,794,'2024-09-24 19:14:37','2024-09-25 01:14:37','Learn to use MicroPython to control a Raspberry Pico microcontroller. This is a two-part class meant to introduce microcontrollers to complete beginners in the field.\r\n\r\nMicrocontrollers are probably the most straightforward platform for controlling the real world with code. By using MicroPython you can manipulate small circuits connected to the device that can read sensors, drive motors, send data and requests over the internet, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nMake sure to come prepared with a Raspberry Pico W (V1 or V2) and the associated programming cable. All other hardware like resistors and LEDs should be available at denhac already.','Introduction to MicroPython (Part 1)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-micropython-part-1','','','2024-09-30 11:56:45','2024-09-30 17:56:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42590',0,'event','',0),
(42591,794,'2024-09-24 19:16:51','2024-09-25 01:16:51','Learn to use MicroPython to control a Raspberry Pico microcontroller. This is the second part of a two-part class meant to introduce microcontrollers to complete beginners in the field. If you already have some experience with the Pico microcontroller you\'re welcome to attend, but the rest of the class will be picking up where they left off in <a href="https://denhac.org/events/introduction-to-micropython-part-1">part one</a>.\r\n\r\nMicrocontrollers are probably the most straightforward platform for controlling the real world with code. By using MicroPython you can manipulate small circuits connected to the device that can read sensors, drive motors, send data and requests over the internet, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nMake sure to come prepared with a Raspberry Pico W (V1 or V2) and the associated programming cable. All other hardware like resistors and LEDs should be available at denhac already.','Introduction to MicroPython (Part 2)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-micropython-part-2','','','2024-09-30 11:57:11','2024-09-30 17:57:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42591',0,'event','',0),
(42759,794,'2024-09-30 11:59:04','2024-09-30 17:59:04','Learn to become a HAM radio operator, get a callsign, and pass the necessary exams required to legally operate radio equipment.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Ham Radio Study Group','','publish','closed','closed','','ham-radio-study-group','','','2024-09-30 11:59:04','2024-09-30 17:59:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42759',0,'event','',0),
(43866,804,'2024-11-11 01:06:57','2024-11-11 08:06:57','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on plates of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with CAD, CAM, and CNC before using this tool.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-11','','','2024-11-11 01:06:57','2024-11-11 08:06:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43866',0,'event','',0),
(45010,804,'2024-12-27 13:10:32','2024-12-27 20:10:32','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>HOMEWORK:</strong></span> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-13','','','2024-12-27 13:10:32','2024-12-27 20:10:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45010',0,'event','',0),
(45058,804,'2024-12-30 04:48:12','2024-12-30 11:48:12','Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>HOMEWORK:</strong></span> <strong>On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-14','','','2024-12-30 04:48:12','2024-12-30 11:48:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45058',0,'event','',0),
(45689,837,'2025-01-21 12:43:34','2025-01-21 19:43:34','Learn the basics of resin printing and get authorized to use denhac\'s resin printers. Resin printing can produce parts with a much finer level of detail than our FDM 3d printers, great for things like mini-figures.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our resin 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jookVGJH8eJ9t8Zodltd1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class-3','','','2025-01-21 12:43:34','2025-01-21 19:43:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45689',0,'event','',0),
(45690,837,'2025-01-21 12:45:35','2025-01-21 19:45:35','Learn the basics of resin printing and get authorized to use denhac\'s resin printers. Resin printing can produce parts with a much finer level of detail than our FDM 3d printers, great for things like mini-figures.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our resin 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jookVGJH8eJ9t8Zodltd1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class-4','','','2025-01-21 12:45:35','2025-01-21 19:45:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45690',0,'event','',0),
(46186,885,'2025-02-08 17:25:57','2025-02-09 00:25:57','Join us for an instructional class on soldering. This class will cover the basics of through-hole soldering so that you can get started assembling basic circuits.\r\n\r\nStudents will need a soldering project kit to participate in this class. Kits will be available at the class to any member that makes a $8 or more donation to denhac\'s electronics Special Interest Group (SIG). Students are also welcome to bring their own through-hole soldering kit.','Guided Introduction to Soldering','','publish','closed','closed','','guided-introduction-to-soldering','','','2025-03-12 14:28:06','2025-03-12 20:28:06','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46186',0,'event','',0),
(46944,840,'2025-03-08 11:14:27','2025-03-08 18:14:27','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">check out the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-16','','','2025-03-08 11:18:10','2025-03-08 18:18:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46944',0,'event','',0),
(47832,789,'2025-04-10 17:28:35','2025-04-10 23:28:35','A study session for the Fundamentals of Engineering exam through the Emily Griffiths CAREERS program.\r\n\r\n<strong>Note:</strong> This event is not open to the public, attendees are coordinated through Emily Griffiths','Emily Griffiths FE Exam Study Session','','publish','closed','closed','','emily-griffiths-fe-exam-study-session','','','2025-04-10 17:28:35','2025-04-10 23:28:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47832',0,'event','',0),
(49023,804,'2025-05-15 13:03:48','2025-05-15 19:03:48','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-22','','','2025-05-15 13:03:48','2025-05-15 19:03:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49023',0,'event','',0),
(50272,837,'2025-06-26 18:30:21','2025-06-27 00:30:21','Learn the basics of resin printing and get authorized to use denhac\'s resin printers. Resin printing can produce parts with a much finer level of detail than our FDM 3d printers, great for things like mini-figures.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\n<strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Prior to training, read the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jookVGJH8eJ9t8Zodltd1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the resin printer wiki </a>and make a plan to <strong>bring PPE</strong> (a respirator).','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class-8','','','2025-06-26 18:30:21','2025-06-27 00:30:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50272',0,'event','',0),
