(60631,804,'2026-04-12 11:02:57','2026-04-12 17:02:57','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-50','','','2026-04-12 11:02:57','2026-04-12 17:02:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60631',0,'event','',0),
(66411,880,'2026-08-31 13:22:44','2026-08-31 19:22:44','Special interest group meeting for stained glass and glass working.','SIG Glass Meeting','SIG Glass Meeting','publish','closed','closed','','sig-glass-meeting-4','','','2026-08-31 13:22:44','2026-08-31 19:22:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66411',0,'event','',0),
(69454,837,'2026-10-31 12:20:09','2026-10-31 18:20:09','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-11','','','2026-10-31 12:20:09','2026-10-31 18:20:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69454',0,'event','',0),
