(43377,968,'2024-10-23 17:06:30','2024-10-23 23:06:30','A LAN Party open to any and all members of denhac and Clear Creek Makerspace! This event will mainly be in the Fishbowl but will expand to fill the Classroom and Lava Rooms as necessary.\r\n\r\nThere will be a limit of 45 gamers due to the physical constraints of our space, availability will be on a first come first serve basis so sign up today if you\'re interested in attending. Even though we have some limits we will do everything we can to make sure that everyone who wants to participate may do so.\r\n\r\nAlthough attendees are welcome to form groups to play whatever they want we are encouraging everyone to stick to Free-to-play games.\r\n\r\nThis is the current official games list (please arrive with these games preinstalled):\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Starcraft 2</li>\r\n 	<li>Team Fortress 2</li>\r\n 	<li>Overwatch 2</li>\r\n 	<li>Counter Strike 2 (If we play CS1.6 an installer will be provided)</li>\r\n 	<li>Unreal Tournament 3 &amp; 2004 (Installers will be provided for these if needed)</li>\r\n 	<li>Fortnite</li>\r\n 	<li>Rocket League</li>\r\n 	<li>Wolfenstein: Enemy Territory</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nPost in #lan-party on slack if you have a game you\'d like added to this list.\r\n\r\nThe event will start with a bit of undirected gaming until lunch time. Lunch will be provided, and after everyone is fed and we\'ve waited 30 minutes to avoid cramps... the Starcraft 2 tournament will begin. All who wish to participate will put their names on a bracket and trophies will be awarded to the contestants that place in the top 3. Any who wish to be considered for the badass battle station award may sign up for that as well and the winner will be decided by a vote from players and spectators alike. Gamers are welcome to stick around after the tournament as long as they\'d like.','Free-to-Play Makerspace LAN Party','','publish','closed','closed','','free-to-play-makerspace-lan-party','','','2024-10-28 16:10:54','2024-10-28 22:10:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43377',0,'event','',0),
(43578,968,'2024-11-01 19:35:42','2024-11-02 01:35:42','Learn to use the TIG Welder and get authorized to use it. This class will teach basic machine safety and introductory welding techniques that should prepare you to practice more on your own safely and confidently.\r\n\r\nUnlike the MIG machine that feeds the wire automatically and draws current through the filler material, the TIG machine requires precise movement of a Tungsten electrode and filler material supplied by hand. MIG is easier but TIG is cleaner and more precise, thus the MIG class is a recommended (but not required) prerequisite to this authorization class.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our TIG welder, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/ahp-alphatig-welder&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PyQUZ225ziQyqT4JOZ74v" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional cost.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-4','','','2024-11-01 19:35:52','2024-11-02 01:35:52','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43578',0,'event','',0),
(43756,968,'2024-11-06 12:36:18','2024-11-06 19:36:18','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a more broad materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-5','','','2024-11-06 12:37:59','2024-11-06 19:37:59','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43756',0,'event','',0),
(43758,968,'2024-11-06 15:28:45','2024-11-06 22:28:45','denhac will be hosting an in-depth Fusion 360 course taught by the amazingly talented Brad Tallis who is a former Autodesk employee and Fusion 360 professional.\r\n\r\nAlthough this class is open to anyone interested in learning Fusion 360 our intention is to prepare a number of people to be CAD/CAM teachers that can prepare members to use the Shapeoko CNC Router. If you\'re certified to use the equipment in the CNC fridge and have an interest in teaching an intro to CAD &amp; CAM please sign up for this class ASAP. Members interested in training will be given priority attendance if the class is full.\r\n\r\nDue to the nature of Colorado\'s roads and the fact that Brad has a long drive to denhac, this class may be delayed until the following weekend (to the 14th) in the event of inclement weather at Brad\'s discretion.','Fusion 360 Master-Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fusion-360-master-class','','','2024-11-09 14:56:07','2024-11-09 21:56:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43758',0,'event','',0),
(43889,968,'2024-11-12 18:48:29','2024-11-13 01:48:29','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete.\r\n\r\nThese machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU. This class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-12','','','2024-11-12 18:48:29','2024-11-13 01:48:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43889',0,'event','',0),
(43890,968,'2024-11-12 18:51:22','2024-11-13 01:51:22','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material.\r\n\r\nThese machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a more broad materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-6','','','2024-11-12 18:51:22','2024-11-13 01:51:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43890',0,'event','',0),
(44353,968,'2024-11-28 11:17:30','2024-11-28 18:17:30','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them.\r\n\r\nThe laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-8','','','2024-11-28 11:17:30','2024-11-28 18:17:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=44353',0,'event','',0),
