(45034,968,'2024-12-28 13:56:57','2024-12-28 20:56:57','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them.\r\n\r\nThe laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-10','','','2025-01-08 14:13:33','2025-01-08 21:13:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45034',0,'event','',0),
(45642,968,'2025-01-20 12:47:13','2025-01-20 19:47:13','This will be a follow up to the Fusion 360 Master Class that was held in December. This class will skip all of the modeling that was covered in the last class and will skip right to basic and intermediate CAM instruction followed by how to create assemblies like a pro, and finishing with some instruction on how to use the sheet metal tools and how to prepare CAM toolpaths to cut sheet metal parts with a CNC plasma cutter (which may be coming to denhac soon).\r\n\r\nThis class will also be available remotely via google meet to any and all denhac members. Please only sign up for a ticket if you plan to attend in person. The link will be posted to #computer-aided-design on slack once the meeting starts (it will be posted just moments before the event starts officially)\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. Members will be expected to bring a workstation with Fusion 360 pre-installed and set up.\r\n\r\nIf you agreed to teach the upcoming CAM class that will serve as an optional prerequisite to the CNC router authorization classes then please plan to attend this class in person if possible. Tickets to this class will again prioritize those who are interested in teaching the intro to CAM class in the future.','Fusion 360 CAM Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fusion-360-cam-class','','','2025-01-20 13:29:31','2025-01-20 20:29:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45642',0,'event','',0),
(45695,968,'2025-01-21 13:02:04','2025-01-21 20:02:04','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-12','','','2025-01-21 13:02:04','2025-01-21 20:02:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45695',0,'event','',0),
(45938,968,'2025-01-29 15:11:46','2025-01-29 22:11:46','The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-14','','','2025-02-10 14:33:05','2025-02-10 21:33:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45938',0,'event','',0),
(46245,968,'2025-02-11 13:38:00','2025-02-11 20:38:00','Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>HOMEWORK:</strong></span> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-17','','','2025-02-11 13:38:00','2025-02-11 20:38:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46245',0,'event','',0),
(46498,968,'2025-02-20 16:55:42','2025-02-20 23:55:42','<strong><span style="color: #cc0000;">Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the homework videos</span></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #cc0000;"><strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong></span>\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #000000;">On <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model.</span>\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101','','','2025-02-23 15:32:01','2025-02-23 22:32:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46498',0,'event','',0),
(46578,968,'2025-02-23 14:04:19','2025-02-23 21:04:19','<span style="color: #cc0000;"><strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you\'ve never used a CNC machine then please sign up for a CAD class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-18','','','2025-02-23 15:31:14','2025-02-23 22:31:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46578',0,'event','',0),
(46823,968,'2025-03-03 17:50:31','2025-03-04 00:50:31','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-21','','','2025-03-03 17:50:31','2025-03-04 00:50:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46823',0,'event','',0),
(45956,974,'2025-01-30 14:18:25','2025-01-30 21:18:25','Get trained and signed off to use the 4 major woodworking power tools at denhac. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. If you\'re interested in becoming a denhac member, come to an open house or contact us','General Woodshop Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','general-woodshop-authorization-class-12','','','2025-01-30 14:18:25','2025-01-30 21:18:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=45956',0,'event','',0),
