(51855,985,'2025-08-15 12:34:29','2025-08-15 18:34:29','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-3','','','2025-08-15 12:34:41','2025-08-15 18:34:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51855',0,'event','',0),
(54431,985,'2025-10-29 11:04:03','2025-10-29 17:04:03','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="presentation" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-5','','','2025-10-29 11:04:03','2025-10-29 17:04:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54431',0,'event','',0),
(57725,974,'2026-01-27 19:35:22','2026-01-28 02:35:22','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-14','','','2026-01-27 19:35:22','2026-01-28 02:35:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57725',0,'event','',0),
(57729,974,'2026-01-27 19:44:04','2026-01-28 02:44:04','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-12','','','2026-01-27 19:44:04','2026-01-28 02:44:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57729',0,'event','',0),
(58153,991,'2026-02-07 19:30:23','2026-02-08 02:30:23','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-37','','','2026-02-07 19:30:23','2026-02-08 02:30:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58153',0,'event','',0),
(58642,974,'2026-02-22 13:06:10','2026-02-22 20:06:10','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-11','','','2026-02-22 13:06:10','2026-02-22 20:06:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58642',0,'event','',0),
(58643,974,'2026-02-22 13:07:26','2026-02-22 20:07:26','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-14','','','2026-02-22 13:07:26','2026-02-22 20:07:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58643',0,'event','',0),
(59013,991,'2026-03-01 17:01:18','2026-03-02 00:01:18','Stop by the Fishbowl to see bookbinding in action! Rory and Craig will be hanging out binding books and answering questions. There\'s no formal itinerary, just stop by whenever.\r\n\r\nAnd if you\'ve got your own bookbinding projects, feel free to bring them to show off to others!\r\n\r\n______________\r\n\r\nIf you\'d like to make your own book - we have a book binding class taught by Rory happening 3/14\r\n\r\nBook binding class: https://denhac.org/events/bookbinding-fundamentals-japanese-stab-binding','Bookbinding Show \'n Tell','','publish','closed','closed','','bookbinding-show-n-tell','','','2026-03-01 17:01:18','2026-03-02 00:01:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59013',0,'event','',0),
(59015,991,'2026-03-01 17:05:17','2026-03-02 00:05:17','We\'re gonna get a bunch of people and a bunch of musical instruments together in the same room and see what happens! Grab your rosin and your reeds, your finger picks and drum sticks. And even if you\'ve never done any music stuff, you should still join us! We\'ll have a bag of small shakers, cowbells, tambourines and other music toys so anyone can participate.\r\n\r\nFor more info and updates, join our <a class="internal_channel_link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08GWP9T5L1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#music-makers" data-channel-id="C08GWP9T5L1" data-qa="channel_link">#music-makers</a> channel on Slack.','denhac Jam Night','','publish','closed','closed','','denhac-jam-night','','','2026-03-01 18:09:24','2026-03-02 01:09:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59015',0,'event','',0),
(68064,985,'2026-09-30 19:23:47','2026-10-01 01:23:47','This end-to-end training will impart the skills and knowledge necessary to safely design, and sew basic embroidery projects using our 7-Needle Embroidery Machine.\r\n\r\nFor more information about our textiles equipment, check out the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge','[CANCELED] 7-Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-7','','','2026-10-23 11:20:33','2026-10-23 17:20:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68064',0,'event','',0),
(39000,1015,'2024-05-23 21:40:39','2024-05-24 03:40:39','<p class="mb-4">Get trained and signed off to use some of the woodworking tools at <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">denhac</a>. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading the <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/wood-working-area" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">woodshop wiki page</a> and all tool wiki pages linked below</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.</p>\r\n<p class="mb-4">This class includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="pl-5 list-disc mb-4">\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/saw-stop" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Saw Stop table saw</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/jointer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Powermatic jointer</a></li>\r\n 	<li><a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/wiki/dw375-planer" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">Dewalt planer</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="mb-4"><strong>Cost:</strong>\r\ndenhac <strong>members: Free!</strong>\r\n<strong>non members:</strong> If you\'re interested in this class you must first become a denhac member. First see our website: <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://denhac.org/howto" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener ugc">https://denhac.org/</a>. Think our organization sounds cool and interested in joining? Attend an <a class="!text-viridian" href="https://www.meetup.com/denhac-hackerspace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open house tour</a>, every Tuesday 8 - 10pm. After your tour if you like our community - you can sign up, show us your official ID, and become a member.</p>','Woodshop Training','Woodshop training for: Table saw, Jointer, Planer, and Router Table','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-training-2024-06-30','','','2024-05-30 20:30:44','2024-05-31 02:30:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/woodshop-training-2024-06-30',0,'event','',0),
(40743,1007,'2024-07-26 19:18:17','2024-07-27 01:18:17','This class provides training and authorization to use our fleet of Prusa Mk4 FDM printers.\r\n\r\nThis class is for members only.\r\n\r\nCheck out our wiki for more information: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/prusa-3d-printer&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Fb_pGBY78yy2je0nimwGJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://denhac.org/wiki/prusa-3d-printer</a>','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class','','','2024-07-26 19:18:17','2024-07-27 01:18:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=40743',0,'event','',0),
(41053,1007,'2024-08-03 12:33:09','2024-08-03 18:33:09','<span class="event-description">This class provides training and authorization to use our fleet of Prusa Mk4 FDM printers.</span>\r\n\r\n<span class="event-description">This class is free and available to denhac members only.</span>\r\n\r\n<span class="event-description">Check out our wiki for more information: <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/prusa-3d-printer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://denhac.<wbr />org/wiki/prusa-<wbr />3d-printer.</a></span>','FDM 3D Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-2','','','2024-08-03 12:33:09','2024-08-03 18:33:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41053',0,'event','',0),
(41531,1007,'2024-08-18 13:42:11','2024-08-18 19:42:11','This class provides training and authorization to use our fleet of Prusa Mk4 FDM printers. This class does not authorize you to use the Large Format FDM printers, but this class is a prerequisite to take the Advanced FDM Workshop.\r\n\r\nThis class is free and available to denhac members only.\r\n\r\nCheck out <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/prusa-3d-printer">the wiki</a> for more information.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-3','','','2024-08-18 13:42:11','2024-08-18 19:42:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=41531',0,'event','',0),
(42658,995,'2024-09-26 12:57:31','2024-09-26 18:57:31','Learn to use the TIG Welder and get authorized to use it. This class will teach basic machine safety and introductory welding techniques.\r\n\r\nUnlike the MIG machine that feeds the wire automatically and draws current through the filler material, the TIG machine requires precise movement of a Tungsten rod and filler material supplied by hand. MIG is easier but TIG is cleaner, thus the MIG class is a recommended (but not required) prerequisite to this authorization class.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our TIG welder, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/ahp-alphatig-welder">read the wiki</a>.','TIG Welding Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welding-authorization-class','','','2024-09-26 12:59:33','2024-09-26 18:59:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42658',0,'event','',0),
(42659,995,'2024-09-26 13:00:51','2024-09-26 19:00:51','Learn to use the TIG Welder and get authorized to use it. This class will teach basic machine safety and introductory welding techniques.\r\n\r\nUnlike the MIG machine that feeds the wire automatically and draws current through the filler material, the TIG machine requires precise movement of a Tungsten rod and filler material supplied by hand. MIG is easier but TIG is cleaner, thus the MIG class is a recommended (but not required) prerequisite to this authorization class.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our TIG welder, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/ahp-alphatig-welder">read the wiki</a>.','TIG Welding Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welding-authorization-class-2','','','2024-09-27 13:28:17','2024-09-27 19:28:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42659',0,'event','',0),
(42660,995,'2024-09-26 13:02:09','2024-09-26 19:02:09','Learn to use the TIG Welder and get authorized to use it. This class will teach basic machine safety and introductory welding techniques.\r\n\r\nUnlike the MIG machine that feeds the wire automatically and draws current through the filler material, the TIG machine requires precise movement of a Tungsten rod and filler material supplied by hand. MIG is easier but TIG is cleaner, thus the MIG class is a recommended (but not required) prerequisite to this authorization class.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our TIG welder, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/ahp-alphatig-welder">read the wiki</a>.','TIG Welding Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welding-authorization-class-3','','','2024-09-27 13:28:51','2024-09-27 19:28:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=42660',0,'event','',0),
(43754,1007,'2024-11-06 12:04:55','2024-11-06 19:04:55','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-10','','','2024-11-06 12:04:55','2024-11-06 19:04:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=43754',0,'event','',0),
