(48995,1035,'2025-05-14 16:48:07','2025-05-14 22:48:07','Learn to do basic bicycle repairs in this class that will cover; safety torquing bolts, how to fix a flat, brake adjustments, how to shift your bicycle, removing and installing pedals, basic tools you should have, and how to clean your bicycle\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Bicycle Repair Class','','publish','closed','closed','','bicycle-repair-class','','','2025-05-15 11:52:37','2025-05-15 17:52:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=48995',0,'event','',0),
(50295,1052,'2025-06-27 08:26:08','2025-06-27 14:26:08','Get trained and signed off to use the 4 major woodworking power tools at denhac. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n 	<li>And possibly the drum sander if there\'s still time</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge','General Woodshop Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','general-woodshop-authorization-class-31','','','2025-06-27 08:26:08','2025-06-27 14:26:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50295',0,'event','',0),
(52411,1052,'2025-08-31 17:50:20','2025-08-31 23:50:20','The lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-36','','','2025-08-31 17:50:20','2025-08-31 23:50:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52411',0,'event','',0),
(54195,1052,'2025-10-23 17:22:28','2025-10-23 23:22:28','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-7','','','2025-10-23 17:22:28','2025-10-23 23:22:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54195',0,'event','',0),
(55163,1020,'2025-11-17 09:02:29','2025-11-17 16:02:29','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-13','','','2025-11-17 09:02:29','2025-11-17 16:02:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55163',0,'event','',0),
(56294,1020,'2025-12-18 17:21:49','2025-12-19 00:21:49','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-17','','','2025-12-18 23:37:18','2025-12-19 06:37:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56294',0,'event','',0),
(57724,1052,'2026-01-27 19:34:39','2026-01-28 02:34:39','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-13','','','2026-01-27 19:34:39','2026-01-28 02:34:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57724',0,'event','',0),
(40640,1068,'2024-07-23 19:08:55','2024-07-24 01:08:55','In this class any complete beginner can learn to design a Printed Circuit Board. We\'ll use KiCad to design a circuit schematic and board design from scratch.','PCB Design Class','','publish','closed','closed','','pcb-design-class','','','2024-07-24 14:27:29','2024-07-24 20:27:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=40640',0,'event','',0),
(58638,1052,'2026-02-22 12:53:10','2026-02-22 19:53:10','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-16','','','2026-02-22 12:55:55','2026-02-22 19:55:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58638',0,'event','',0),
(58641,1070,'2026-02-22 13:02:41','2026-02-22 20:02:41','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-19','','','2026-02-22 13:02:41','2026-02-22 20:02:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58641',0,'event','',0),
(59924,1052,'2026-03-24 14:29:18','2026-03-24 20:29:18','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-17','','','2026-03-24 14:31:57','2026-03-24 20:31:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59924',0,'event','',0),
