(51386,1119,'2025-07-31 14:26:04','2025-07-31 20:26:04','Get trained and signed off to use the 4 major woodworking power tools at denhac. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n 	<li>Router table</li>\r\n 	<li>And possibly the drum sander if there\'s still time</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge','General Woodshop Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','general-woodshop-authorization-class-37','','','2025-07-31 14:26:04','2025-07-31 20:26:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51386',0,'event','',0),
(52404,1119,'2025-08-31 17:37:05','2025-08-31 23:37:05','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-2','','','2025-08-31 17:37:05','2025-08-31 23:37:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52404',0,'event','',0),
(52407,1119,'2025-08-31 17:44:07','2025-08-31 23:44:07','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-2','','','2025-08-31 17:59:38','2025-08-31 23:59:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52407',0,'event','',0),
(44287,1210,'2024-11-26 18:49:15','2024-11-27 01:49:15','Learn to use the TIG Welder and get authorized to use it\r\n\r\nThis class will teach basic machine safety and introductory welding techniques that should prepare you to practice more on your own safely and confidently. Unlike the MIG machine that feeds the wire automatically and draws current through the filler material, the TIG machine requires precise movement of a Tungsten electrode and filler material supplied by hand. MIG is easier but TIG is cleaner and more precise, thus the MIG class is a recommended (but not required) prerequisite to this authorization class.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our TIG welder, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/ahp-alphatig-welder&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PyQUZ225ziQyqT4JOZ74v" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional cost','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-5','','','2024-11-26 18:49:15','2024-11-27 01:49:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=44287',0,'event','',0),
(44288,1210,'2024-11-26 18:56:49','2024-11-27 01:56:49','Become authorized to use the denhac MIG/Flux Core welder\r\n\r\nThis class will also provide an overview of some of the other equipment in the room. The class will cover basic safety training regarding the MIG welder but will not be an exhaustive lesson on welding. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use the MIG machine. If you have never welded before you should absolutely take this class before you consider taking the TIG class.\r\n\r\n<strong>Attendees must wear non-synthetic clothing and shoes.</strong> Welding helmets, jackets, and gloves are provided, but you’re also welcome to bring your own.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the MIG welder at denhac, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/lincoln-electric-125-hd-welder&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3kfjjS-nIXqF_9gBhjoH2U" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','MIG / Flux Core Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','mig-flux-core-welder-authorization-class','','','2024-11-26 18:56:49','2024-11-27 01:56:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=44288',0,'event','',0),
(48611,1217,'2025-04-17 15:28:30','2025-04-17 21:28:30','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K">homework videos</a></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training\r\n\r\nDownload Fusion 360 for personal use <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/fusion-360/personal">here</a>','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2026-01-16','','','2026-01-29 18:38:10','2026-01-30 01:38:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2026-01-09',0,'event','',0),
(49709,1184,'2025-06-07 22:42:31','2025-06-08 04:42:31','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete.\r\n\r\nThese machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU. This class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-27','','','2025-06-10 10:16:40','2025-06-10 16:16:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49709',0,'event','',0),
