(54779,1184,'2025-11-07 11:33:04','2025-11-07 18:33:04','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 8 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Colin Rooney 12mv2','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-39','','','2025-11-07 11:33:04','2025-11-07 18:33:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54779',0,'event','',0),
(57797,1217,'2025-04-17 15:28:30','2025-04-17 21:28:30','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K">homework videos</a></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training\r\n\r\nDownload Fusion 360 for personal use <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/fusion-360/personal">here</a>','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16','','','2026-01-29 18:38:10','2026-01-30 01:38:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16',0,'event','',0),
(57798,1217,'2025-04-17 15:28:30','2025-04-17 21:28:30','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K">homework videos</a></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training\r\n\r\nDownload Fusion 360 for personal use <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/fusion-360/personal">here</a>','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16-2025-06-20','','','2026-01-29 18:38:10','2026-01-30 01:38:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16-2