am-cnc101-2025-05-16-2025-06-20-2025-07-18-2025-08-15',0,'event','',0),
(46837,1226,'2025-03-04 15:12:21','2025-03-04 22:12:21','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the homework videos</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #cc0000;"><strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2','','','2025-03-04 15:12:21','2025-03-04 22:12:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46837',0,'event','',0),
(47152,1257,'2025-03-15 22:57:27','2025-03-16 04:57:27','PThe laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-18','','','2025-03-22 13:08:35','2025-03-22 19:08:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=47152',0,'event','',0),
(48085,1227,'2025-04-17 14:59:32','2025-04-17 20:59:32','Learn the basics of resin printing and get authorized to use denhac\'s resin printers. Resin printing can produce parts with a much finer level of detail than our FDM 3d printers, great for things like mini-figures.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our resin 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jookVGJH8eJ9t8Zodltd1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Resin 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-3d-printer-authorization-class-5','','','2025-04-17 14:59:32','2025-04-17 20:59:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=48085',0,'event','',0),
(48982,1257,'2025-05-14 16:33:23','2025-05-14 22:33:23','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-2025-06-10','','','2025-09-24 15:02:45','2025-09-24 21:02:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/laser-cutter-authorization-class-2025-06-10',0,'event','',0),
