(57807,1217,'2025-04-17 15:28:30','2025-04-17 21:28:30','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K">homework videos</a></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training\r\n\r\nDownload Fusion 360 for personal use <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/fusion-360/personal">here</a>','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16-2025-06-20-2025-07-18-2025-08-15-2025-09-19-2025-10-17-2025-11-21-2025-12-19-2026-02-20-2026-03-20-2026-04-17','','','2026-02-28 16:48:22','2026-02-28 23:48:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-2025-05-16-2025-06-20-2025-07-18-2025-08-15-2025-09-19-2025-10-17-2025-11-21-2025-12-19-2026-02-20-2026-03-20-2026-04-17',0,'event','',0),
(60730,1227,'2026-04-16 11:07:49','2026-04-16 17:07:49','Get authorized to use our resin printers. The resin printers are 3d printers that use a photosensitive resin and a UV screen (as opposed to filament plastic and a hot nozzle on a gantry) to selectively cure layers at the bottom of the resin puddle, effectively summoning your part from a pool of fluid.\r\n\r\n<strong>You must bring your own respirator.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is for members only. For more details, see the wiki: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1776791084862217&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pRzJo2O5876j-wCcYehkz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://denhac.org/wiki/resin-printing-process</a>','Resin Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','resin-printer-authorization-class','','','2026-04-16 11:07:49','2026-04-16 17:07:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60730',0,'event','',0),
(61929,1226,'2026-05-14 13:07:49','2026-05-14 19:07:49','This class will be an intro to Blender for a variety of purposes like modeling, rendering, animating, and 3D printing. I\'m mostly interested in catering this class for what attendees would find most useful, so bring a computer with Blender downloaded and some idea of what you\'d be interested in using it for!','Blender 101 - 3D Mesh Modeling Beginners Class','','publish','closed','closed','','blender-101-3d-mesh-modeling-beginners-class','','','2026-05-14 16:13:17','2026-05-14 22:13:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61929',0,'event','',0),
(48986,1257,'2025-05-14 16:33:23','2025-05-14 22:33:23','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-2025-10-14','','','2025-09-24 15:02:45','2025-09-24 21:02:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/laser-cutter-authorization-class-2025-10-14',0,'event','',0),
