(49542,1318,'2025-06-02 11:11:22','2025-06-02 17:11:22','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is very highly recommended you take the introduction to metal shop safety class prior to this class, however it is not currently required.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-6','','','2025-06-02 11:11:22','2025-06-02 17:11:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49542',0,'event','',0),
(50025,1318,'2025-06-18 11:44:30','2025-06-18 17:44:30','Come learn to make stained glass with us!\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. You\'re welcome to think about a pattern you might want to make, but you\'re encouraged to keep it simple during the workshop.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Attendance for the entire event duration is not required. Plan for your project to take about 45 minutes of work. However, the soldering process can create a bit of a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a bit of a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing materials for another project or something to keep you busy if a line forms, and check <code>#stained-glass</code> for coordination of start times.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass','','','2025-06-18 11:44:30','2025-06-18 17:44:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50025',0,'event','',0),
(50031,1318,'2025-06-18 11:54:34','2025-06-18 17:54:34','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is very highly recommended you take the introduction to metal shop safety class prior to this class, however it is not currently required.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-7','','','2025-06-18 11:54:34','2025-06-18 17:54:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50031',0,'event','',0),
