(50810,1318,'2025-07-13 10:37:59','2025-07-13 16:37:59','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-10','','','2025-08-06 18:01:44','2025-08-07 00:01:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50810',0,'event','',0),
(50811,1318,'2025-07-13 10:39:08','2025-07-13 16:39:08','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is very highly recommended you take the introduction to metal shop safety class prior to this class, however it is not currently required.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-11','','','2025-07-13 10:39:08','2025-07-13 16:39:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50811',0,'event','',0),
(52711,1295,'2025-09-08 13:05:59','2025-09-08 19:05:59','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-25','','','2025-09-08 13:18:25','2025-09-08 19:18:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52711',0,'event','',0),
(53518,1295,'2025-10-02 23:58:47','2025-10-03 05:58:47','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-30','','','2025-10-02 23:58:47','2025-10-03 05:58:47','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53518',0,'event','',0),
