(59312,1295,'2026-03-07 13:14:17','2026-03-07 20:14:17','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-46','','','2026-03-07 13:14:17','2026-03-07 20:14:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59312',0,'event','',0),
(50812,1318,'2025-07-13 10:44:31','2025-07-13 16:44:31','Come learn to make stained glass with us!\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. You\'re welcome to think about a pattern you might want to make, but you\'re encouraged to keep it simple during the workshop.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Attendance for the entire event duration is not required. Plan for your project to take about 45-60 minutes of work. However, the soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms. We stagger start times via limited availability of soldering surfaces. If there is an available surface in the kitchen, it means we are ready for another person to begin! Join <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#stained-glass" data-channel-id="C08HF2H4DHN" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-2','','','2025-07-13 10:44:31','2025-07-13 16:44:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50812',0,'event','',0),
(51496,1318,'2025-08-04 17:25:49','2025-08-04 23:25:49','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-12','','','2025-08-06 18:02:28','2025-08-07 00:02:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51496',0,'event','',0),
(51511,1318,'2025-08-04 17:30:52','2025-08-04 23:30:52','Come learn to make stained glass with us!\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. You\'re welcome to think about a pattern you might want to make, but you\'re encouraged to keep it simple during the workshop.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Attendance for the entire event duration is not required. Plan for your project to take about 45-60 minutes of work. However, the soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms. We stagger start times via limited availability of soldering surfaces. If there is an available surface in the kitchen, it means we are ready for another person to begin! Join <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#stained-glass" data-channel-id="C08HF2H4DHN" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-3','','','2025-08-04 17:30:52','2025-08-04 23:30:52','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51511',0,'event','',0),
(51513,1318,'2025-08-04 17:32:32','2025-08-04 23:32:32','Come learn to make stained glass with us!\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. You\'re welcome to think about a pattern you might want to make, but you\'re encouraged to keep it simple during the workshop.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Attendance for the entire event duration is not required. Plan for your project to take about 45-60 minutes of work. However, the soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms. We stagger start times via limited availability of soldering surfaces. If there is an available surface in the kitchen, it means we are ready for another person to begin! Join <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#stained-glass" data-channel-id="C08HF2H4DHN" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-5','','','2025-08-04 17:32:32','2025-08-04 23:32:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51513',0,'event','',0),
(51514,1318,'2025-08-04 17:35:37','2025-08-04 23:35:37','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety','','','2025-08-04 17:35:37','2025-08-04 23:35:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51514',0,'event','',0),
(51515,1318,'2025-08-04 17:36:52','2025-08-04 23:36:52','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-2','','','2025-08-15 12:35:51','2025-08-15 18:35:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51515',0,'event','',0),
(51916,1318,'2025-08-18 15:17:49','2025-08-18 21:17:49','Are you already authorized to use the TIG welder at Denhac? Do you want some time to practice welding while someone cheerleads / gives advice? Would you like some welding project recommendations? This event is for you! Come practice welding and hang out :)\r\n\r\nThis is not an authorization class. You must have prior TIG welder authorization to participate. This event is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the event. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Leather spats available. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.','TIG Welding Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welding-office-hours','','','2025-08-18 16:05:03','2025-08-18 22:05:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=51916',0,'event','',0),
(53747,1318,'2025-10-09 13:30:07','2025-10-09 19:30:07','<b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b>\r\n\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-13','','','2025-10-23 23:25:41','2025-10-24 05:25:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53747',0,'event','',0),
(53748,1318,'2025-10-09 13:33:17','2025-10-09 19:33:17','Completing and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-14','','','2025-10-09 13:33:17','2025-10-09 19:33:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53748',0,'event','',0),
(53750,1318,'2025-10-09 13:54:01','2025-10-09 19:54:01','Come learn to make stained glass with us!\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. You\'re welcome to think about a pattern you might want to make. We do have some pre-made Halloween patterns for the month of October!\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: We have staggered start times, attendance for the entire event duration is not required. Plan for your project to take about 1-1.5 hours of work. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#stained-glass" data-channel-id="C08HF2H4DHN" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only, at no additional cost.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-4','','','2025-10-09 14:03:00','2025-10-09 20:03:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53750',0,'event','',0),
