(56998,1318,'2026-01-08 19:22:42','2026-01-09 02:22:42','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: We have staggered start times, that is why there are multiple events back to back. Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only, at no additional cost.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project - materials provided!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-stained-glass-3','','','2026-01-12 18:25:57','2026-01-13 01:25:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56998',0,'event','',0),
