(59552,1318,'2026-03-14 15:08:25','2026-03-14 21:08:25','We are seeking out people who have experience with or interest in Jewelry Making and Fine Metalworking. We would like to better enable these activities at denhac. We want to inventory what relevant equipment we have, what skills our members have, and then discuss what we need to get to better support these activities at denhac.\r\n\r\nThis is a very high level planning meeting! Join us if you are interested in bringing new capabilities to denhac :)','Fine Metalworking and Jewelry Making Kickoff Meeting','Shiny objects','publish','closed','closed','','fine-metalworking-and-jewelry-making-kickoff-meeting','','','2026-03-14 15:08:25','2026-03-14 21:08:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59552',0,'event','',0),
(46446,1353,'2025-02-18 13:40:42','2025-02-18 20:40:42','<div><strong>Food has been bought, and as such reservations are now closed. Folks who have not yet secured a ticket may be served on a first-come-first-serve basis while supplies last. </strong></div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Join us to celebrate surpassing 500 active members and counting! Burgers, Hot Dogs, and Assorted Grilled Vegetables will be cooked and served on site along with member-provided sides. Sign up for a ticket using this page so that we know how much meat and kebabs to provide (if you\'re bringing guests make sure to add the appropriate number of spaces to your booking so that we maintain an accurate headcount).</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This event is open to any and all current denhac members and their families. The space will be closed for personal project work to accommodate for this event.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Members that coordinate through the #500-member-bbq channel on slack to bring a side dish for every two people in their party will be given a <strong>free priority-access meal</strong> <strong>ticket</strong> that guarantees them a plate before normal meal tickets start getting sold. Meal tickets will be available until the food is gone in exchange for a minimum $5 donation to the space.</div>\r\n<div></div>','500 Member Barbecue and Potluck','','publish','closed','closed','','500-member-bbq-potluck','','','2025-04-26 09:08:20','2025-04-26 15:08:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=46446',0,'event','',0),
(53302,1371,'2025-09-26 20:38:18','2025-09-27 02:38:18','Join the rest of the haunted house crew in preparing for the event on October 3rd.\r\n\r\nWe need any and all prop makers to help us make the haunted house the best it can be!','Haunted House Prop and Painting Party!','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-prop-and-painting-party','','','2025-09-26 20:38:18','2025-09-27 02:38:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53302',0,'event','',0),
(53306,1371,'2025-09-26 20:39:46','2025-09-27 02:39:46','Join the rest of the haunted house crew in preparing for the event on October 3rd.\r\n\r\nWe need any and all prop makers to help us make the haunted house the best it can be!','Haunted House Prop and Painting Party!','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-prop-and-painting-party-2','','','2025-09-26 20:39:46','2025-09-27 02:39:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53306',0,'event','',0),
(59555,1318,'2026-03-14 15:24:00','2026-03-14 21:24:00','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-21','','','2026-03-14 15:24:00','2026-03-14 21:24:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59555',0,'event','',0),
(61553,1318,'2026-05-04 18:44:25','2026-05-05 00:44:25','Special interest group meeting for stained glass and glass working.','SIG Glass Meeting','SIG Glass Meeting','publish','closed','closed','','sig-glass-meeting-2','','','2026-05-04 18:44:25','2026-05-05 00:44:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61553',0,'event','',0),
(61618,1318,'2026-05-06 21:11:19','2026-05-07 03:11:19','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-10','','','2026-05-06 21:11:19','2026-05-07 03:11:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61618',0,'event','',0),
(61621,1318,'2026-05-06 21:28:22','2026-05-07 03:28:22','Please bring either fresh or pre-pressed plants/flowers and learn how to add them into your stained glass artwork! This method works best on plants that can be easily squished flat. You will also learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nPreserving plants can cause them to lose color. Sunlight exposure will cause color to fade more quickly.\r\n\r\nYou can make stained glass artwork with a mixture of art glass and preserved plants. Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nWe have staggered start times, that is why there are multiple events back to back.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Stained Glass Preserving Plants','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','preserving-plants','','','2026-05-07 10:43:50','2026-05-07 16:43:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61621',0,'event','',0),
(62764,1318,'2026-06-03 14:27:26','2026-06-03 20:27:26','<blockquote><b>Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></blockquote>\r\nTHIS IS A TRAINERS TRAINING EVENT. PLEASE LET LINDSEY KNOW IF YOU ARE SIGNING UP FOR THIS EVENT.\r\n\r\nWe will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld. It is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class. You must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Trainers Training','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-trainers-training','','','2026-06-03 14:27:26','2026-06-03 20:27:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62764',0,'event','',0),
(62765,1318,'2026-06-03 14:30:25','2026-06-03 20:30:25','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-23','','','2026-06-03 14:30:25','2026-06-03 20:30:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62765',0,'event','',0),
(62766,1318,'2026-06-03 14:40:27','2026-06-03 20:40:27','This event is effectively an intro to stained glass workshop. We are celebrating pride month by having materials and jigs available to create 3D pride heart pins! We will have a full rainbow of glass colors available.\r\n\r\nIn this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: We have staggered start times, that is why there are multiple events back to back. Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Stained Glass - 3D Pride Heart Pins','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','stained-glass-3d-pride-heart-pins','','','2026-06-03 14:50:49','2026-06-03 20:50:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62766',0,'event','',0),
