(66472,1318,'2026-09-01 03:32:12','2026-09-01 09:32:12','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metalshop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metalshop-safety','','','2026-09-02 18:07:03','2026-09-03 00:07:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66472',0,'event','',0),
(66479,1318,'2026-09-01 03:35:28','2026-09-01 09:35:28','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-24','','','2026-09-01 03:35:28','2026-09-01 09:35:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66479',0,'event','',0),
(67403,1322,'2026-09-16 08:58:33','2026-09-16 14:58:33','<pre>All electronics run on magic smoke. If you let it out everything stops working. This hands-on class covers the basics for anyone curious about electronics, circuits, or is looking for a place to get started.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll learn about a basic circuit diagram, what all those things in the electronics room do, and build a prototype on a breadboard. ZERO experience required!</pre>','Electronics 101: Keep the Magic Smoke In','','publish','closed','closed','','electronics-101-keep-the-magic-smoke-in','','','2026-09-16 08:58:33','2026-09-16 14:58:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67403',0,'event','',0),
(48556,1385,'2025-05-01 18:12:17','2025-05-02 00:12:17','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="-1" role="presentation" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class','','','2025-05-01 18:15:14','2025-05-02 00:15:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=48556',0,'event','',0),
(48558,1385,'2025-05-01 18:19:24','2025-05-02 00:19:24','Join us for a basic skills class on how to accurately read and use precision measurement equipment such as Dial and Test Indicators, Dial and Vernier Calipers, Micrometers, and various accessories to take measurements with one-thou accuracy (measurements as accurate as one one-thousandth of an inch)\r\n\r\nThis class is intended for people that are not familiar with how to properly use these types of instruments but feel free to join and collaborate if you are already knowledgeable in this area as well!','Introduction to Metrology','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metrology','','','2025-05-01 18:19:24','2025-05-02 00:19:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=48558',0,'event','',0),
(49535,1385,'2025-06-02 10:53:21','2025-06-02 16:53:21','Completing and Passing this class will authorize you to operate the milling machines in the metalworking shop. We will go over basic setup and operation of the machine as well as some basic theory on machining. It\'s not required but highly recommended you be familiar with some basic machining concepts before taking this class.\r\n\r\nThe wiki page for the Grizzly Mill has a basic outline of what skills you can be expected to need to practice to operate these machines. You are also encouraged to ask on slack in the <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C4H2U842E" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#help-metalwork" data-channel-id="C4H2U842E" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#help-metalwork</a>  channel for advice.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-2','','','2025-06-02 10:53:21','2025-06-02 16:53:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49535',0,'event','',0),
(49537,1385,'2025-06-02 10:59:58','2025-06-02 16:59:58','Completing and Passing this class will authorize you to operate the metalworking lathes we have in the metal shop. We will go over basic setup and operation of the machine as well as some basic theory on machining. It\'s not required but highly recommended you be familiar with some basic machining concepts before taking this class.\r\n\r\nThere are resources online as well as some books and manuals in the metal shop area that are good starting resources for learning about operating these machines.  You are also encouraged to ask on slack in the <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C4H2U842E" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#help-metalwork" data-channel-id="C4H2U842E" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#help-metalwork</a> channel for advice.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Metal Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','metal-lathe-authorization-class','','','2025-06-18 11:30:58','2025-06-18 17:30:58','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49537',0,'event','',0),
(49539,1385,'2025-06-02 11:03:55','2025-06-02 17:03:55','Join us in the metalworking shop for some time dedicated to community and collaboration. Have a project that you need some help or advice on? Bring it by the shop and we can try and problem solve it together!\r\n\r\nAsk for or provide instruction/advice on specific techniques and operations on the machines (things like thread cutting on the lathe, discussions about feeds and speeds and the like)\r\nCome show off your projects and creations! Get feedback on drawings and plans or help brainstorm with others!\r\nThe intent of this event is to give everyone a set time and date to get together to share their knowledge and skills (something we have no shortage of here at denhac!) in a setting where we can also spend some hands on time with the machines working on them together and grow as a community!\r\n\r\nNote: this event is not a formal training event and no machine authorizations can be provided at it. Please check the calendar for authorization classes. Sign up for a ticket if you plan to attend so that we know how many people to expect.','Shop Talk: Metalworking','','publish','closed','closed','','shop-talk-metalworking','','','2025-06-02 11:08:25','2025-06-02 17:08:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49539',0,'event','',0),
(50463,1385,'2025-07-02 10:20:42','2025-07-02 16:20:42','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="0" role="listitem" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" aria-roledescription="message" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" tabindex="-1" role="presentation" aria-setsize="-1" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-4','','','2025-07-02 10:22:31','2025-07-02 16:22:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50463',0,'event','',0),
(50464,1385,'2025-07-02 10:24:22','2025-07-02 16:24:22','Completing and Passing this class will authorize you to operate the metalworking lathes we have in the metal shop. We will go over basic setup and operation of the machine as well as some basic theory on machining. It\'s not required but highly recommended you be familiar with some basic machining concepts before taking this class.\r\n\r\nThere are resources online as well as some books and manuals in the metal shop area that are good starting resources for learning about operating these machines.  You are also encouraged to ask on slack in the <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C4H2U842E" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#help-metalwork" data-channel-id="C4H2U842E" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#help-metalwork</a> channel for advice.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Metal Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','metal-lathe-authorization-class-2','','','2025-07-02 10:24:22','2025-07-02 16:24:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50464',0,'event','',0),
(50466,1385,'2025-07-02 10:27:22','2025-07-02 16:27:22','Join us for a basic skills class on how to accurately read and use precision measurement equipment such as Dial and Test Indicators, Dial and Vernier Calipers, Micrometers, and various accessories to take measurements with one-thou accuracy (measurements as accurate as one one-thousandth of an inch)\r\n\r\nThis class is intended for people that are not familiar with how to properly use these types of instruments but feel free to join and collaborate if you are already knowledgeable in this area as well!','Introduction to Metrology','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metrology-2','','','2025-07-02 10:27:22','2025-07-02 16:27:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=50466',0,'event','',0),
