(49312,1426,'2025-05-25 13:46:38','2025-05-25 19:46:38','The board game that demands more top than most tables have to give, and more time than most people have to give...\r\n\r\nTwilight Imperium is a 4x space board game where each player takes the role of a different civilization in a galaxy, in an attempt to assert their dominance over the other civilizations; be it by trade, espionage, diplomacy, or brute force.\r\n\r\nBy the end of the night, 1 person will be crowned "Imperius Rex".','Hopkins/Rivers Twilight Imperium','','publish','closed','closed','','hopkins-rivers-twilight-imperium','','','2025-05-25 13:46:38','2025-05-25 19:46:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=49312',0,'event','',0),
(50815,1426,'2025-07-13 10:50:27','2025-07-13 16:50:27','Come learn the basics of electronic circuitry and soldering! This class will cover an introduction to electronic circuits, soldering (through-hole, not surface mount), and PCB usage. There is no expectation of any prior knowledge, all are welcome to come learn. We will provide all necessary equipment, but ask for an $8 donation to the electronics SIG to cover cost of kit.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Electronics and Soldering 101','Learn to solder and assemble basic electronics projects!','publish','closed','closed','','electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-08-07','','','2025-09-24 15:02:40','2025-09-24 21:02:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-08-07',0,'event','',0),
(50816,1426,'2025-07-13 10:50:27','2025-07-13 16:50:27','Come learn the basics of electronic circuitry and soldering! This class will cover an introduction to electronic circuits, soldering (through-hole, not surface mount), and PCB usage. There is no expectation of any prior knowledge, all are welcome to come learn. We will provide all necessary equipment, but ask for an $8 donation to the electronics SIG to cover cost of kit.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Electronics and Soldering 101','Learn to solder and assemble basic electronics projects!','publish','closed','closed','','electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-09-04','','','2025-09-24 15:02:40','2025-09-24 21:02:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-09-04',0,'event','',0),
(50817,1426,'2025-07-13 10:50:27','2025-07-13 16:50:27','Come learn the basics of electronic circuitry and soldering! This class will cover an introduction to electronic circuits, soldering (through-hole, not surface mount), and PCB usage. There is no expectation of any prior knowledge, all are welcome to come learn. We will provide all necessary equipment, but ask for an $8 donation to the electronics SIG to cover cost of kit.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Electronics and Soldering 101','Learn to solder and assemble basic electronics projects!','publish','closed','closed','','electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-10-02','','','2025-09-27 17:49:01','2025-09-27 23:49:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/electronics-and-soldering-101-2025-10-02',0,'event','',0),
(52775,1426,'2025-09-10 08:32:35','2025-09-10 14:32:35','<strong>Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K">homework videos</a></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong>\r\n\r\nOn <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2nqhTNiaoVKsRnCz3UsT5K" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\nhttps://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training\r\n\r\nDownload Fusion 360 for personal use <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/fusion-360/personal">here</a>','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-3','','','2025-09-10 08:32:35','2025-09-10 14:32:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52775',0,'event','',0),
(53290,1426,'2025-09-25 23:27:51','2025-09-26 05:27:51','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-28','','','2025-09-25 23:27:51','2025-09-26 05:27:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53290',0,'event','',0),
(53970,1426,'2025-10-16 13:39:43','2025-10-16 19:39:43','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-31','','','2025-10-16 13:39:43','2025-10-16 19:39:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53970',0,'event','',0),
(54775,1426,'2025-11-07 11:26:11','2025-11-07 18:26:11','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-33','','','2025-11-07 21:55:30','2025-11-08 04:55:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54775',0,'event','',0),
(55364,1426,'2025-11-21 13:51:55','2025-11-21 20:51:55','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-7','','','2025-11-21 13:51:55','2025-11-21 20:51:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55364',0,'event','',0),
(55365,1426,'2025-11-21 13:52:59','2025-11-21 20:52:59','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-8','','','2025-11-21 13:52:59','2025-11-21 20:52:59','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55365',0,'event','',0),
