(55508,1426,'2025-11-24 15:29:48','2025-11-24 22:29:48','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-36','','','2025-11-24 15:29:48','2025-11-24 22:29:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55508',0,'event','',0),
(57160,1426,'2026-01-13 12:42:10','2026-01-13 19:42:10','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-37','','','2026-01-13 12:42:10','2026-01-13 19:42:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57160',0,'event','',0),
(58144,1385,'2026-02-07 19:03:27','2026-02-08 02:03:27','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-22','','','2026-02-07 19:03:27','2026-02-08 02:03:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58144',0,'event','',0),
(58147,1385,'2026-02-07 19:06:11','2026-02-08 02:06:11','Completing and Passing this class will authorize you to operate the metalworking lathes we have in the metal shop. We will go over basic setup and operation of the machine as well as some basic theory on machining. It\'s not required but highly recommended you be familiar with some basic machining concepts before taking this class.\r\n\r\nThere are resources online as well as some books and manuals in the metal shop area that are good starting resources for learning about operating these machines.  You are also encouraged to ask on slack in the <a class="c-link c-mrkdwn__channel c-member_slug internal_channel_link c-member_slug--link" href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C4H2U842E" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-channel-name="#help-metalwork" data-channel-id="C4H2U842E" data-qa="channel_link" data-stringify-type="channel" data-sk="tooltip_parent">#help-metalwork</a> channel for advice.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Metal Lathe Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','metal-lathe-authorization-class-5','','','2026-02-07 19:06:11','2026-02-08 02:06:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58147',0,'event','',0),
