(59343,1426,'2026-03-08 15:46:02','2026-03-08 21:46:02','Come learn how to do V-Bit Wood Inlays. You should have some experience with the Shapeoko, as well as with CAM software. During the class we will be using Fusion360.','Intermediate CNC - Inlays','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-cnc-inlays','','','2026-04-22 22:33:33','2026-04-23 04:33:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59343',0,'event','',0),
(61487,1385,'2026-05-02 15:34:45','2026-05-02 21:34:45','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1776803252068746&amp;usg=AOvVaw2bXZHfN0YLduXvqRd10-FO" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-28','','','2026-05-02 15:34:45','2026-05-02 21:34:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61487',0,'event','',0),
(59930,1426,'2026-03-24 14:39:16','2026-03-24 20:39:16','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-17','','','2026-03-24 14:39:16','2026-03-24 20:39:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59930',0,'event','',0),
(61165,1426,'2026-04-27 20:22:55','2026-04-28 02:22:55','With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>','Woodshop A (4 spots) [Jointer, Planer, Table Saw]','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-a-4-spots-jointer-planer-table-saw','','','2026-04-27 20:22:55','2026-04-28 02:22:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61165',0,'event','',0),
(61169,1426,'2026-04-27 20:54:00','2026-04-28 02:54:00','With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-19','','','2026-04-27 20:54:00','2026-04-28 02:54:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61169',0,'event','',0),
(61786,1426,'2026-05-09 21:28:21','2026-05-10 03:28:21','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-51','','','2026-05-09 21:30:22','2026-05-10 03:30:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61786',0,'event','',0),
(61791,1426,'2026-05-09 21:40:46','2026-05-10 03:40:46','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-54','','','2026-05-09 21:40:46','2026-05-10 03:40:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61791',0,'event','',0),
(62678,1426,'2026-06-01 17:32:20','2026-06-01 23:32:20','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2F3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1780783620000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2w-X5IsxvpdZOTbDuQ811y" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization','','','2026-06-01 17:32:20','2026-06-01 23:32:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62678',0,'event','',0),
(62680,1426,'2026-06-01 17:36:46','2026-06-01 23:36:46','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-9','','','2026-06-01 17:36:46','2026-06-01 23:36:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62680',0,'event','',0),
(62700,1426,'2026-06-02 00:16:46','2026-06-02 06:16:46','<div class="p-rich_text_section">\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nThis class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-10','','','2026-06-02 00:16:46','2026-06-02 06:16:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62700',0,'event','',0),
(62974,1426,'2026-06-07 21:46:01','2026-06-08 03:46:01','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-3','','','2026-06-07 21:46:01','2026-06-08 03:46:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62974',0,'event','',0),
(62975,1426,'2026-06-07 22:10:30','2026-06-08 04:10:30','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-56','','','2026-06-07 22:10:30','2026-06-08 04:10:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62975',0,'event','',0),
(62979,1426,'2026-06-07 21:47:46','2026-06-08 03:47:46','<strong><span style="color: #cc0000">Do not sign up for this class until after you\'ve already watched the homework videos</span></strong>\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of computer aided manufacturing using Fusion360. Fusion 360 for hobbyists is the only all-in-one design and manufacturing suite so we use it extensively. This class is a heavily recommended but technically optional prerequisite to the CNC Router Authorization class. Even if you\'ve used a CNC machine a few times before then please take this class first, we only recommend skipping it if you know you\'re an expert with toolpaths, feeds/speeds, endmill considerations, etc.\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #cc0000"><strong>&lt;-- Homework --&gt;</strong></span>\r\n\r\n<span style="color: #000000">On <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/cad-cam-training">the wiki page</a> are some homework videos, <strong>please watch them before signing up for this class</strong>. You should come to this class with a computer that has Fusion pre-installed, and with some familiarity with Fusion in general. You should know how the feature tree on the left works, along with the history browser at the bottom, and how to do basic modelling. This class will show you how to program the Shapeoko to cut out your model.</span>\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Introduction to CAD/CAM (CNC101)','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-cad-cam-cnc101-4','','','2026-06-07 22:12:36','2026-06-08 04:12:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62979',0,'event','',0),
(64526,1426,'2026-07-20 13:54:45','2026-07-20 19:54:45','Learn the basics of Fusion360. Fusion is great for both designing models used in 3d printing, and for doing the CAM work to get a part cut on the CNC machine. Fusion360 is free, please have it pre-installed on your laptop.','Intro to CAD/CAM','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-cad-cam-2','','','2026-07-21 16:31:38','2026-07-21 22:31:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64526',0,'event','',0),
(64852,1426,'2026-07-28 19:44:20','2026-07-29 01:44:20','This training will authorize you to use 4 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and complete your homework before the class by reading the woodshop wiki page and all woodshop tool wiki pages. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.\r\n\r\nThis class includes:<br aria-hidden="true" />Dewalt compound sliding miter saw<br aria-hidden="true" />Saw Stop table saw<br aria-hidden="true" />Powermatic jointer<br aria-hidden="true" />Grizzly Planer\r\n\r\nThe router table/bandsaw/drum sander will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization “A”','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-30','','','2026-07-28 19:44:20','2026-07-29 01:44:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64852',0,'event','',0),
(65037,1426,'2026-08-01 14:16:30','2026-08-01 20:16:30','This training will authorize you to use 4 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and complete your homework before the class by reading the woodshop wiki page and all woodshop tool wiki pages. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.\r\n\r\nThis class includes:\r\nDewalt compound sliding miter saw\r\nSaw Stop table saw\r\nPowermatic jointer\r\nGrizzly Planer\r\n\r\nThe router table/bandsaw/drum sander will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-30','','','2026-08-01 14:16:30','2026-08-01 20:16:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65037',0,'event','',0),
(65038,1426,'2026-08-01 14:34:31','2026-08-01 20:34:31','','CNC Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-authorization','','','2026-08-01 14:34:31','2026-08-01 20:34:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65038',0,'event','',0),
(67204,1426,'2026-09-12 12:44:22','2026-09-12 18:44:22','Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.<br aria-hidden="true" />Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\nHOMEWORK: On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-5','','','2026-09-12 12:46:57','2026-09-12 18:46:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67204',0,'event','',0),
(67207,1426,'2026-09-12 12:45:04','2026-09-12 18:45:04','Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.<br aria-hidden="true" />Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\nHOMEWORK: On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-6','','','2026-09-12 12:46:24','2026-09-12 18:46:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67207',0,'event','',0),
(67781,1426,'2026-09-25 08:06:42','2026-09-25 14:06:42','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-4','','','2026-09-25 17:39:00','2026-09-25 23:39:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67781',0,'event','',0),
(67784,1426,'2026-09-25 08:06:54','2026-09-25 14:06:54','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-6','','','2026-09-25 08:09:04','2026-09-25 14:09:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67784',0,'event','',0),
(68214,1426,'2026-10-02 06:28:16','2026-10-02 12:28:16','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-37','','','2026-10-02 06:28:16','2026-10-02 12:28:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68214',0,'event','',0),
(55521,1480,'2025-11-24 20:41:26','2025-11-25 03:41:26','Skills needed: prior experience with a sewing machine\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Understand how to thread a bobbin on two machines, thread both machines, and how to use the machine to sew.\r\n\r\nAuthorization obtained: Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization\r\n\r\nInstructor: Danielle\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-2','','','2025-11-24 20:41:26','2025-11-25 03:41:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55521',0,'event','',0),
(55648,1465,'2025-11-30 20:11:17','2025-12-01 03:11:17','Skills needed: None\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Light quilting, easy sewing machine trouble shooting (threading a machine, changing a bobbin), fabric layout\r\n\r\nLogan will help you create a landscape fabric art piece the size of a postcard. You can either use the precut pieces or cut some out yourself.\r\n\r\nExamples of fabric art and fabric landscape art below.\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-55698" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/il_570xN.1636719042_ev1q-232x300.webp" alt="" width="232" height="300" /><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-55696" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/94f3fdf891739a84ed0b7c9ed60ee0cd-233x300.jpg" alt="" width="233" height="300" /><img class="alignnone wp-image-55697" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/222.jpg" alt="" width="270" height="303" />','Intro to Sewing - Make and Take - Level 100 - Fabric Landscapes','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-make-and-take-level-100-fabric-landscapes','','','2025-11-30 20:11:17','2025-12-01 03:11:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55648',0,'event','',0),
(59037,1432,'2026-03-01 20:38:15','2026-03-02 03:38:15','It\'s at <span style="text-decoration: underline"><strong>Boulder Valley Ranch Trailhead just north of boulder (Not at denhac classroom)</strong></span>. A 2 hr program where I will show you different types of telescopes, basics of astronomy, constellations, navigation, folklore, and seasonal indicators as it gets darker we will look at deep sky objects in the telescope and see the earth turning.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nCarpooling is encouraged.','Star Gazing Night','','publish','closed','closed','','star-gazing-night','','','2026-03-01 20:39:44','2026-03-02 03:39:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59037',0,'event','',0),
(59554,1432,'2026-03-14 15:14:24','2026-03-14 21:14:24','It\'s at <span style="text-decoration: underline"><strong>Boulder Valley Ranch Trailhead just north of boulder (Not at denhac classroom)</strong></span>. A 2 hr program where I will show you different types of telescopes, basics of astronomy, constellations, navigation, folklore, and seasonal indicators as it gets darker we will look at deep sky objects in the telescope and see the earth turning.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nCarpooling is encouraged.','Star Gazing Night','','publish','closed','closed','','star-gazing-night-2','','','2026-03-14 15:14:24','2026-03-14 21:14:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59554',0,'event','',0),
(60083,1480,'2026-03-28 10:53:15','2026-03-28 16:53:15','<p data-path-to-node="3">Pack like a pro! Join <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="22">Danielle</b> to create durable, custom zipper bags designed to organize your wardrobe for any journey. Fresh off an international trip where she put her own handmade gear to the test, Danielle will guide you through constructing these essential travel companions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Learn</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="5">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Perfect Fit:</b> Measuring and cutting fabric to create efficient, space-saving packing cubes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Hardware Mastery:</b> Confidently installing zippers for secure, snag-free closures.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Travel Logic:</b> Insights on sizing and materials based on real-world international travel experience.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Skills needed:</strong> You should be comfortable troubleshooting basic machine errors and working independently with cutting and measuring tools.','Make &amp; Take 300 - Zipper Packing Cubes','','publish','closed','closed','','make-take-300-zipper-packing-cubes','','','2026-04-01 08:20:07','2026-04-01 14:20:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60083',0,'event','',0),
(60104,1480,'2026-03-28 14:54:41','2026-03-28 20:54:41','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Danielle to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-4','','','2026-04-18 12:23:16','2026-04-18 18:23:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60104',0,'event','',0),
(60108,1465,'2026-03-28 15:26:39','2026-03-28 21:26:39','<p data-path-to-node="1">Discover the art of quilting with <b data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="39">Logan</b>! This make and take class is the perfect entry point for anyone curious about how those beautiful, stitched patterns come to life. You will learn the foundational "sandwich" technique, layering fabric and batting, to create a functional, decorative leaf-shaped pot holder.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="2">During the class, we will cover the essentials of measuring for precision and how to guide your project through the machine to create "quilted" textures. You’ll leave with a finished project in hand and the skills to tackle larger quilts at home.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="2"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Experience Level:</b> Beginners are welcome, though you should be comfortable operating a sewing machine and troubleshooting minor issues independently.</li>\r\n 	<li data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Skills Needed:</b> You should be able to follow measurement and cutting instructions with less oversight than a 100-level introductory course.</li>\r\n</ul>','Make and Take 200 - Quilted Leaf Pot Holders','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-200-quilted-leaf-pot-holders','','','2026-03-28 15:26:39','2026-03-28 21:26:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60108',0,'event','',0),
(61287,1449,'2026-04-30 10:26:21','2026-04-30 16:26:21','This class will demonstrate putting Celtic knots in turned objects with a focus on pens and handles. If you would like to turn an inlaid pen yourself then please bring a pen kit that only requires a single piece of wood. You can get kits from Penn State Industries, Rockler, Woodcraft, Craft Supplies USA, Turner\'s Warehouse, or Woodturningz. There are free wood pen blanks available under the lathe. If you have small scraps of nicer woods that you don\'t know what to do with (and we all know you do), this is your opportunity to use them.\r\n\r\nOther topics covered will be pen finishing.\r\n\r\nWoodshop "A" and Wood Lathe Auth required.','Celtic knot turning (Prior Wood Lathe Auth and Woodshop \'A\' Required)','','publish','closed','closed','','bowl-turning-demo-class-prior-wood-lathe-auth-required-7','','','2026-04-30 10:37:19','2026-04-30 16:37:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61287',0,'event','',0),
(61294,1465,'2026-04-30 10:58:28','2026-04-30 16:58:28','<p data-path-to-node="1">Give your furry friend a touch of style in this beginner-friendly crafting workshop! You will learn how to transform simple fabric and elastic into a charming, professional-looking bow tie that slides easily onto any standard dog collar.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Learn</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Fabric Preparation:</b> Master the use of <b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="38">iron-on fusing</b> to stiffen fabric, ensuring your bow tie holds its "crisp" shape even during zoomies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Precision Folding:</b> Learn the "Piece A &amp; Piece B" folding technique to create a perfectly symmetrical bow without complex sewing.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Assembly &amp; Attachment:</b> Practice hand-stitching to secure the bow and create a custom-sized <b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="91">elastic loop</b> that fits snugly onto your dog\'s specific collar.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Materials Used</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0">Cotton fabric &amp; interfacing (fusing)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0">Needle and thread</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0">Elastic (for the collar attachment)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,3,0">Fabric scissors and iron</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Difficulty Level:</b> Beginner (No prior sewing machine experience required).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Customization:</b> Bring your own fabric to match your dog\'s personality or use our provided patterns.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<b data-path-to-node="10,0" data-index-in-node="0">Take Home:</b> A finished, stylish bow tie and a reusable pattern to make more for every holiday and season!\r\n\r\n<a href="https://www.thecaninestory.com/post/make-your-own-doggy-bow-tie">You will be making this tutorial in class if you\'d like to review it in advance. </a>','DIY Doggy Bow Ties - Make and Take - Beginner','','publish','closed','closed','','diy-doggy-bow-ties-make-and-take-beginner','','','2026-04-30 13:22:54','2026-04-30 19:22:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61294',0,'event','',0),
(61309,1474,'2026-04-30 12:17:58','2026-04-30 18:17:58','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @oblongflight','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-46','','','2026-05-01 17:45:26','2026-05-01 23:45:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61309',0,'event','',0),
(62761,1449,'2026-06-03 14:18:50','2026-06-03 20:18:50','This is an authorization class, please only sign up if you need authorization for the lathe. Material will be provided. If you wish to use your own material please make sure it\'s at least 2.5"x2.5"x10"\r\n\r\nThe lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class - Make n\' Take Mallet','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-make-n-take-mallet','','','2026-06-03 14:18:50','2026-06-03 20:18:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62761',0,'event','',0),
