(66206,1449,'2026-08-27 10:38:16','2026-08-27 16:38:16','This is an authorization class, please only sign up if you need authorization for the lathe. Material will be provided. If you wish to use your own material please make sure it\'s at least 2.5"x2.5"x10"\r\n\r\nThe lathe turning class will demonstrate basic lathe safety, operation, and spindle turning.\r\n\r\n<strong>This class is required to operate the denhac wood lathe.</strong> <em>This class has <strong>limited attendance</strong> and generally has a waiting list. If you RSVP and <strong>decide not to go</strong>, please <strong>cancel your RSVP</strong> so the next person on the waiting list can attend!</em>\r\n\r\nTo read more about our Wood Lathe, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/jet-1236-wood-lathe&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0z0At8zjoF7anwf-Oq_bmQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">checkout the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Wood Lathe Authorization Class - Make n\' Take Mallet','','publish','closed','closed','','wood-lathe-authorization-class-make-n-take-mallet-3','','','2026-08-27 10:38:16','2026-08-27 16:38:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66206',0,'event','',0),
(66209,1449,'2026-08-27 10:57:55','2026-08-27 16:57:55','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-37','','','2026-08-27 10:57:55','2026-08-27 16:57:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66209',0,'event','',0),
(66212,1449,'2026-08-27 11:00:55','2026-08-27 17:00:55','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-34','','','2026-08-27 11:00:55','2026-08-27 17:00:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66212',0,'event','',0),
(69216,1426,'2026-10-23 23:19:03','2026-10-24 05:19:03','denhac is taking a fieldtrip! Come join us at Nicks Garden Center and grab a pumpkin to carve/decorate/paint. The space will be buying pumpkins for whoever wants one. Afterwards we\'ll be headed back to the space to make a giant mess of pumpkin carving. Let\'s all have some fun. We\'ll leave from the space around noon but feel free to meet us there.\r\n\r\n*we will be back long before the haunted house postmortem\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-69217" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/2-224x300.png" alt="" width="224" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-69218" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/1-224x300.png" alt="" width="224" height="300" />','Pumpkin Patch Fieldtrip','','publish','closed','closed','','pumpkin-patch-fieldtrip','','','2026-10-24 00:00:16','2026-10-24 06:00:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69216',0,'event','',0),
(69464,1426,'2026-10-31 12:27:15','2026-10-31 18:27:15','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metalshop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metalshop-safety-8','','','2026-10-31 12:27:15','2026-10-31 18:27:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69464',0,'event','',0),
(52211,1495,'2025-08-24 23:17:20','2025-08-25 05:17:20','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-30','','','2025-08-24 23:17:20','2025-08-25 05:17:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52211',0,'event','',0),
(53138,1495,'2025-09-21 23:10:02','2025-09-22 05:10:02','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-31','','','2025-09-21 23:10:02','2025-09-22 05:10:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53138',0,'event','',0),
(53903,1495,'2025-10-14 15:18:06','2025-10-14 21:18:06','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers','','','2025-10-14 15:18:06','2025-10-14 21:18:06','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53903',0,'event','',0),
(54095,1495,'2025-10-21 08:01:05','2025-10-21 14:01:05','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-2','','','2025-10-21 10:59:37','2025-10-21 16:59:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54095',0,'event','',0),
(54480,1487,'2025-10-30 17:00:58','2025-10-30 23:00:58','Come to learn simple sewing skills, make a seasonal item in class to take home with you.\r\n\r\nSkills required: None\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll learn: Tracing, cutting, pinning, sewing on machines, stuffing, and finishing a project, how to thread a sewing machine and change a bobbin, attaching felt to felt\r\n\r\nInstructor: Lauren\r\n\r\n(and yes you get to make faces for your pillows!)\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class.</strong>','Intro to Sewing 100 - Monster Pillows with Lauren','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-100-monster-pillows-with-lauren','','','2025-10-30 17:07:45','2025-10-30 23:07:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54480',0,'event','',0),
(55412,1487,'2025-11-23 10:58:50','2025-11-23 17:58:50','Intro to Sewing 100\r\n\r\nCome to learn simple sewing skills, make a seasonal item in class to take home with you.\r\n\r\nSkills required: None\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll learn: Tracing, cutting, pinning, sewing on machines, stuffing, and finishing a project, how to thread a sewing machine and change a bobbin\r\n\r\nInstructor: Lauren\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','Intro to Sewing 100 - Fruit Stuffies / Pillows - with faces!','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-100-fruit-stuffies-pillows-with-faces','','','2025-11-23 10:58:50','2025-11-23 17:58:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55412',0,'event','',0),
(55447,1487,'2025-11-23 09:51:51','2025-11-23 16:51:51','Skills needed: chain, single stitch, double stitch, half double stitch\r\n\r\nSkills gained: make crochet plants, 3 different types, no new stitches, learn how to build a form and make a 3D plant\r\n\r\nFeel free to bring your own yarn and hooks\r\n\r\nInstructor: Lauren\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class opens 10 days prior to class\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-55449" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/325f5b_d255c426ea8d48eaa526317eae67502fmv2-300x300.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="300" />','Intermediate Crochet - Hanging Plants','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-crochet-hanging-plants','','','2025-11-30 20:11:35','2025-12-01 03:11:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55447',0,'event','',0),
(56627,1487,'2026-01-01 23:24:39','2026-01-02 06:24:39','What you bring:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>one tshirt that is one size too big</li>\r\n 	<li>1-3 other shirts as donor shirts that we will be cutting up and using as transplants</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nSkills needed: ability to use a cutting tool\r\n\r\nSkills learned: how to cut along lines, how to thread a sewing machine, how to add and remove a bobbin, how to sew on a home sewing machine, how to use pins and clips\r\n\r\nInstructor: Lauren\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>','Make and Take Sewing - 100 Level - Tshirt adjusting','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-sewing-100-level-tshirt-adjusting','','','2026-01-01 23:24:39','2026-01-02 06:24:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56627',0,'event','',0),
(56651,1495,'2025-12-31 06:52:10','2025-12-31 13:52:10','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-4','','','2025-12-31 06:52:10','2025-12-31 13:52:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56651',0,'event','',0),
(57022,1495,'2026-01-08 18:38:40','2026-01-09 01:38:40','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-5','','','2026-01-08 23:35:20','2026-01-09 06:35:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57022',0,'event','',0),
(57023,1495,'2026-01-08 18:41:35','2026-01-09 01:41:35','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-40','','','2026-01-08 18:41:35','2026-01-09 01:41:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57023',0,'event','',0),
(57256,1495,'2026-01-15 13:01:56','2026-01-15 20:01:56','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Prusa XL upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-6','','','2026-01-15 13:01:56','2026-01-15 20:01:56','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57256',0,'event','',0),
(57332,1487,'2026-01-17 19:43:12','2026-01-18 02:43:12','Join Lauren to make fruit pillows on home sewing machines! We\'ll teach you how to use the machines.\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills required: None</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills you’ll learn: Tracing, cutting, pinning, sewing on machines, stuffing, and finishing a project.</span>\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting: How to thread a machine and change a bobbin\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Instructor: Lauren</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>\r\n\r\nExamples from her last class below:\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57336" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/IMG_4543-225x300.jpg" alt="" width="225" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57337" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/IMG_4540-225x300.jpg" alt="" width="225" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57338" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/IMG_4539-225x300.jpg" alt="" width="225" height="300" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Fruit Stuffies - ITS Level 100','','publish','closed','closed','','fruit-stuffies-its-level-100','','','2026-01-17 19:43:12','2026-01-18 02:43:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57332',0,'event','',0),
(61243,1480,'2026-04-28 23:42:54','2026-04-29 05:42:54','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Danielle to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Master Industrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nClass Outcomes\r\n<strong>Full Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.</strong>','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-6','','','2026-04-28 23:42:54','2026-04-29 05:42:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61243',0,'event','',0),
(63489,1480,'2026-06-23 20:28:37','2026-06-24 02:28:37','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Danielle to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-9','','','2026-07-14 20:22:42','2026-07-15 02:22:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63489',0,'event','',0),
(65093,1480,'2026-08-03 12:08:39','2026-08-03 18:08:39','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Danielle to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Master\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n\r\nMachine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.\r\nSafe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.\r\nTroubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.\r\n\r\nClass Outcomes\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-10','','','2026-08-03 12:08:39','2026-08-03 18:08:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65093',0,'event','',0),
