(52488,1515,'2025-09-02 14:39:22','2025-09-02 20:39:22','This optional class seeks to help members learn to confidently use the sewing machine. In addition to going over how to operate the machine we’ll discuss avoiding common troubleshoots','Intro to Sewing Machines','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-machines','','','2025-09-02 14:39:22','2025-09-02 20:39:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52488',0,'event','',0),
(57257,1495,'2026-01-15 13:03:34','2026-01-15 20:03:34','Learn to use the Prusas (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-41','','','2026-01-15 13:03:34','2026-01-15 20:03:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57257',0,'event','',0),
(58640,1506,'2026-02-22 12:59:58','2026-02-22 19:59:58','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 8 days prior to event.</span></span>\r\n</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-18','','','2026-02-22 12:59:58','2026-02-22 19:59:58','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58640',0,'event','',0),
(58912,1495,'2026-02-28 16:46:14','2026-02-28 23:46:14','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-44','','','2026-02-28 23:11:42','2026-03-01 06:11:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58912',0,'event','',0),
