(59769,1495,'2026-03-18 16:42:57','2026-03-18 22:42:57','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-47','','','2026-03-25 10:41:21','2026-03-25 16:41:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59769',0,'event','',0),
(61167,1506,'2026-04-27 20:28:39','2026-04-28 02:28:39','With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>','Woodshop A (4 spots) [Jointer, Planer, Table Saw]','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-a-4-spots-jointer-planer-table-saw-2','','','2026-04-27 20:45:57','2026-04-28 02:45:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61167',0,'event','',0),
(52593,1515,'2025-09-05 12:21:35','2025-09-05 18:21:35','Join us for a hands-on leathercraft class where we’ll start with a brief journey through the history of leatherworking, exploring its ancient roots and timeless importance in daily life. After gaining a bit of background, you’ll dive right into crafting your very own thumb thimble, learning essential techniques like cutting, shaping, and stitching leather. This beginner-friendly project is both practical and fun, giving you a useful tool for sewing or crafting while introducing you to the artistry of working with leather.','Leatherworking Class','[Optional training]  Leatherworking','publish','closed','closed','','leatherworking-class','','','2025-09-05 12:21:35','2025-09-05 18:21:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52593',0,'event','',0),
(53349,1515,'2025-09-27 22:22:38','2025-09-28 04:22:38','Learn to use the industrial sewing machine and get authorized to use it. This machine has the power to sew together almost any type of fabric, including things like velcro and leather.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Industrial Sewing Machine <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/kingmax-gc-8700d-industrial-straight-stitch-sewing-machine&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3x0ryiemnlUewXUDOMF65V" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-class-10','','','2025-09-27 22:24:16','2025-09-28 04:24:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53349',0,'event','',0),
(53350,1515,'2025-09-27 22:24:53','2025-09-28 04:24:53','Learn to use the industrial sewing machine and get authorized to use it. This machine has the power to sew together almost any type of fabric, including things like velcro and leather.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Industrial Sewing Machine <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/kingmax-gc-8700d-industrial-straight-stitch-sewing-machine&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3x0ryiemnlUewXUDOMF65V" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-class-11','','','2025-09-27 22:24:53','2025-09-28 04:24:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53350',0,'event','',0),
(53352,1515,'2025-09-27 22:30:57','2025-09-28 04:30:57','This optional class seeks to help members learn to confidently use the sewing machine. In addition to going over how to operate the machine we’ll discuss avoiding and troubleshooting common problems. Learn how to add thread to a bobbin and thread multiple machines','Intro to Sewing Machines','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-machines-2','','','2025-09-27 22:30:57','2025-09-28 04:30:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53352',0,'event','',0),
(53353,1515,'2025-09-27 22:35:51','2025-09-28 04:35:51','Learn how to use a Projector for textile projects.','How to use a projector','Learn how to use a Projector for Textile Projects','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-a-projector','','','2025-09-27 22:35:51','2025-09-28 04:35:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53353',0,'event','',0),
(53358,1515,'2025-09-27 22:41:19','2025-09-28 04:41:19','In this hands-on leather mask-making class, participants will explore the art of shaping, molding, and detailing leather into unique wearable creations. The session begins with a brief introduction to leatherworking techniques and the types of hides best suited for mask making, followed by step-by-step instruction on cutting, soaking, forming, and hardening the leather to achieve the desired fit and structure. Students will learn various decorative methods—such as stamping, dyeing, and painting—to bring personality and character to their masks, whether aiming for elegant, theatrical, or fantasy-inspired designs. By the end of the class, each participant will leave with a custom-crafted leather mask that reflects their own creativity and craftsmanship.','Mask Making / Leatherworking','[Optional training]  Leatherworking','publish','closed','closed','','mask-making-leatherworking','','','2025-10-04 12:29:15','2025-10-04 18:29:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53358',0,'event','',0),
(54146,1515,'2025-10-22 12:44:57','2025-10-22 18:44:57','This optional class seeks to help members learn to confidently use the sewing machine. In addition to going over how to operate the machine we’ll discuss avoiding common troubleshoots','Intro to Sewing Machines','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-machines-3','','','2025-10-22 12:44:57','2025-10-22 18:44:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54146',0,'event','',0),
(54225,1515,'2025-10-30 16:57:50','2025-10-30 22:57:50','Skills needed: Industrial Sewing Machine authorization or previous experience sewing\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Industrial Serger authorization. Understanding of how to thread the industrial serger and use it.\r\n\r\nNote: This class will have timeslots. Every half hour someone else can show up, according to your position of sign up. Please note how many people there are when you sign up as that will determine your position.\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class.</strong>','Industrial Serger Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-industrial-serger','','','2025-11-16 22:50:02','2025-11-17 05:50:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54225',0,'event','',0),
(54470,1515,'2025-10-30 16:55:19','2025-10-30 22:55:19','Skills you’ll need: basic sewing understanding, ability to thread a needle by hand\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Learn how to stitch button holes into fabric and attach a button to fabric\r\n\r\nNote: You can bring clothing to class to work on after class, but you will not be learning on your own clothing\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open one week prior to class\r\n\r\nTeacher: Mohr','How to Hand Sew Buttons','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-hand-sew-buttons','','','2025-10-30 16:55:19','2025-10-30 22:55:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54470',0,'event','',0),
(54474,1515,'2025-10-30 16:55:57','2025-10-30 22:55:57','How to Use Sewing Machines\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll need: none\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: How to thread our home sewing machines, thread a bobbin, learn fixes for common sewing machine problems.\r\n\r\nTaught by: Mohr\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open one week prior to class.','How to Use Sewing Machines','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-sewing-machines','','','2025-10-30 16:55:57','2025-10-30 22:55:57','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54474',0,'event','',0),
(54476,1515,'2025-10-30 16:54:06','2025-10-30 22:54:06','Skills needed: prior experience with a sewing machine\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Understand how to thread a bobbin on two machines, thread both machines, and how to use the machine to sew.\r\n\r\nAuthorization obtained: Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr or Danielle\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class.</strong>','How to use Industrial Sewing Machine','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-industrial-sewing-machine','','','2025-10-30 17:41:28','2025-10-30 23:41:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54476',0,'event','',0),
(54482,1515,'2025-10-30 16:45:29','2025-10-30 22:45:29','<strong>Timed event. When you sign up you will receive an email with a link to sign up for a time slot and explain your issue.</strong>\r\n\r\nMohr will work with you on specific issues, come prepared to make the most use of your time. These office hours are for everyone but Mohr has advanced / professional level knowledge and will be able to provide high level assistance.\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class</strong>','Mohr\'s Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','mohrs-office-hours','','','2025-10-30 16:52:49','2025-10-30 22:52:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54482',0,'event','',0),
(55418,1515,'2025-11-23 09:54:22','2025-11-23 16:54:22','Skills needed: Industrial Sewing Machine authorization or previous experience sewing\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Industrial Serger authorization. Understanding of how to thread the industrial serger and use it.\r\n\r\nNote: This accounts for a twenty minute break in the middle. Feel free to bring food and drinks as well as something to occupy yourself with in between threading opportunities.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','How to use Industrial Serger','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-industrial-serger-2','','','2025-11-23 09:54:22','2025-11-23 16:54:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55418',0,'event','',0),
(55420,1515,'2025-11-23 10:53:07','2025-11-23 17:53:07','Skills needed: prior experience with a sewing machine\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Understand how to thread a bobbin on two machines, thread both machines, and how to use the machine to sew.\r\n\r\nAuthorization obtained: Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization','','','2025-11-23 10:53:07','2025-11-23 17:53:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55420',0,'event','',0),
(55422,1515,'2025-11-23 09:53:42','2025-11-23 16:53:42','Note: Mohr is the professional level, you do not need to be to come get advice.\r\n\r\nTimed event. When you sign up you will receive an email with a link to sign up for a time slot and explain your issue.\r\n\r\nMohr will work with you on specific issues, come prepared to make the most use of your time. These office hours are for everyone but Mohr has advanced / professional level knowledge and will be able to provide high level assistance.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','Professional Level Textile Project Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','professional-level-textile-project-office-hours','','','2025-11-23 09:53:42','2025-11-23 16:53:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55422',0,'event','',0),
(55512,1515,'2025-11-24 20:34:00','2025-11-25 03:34:00','Skills you’ll need: none\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: How to thread our home sewing machines, thread a bobbin, learn fixes for common sewing machine problems.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.','How to Use Sewing Machines','','publish','closed','closed','','how-to-use-sewing-machines-2','','','2025-11-24 20:34:00','2025-11-25 03:34:00','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55512',0,'event','',0),
(56685,1515,'2026-01-01 23:06:34','2026-01-02 06:06:34','Bring a pair of pants to learn how to hem.\r\n\r\nMohr will teach you how to adjust the length of your pants by using a Textile pair to demonstrate before walking you all through step-by-step on how to hem a pair of pants by hand.\r\n\r\nWe will provide sewing needles, thread, and measuring tools. If you have your own you are welcome to bring them for the class.\r\n\r\nSkills needed:\r\n\r\nPatience\r\n\r\nSkills learned:\r\n\r\nHand sewing, measuring clothing, types of stitches, threading a hand sewing needle, adjusting clothing, sewing with thick material\r\n\r\nThere will be a small break for snacks during this class. Snacks will not be provided.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr','Pants Hemming - Learn to shorten any pants to the right size','','publish','closed','closed','','pants-hemming-hand-sewing','','','2026-01-04 13:36:17','2026-01-04 20:36:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56685',0,'event','',0),
(56687,1515,'2026-01-01 23:19:41','2026-01-02 06:19:41','<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills needed: Industrial Sewing Machine authorization or previous experience sewing</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills obtained: Industrial Serger authorization. Understanding of how to thread the industrial Serger and use it. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Note: This class will have timeslots. Every half hour someone else can show up, according to your position of sign up. Please note how many people there are when you sign up as that will determine your position.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Instructor: Mohr</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization','','','2026-01-01 23:21:16','2026-01-02 06:21:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56687',0,'event','',0),
(56718,1515,'2026-01-01 23:26:56','2026-01-02 06:26:56','<div class="p-rich_text_section">Come join us for an evening of all things nails related. Has it been a while since you had cuticle work? Ever tried a Russian manicure? Is your current set lifting and you need a touch up? Or just looking to do a full press on set? We\'ll come to the fishbowl at 8pm January 6thWe\'ll supply</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PPE</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">a wide range of Gel nail polish colors</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">E Files</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Gel X</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Brushes</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">UV lights</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0"> Acetone/rubbing alcohol</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">cat eye gels and magnets</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Feel free to bring your minis and 3d prints if you don\'t want to paint your nails</div>','Nails Hang Out Night','','publish','closed','closed','','nails-hang-out-night','','','2026-01-01 23:26:56','2026-01-02 06:26:56','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56718',0,'event','',0),
(57312,1515,'2026-01-17 19:44:05','2026-01-18 02:44:05','<p data-start="262" data-end="505">Come join Jamie and Mohr to learn how to make a simple pair of drawstring pants!</p>\r\n<p data-start="262" data-end="505">You will need your <strong data-start="301" data-end="340">hip, waist, and inseam measurements</strong> to participate. These measurements are required at sign-up. If you do not already have them, please register for the <strong data-start="458" data-end="479">Measurement Class</strong> scheduled the day before.</p>\r\n<p data-start="507" data-end="642">You will work with a <strong data-start="528" data-end="553">pre-cut pants pattern</strong>, which you will adjust and refine to match your measurements before cutting your fabric.</p>\r\n<p data-start="644" data-end="984">You may use a home sewing machine, industrial sewing machine, or serger to construct and finish your pants. Please note that <strong data-start="773" data-end="831">no machine training will be provided during this class</strong>. You must already be authorized to use industrial machines or the serger. Home sewing machines will be available and do not require prior authorization.</p>\r\n<p data-start="644" data-end="984">We will provide muslin fabric for this class, you are able to bring your own if you would like to use something else.</p>\r\n<p data-start="644" data-end="984"></p>','Intro to Pants Making','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-pants-making','','','2026-01-17 19:44:05','2026-01-18 02:44:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57312',0,'event','',0),
(56661,1541,'2025-12-31 15:03:12','2025-12-31 22:03:12','<span style="font-weight: 400;">How to use Industrial Sewing Machine</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills needed: prior experience with a sewing machine</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills obtained: Understand how to thread a bobbin on two machines, thread both machines, and how to use the machine to sew.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Authorization obtained: Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Instructor: Danielle</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>','Industrial Sewing Machine authorization or previous experience sewing','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-or-previous-experience-sewing','','','2025-12-31 15:03:12','2025-12-31 22:03:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=56661',0,'event','',0),
(57320,1515,'2026-01-17 19:43:53','2026-01-18 02:43:53','<p data-start="80" data-end="253">Join Mohr and Jamie for a measurement session that will equip you with the information needed to adjust sewing patterns to your own body measurements for future classes.</p>\r\n<p data-start="255" data-end="447"><strong data-start="255" data-end="272">What to Wear:</strong><br data-start="272" data-end="275" />Please wear the supportive garments you normally use (such as bras) and <strong data-start="347" data-end="405">skin-tight or close-fitting clothing with minimal bulk</strong>, such as leggings, yoga pants, or tights.</p>\r\n<p data-start="449" data-end="632">You will not be able to participate if you are wearing jeans, sweatpants, or other bulky clothing. If you arrive in bulky clothing, please bring something suitable to change into.</p>\r\n<p data-start="634" data-end="915">During the class, you will pair up with other participants to take full-body measurements in preparation for future classes that require them. You do not need to bring anything, we will provide all necessary tools and record your measurements so you can take them home with you.</p>','Measurement class','','publish','closed','closed','','measurement-class','','','2026-01-17 19:43:53','2026-01-18 02:43:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57320',0,'event','',0),
(57860,1541,'2026-01-31 15:14:48','2026-01-31 22:14:48','<div class="grid w-full min-w-0 grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)]" dir="ltr" data-orientation="horizontal">\r\n<div class="col-start-1 row-start-2">\r\n<div id="radix-:r6u:-content-thread" class="focus:outline-none" tabindex="0" role="tabpanel" data-state="active" data-orientation="horizontal" aria-labelledby="radix-:r6u:-trigger-thread">\r\n<div class="border-subtlest ring-subtlest divide-subtlest bg-transparent">\r\n<div class="gap-y-md flex flex-col">\r\n<div class="relative font-sans text-base text-foreground selection:bg-super/50 selection:text-foreground dark:selection:bg-super/10 dark:selection:text-super">\r\n<div class="min-w-0 break-words [word-break:break-word]">\r\n<div id="markdown-content-2" class="gap-y-md after:clear-both after:block after:content-[\'\']" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="has-inline-images my-2 first:mt-0 [&amp;:has([data-inline-type=image])+&amp;:has([data-inline-type=image])_[data-inline-type=image]]:hidden [&amp;:has(table)_[data-inline-type=image]]:hidden">\r\n<div class="relative">\r\n<div class="prose dark:prose-invert inline leading-relaxed break-words min-w-0 [word-break:break-word] prose-strong:font-medium visRefresh2026Fonts:prose-strong:font-bold [&amp;_&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Have you ever wanted to help your community but weren’t sure how? Or maybe you love technology, consider yourself a bit of an introvert, yet still want to meet people who share your interests? Here’s your chance! Join us in helping organize the IEEE Greentech 2026 and Region 5 conference in Boulder, CO, events focused on innovation, collaboration, and sustainability with student competitions and industry engagement. You don’t have to be a university student; we need everyone’s help to create opportunities, build amazing projects, and have fun competing together!</p>\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2"><strong>Event:</strong> 2026 Greentech - Region 5 Conference Volunteer Rally - Seeking denhac members\r\n<strong>Date:</strong> Saturday, March 7, 2026\r\n<strong>Time:</strong> 2:00 pm\r\n<strong>Location:</strong> Denhac classroom - Discord link available</p>\r\n<a href="https://events.vtools.ieee.org/m/536101">IEEE Event notice</a>\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2"><strong>What we’ll cover:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="marker:text-quiet list-disc">\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Volunteer roles for the 2026 IEEE Region 5 Congress, Student Competitions, and GreenTech 2026 (March 27–29, 2026, Boulder, CO)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Ways volunteers can gain experience, showcase skills, and connect with companies and professionals</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Logistics, A/V, and tech support roles for people who like to build, troubleshoot, and keep things running smoothly</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2"><strong>Organizers &amp; Contacts:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="marker:text-quiet list-disc">\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">David Smith (Conference Volunteer Coordinator): <a class="reset interactable cursor-pointer decoration-1 underline-offset-1 text-super hover:underline font-semibold" href="mailto:David.D.Smith@enmu.edu" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"><span class="text-box-trim-both">David.D.Smith@enmu.edu</span></a><span class="inline-flex" aria-label="Events from January 7 - IEEE Region 5" data-state="closed">​</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Ian MacMillan (Operations Chair &amp; General Chair): <a class="reset interactable cursor-pointer decoration-1 underline-offset-1 text-super hover:underline font-semibold" href="mailto:i.d.macmillan@ieee.org" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"><span class="text-box-trim-both">i.d.macmillan@ieee.org</span></a><span class="inline-flex" aria-label="Events from January 7 - IEEE Region 5" data-state="closed">​</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Lucy Talley (IEEE Organizing Committee): <a class="reset interactable cursor-pointer decoration-1 underline-offset-1 text-super hover:underline font-semibold" href="mailto:lucytalley@ieee.org" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"><span class="text-box-trim-both">lucy@denhac.org</span></a><span class="inline-flex" aria-label="Volunteers - IEEE Region 5" data-state="closed">​</span><span class="inline-flex" aria-label="Events from January 7 - IEEE Region 5" data-state="closed">​</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2"><strong>Additional Resources:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="marker:text-quiet list-disc">\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">Discord coordination channel: <a href="http://discord.gg/fe5pmbVq">discord.gg/fe5pmbVq</a> - Pop into Discord during the event to engage online.<span class="inline-flex" aria-label="Events from January 7 - IEEE Region 5" data-state="closed">​</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2">R5 Volunteer information: <a class="reset interactable cursor-pointer decoration-1 underline-offset-1 text-super hover:underline font-semibold" href="https://r5conferences.org/attendees/volunteers/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"><span class="text-box-trim-both">https://r5conferences.org/attendees/volunteers/</span></a></p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li class="py-0 my-0 prose-p:pt-0 prose-p:mb-2 prose-p:my-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:pt-0 [&amp;&gt;p]:mb-2 [&amp;&gt;p]:my-0">\r\n<p class="my-2 [&amp;+p]:mt-4 [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:inline-block [&amp;_strong:has(+br)]:pb-2"><span class="inline-flex" aria-label="IEEE Region 5 Conference" data-state="closed">Greentech 2026 Volunteer information: <a href="https://ieeegreentech.org/attendees/volunteers/signup/​">https://ieeegreentech.org/attendees/volunteers/signup/​</a></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class="flex items-center justify-between">\r\n<div class="gap-x-xs flex flex-shrink-0 items-center">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class="gap-xs flex items-center border-subtlest ring-subtlest divide-subtlest bg-transparent">The 2026 IEEE Region 5 Congress, Annual Business Meeting and Student Competitions will be held in Boulder, Colorado March 27 – 29, 2026. On Friday, March 27, there will be a reception from 6 PM onwards.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div class="fusion-text fusion-text-1">\r\n\r\nThe IEEE Green Technologies (GreenTech) Conference is a premier international event. GreenTech serves as a dynamic platform for practicing engineers, industry leaders, researchers, and students to present cutting-edge work, interact, and explore latest advances in various areas related to the design, analysis, control, and management of the electric power grid, renewable energy systems, inverter-based resources (IBRs), and large-scale electrification. This will also be held in Boulder.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>','IEEE Conference Volunteer meetup','','publish','closed','closed','','ieee-conference-volunteer-meetup','','','2026-02-26 12:30:39','2026-02-26 19:30:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57860',0,'event','',0),
(58056,1515,'2026-02-06 11:24:56','2026-02-06 18:24:56','Join Mohr to learn how to use the industrial serger. This involves threading 5 needles to produce the stitches found on the serger.\r\n\r\nSergers are finishing tools and used to make a variety of items. Many projects, including pants making, benefit from serger authorization.\r\n\r\nIf you are authorized to use the serger you will be able to use it in other classes, even those where only home sewing machines are available to others.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Mohr','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization-2','','','2026-02-06 11:58:20','2026-02-06 18:58:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58056',0,'event','',0),
(59027,1515,'2026-03-02 18:26:36','2026-03-03 01:26:36','<p data-start="48" data-end="217">Please note this is class is a commutation of everything we learned so far in quarter one. It requires you to take multiple make and take classes prior to signing up.</p>\r\n<p data-start="48" data-end="217">Mohr will teach you how to make a saddle bag in an evening class.</p>\r\n<p data-start="48" data-end="217">This intermediate-beginner-level sewing workshop focuses on constructing a structured saddle bag while building advanced bag-making skills through a detailed, multi-step process.</p>\r\n<p data-start="48" data-end="217">Things you should know going in: bias binding, working with curved shapes, snaps</p>\r\n<p data-start="219" data-end="526">Participants will learn to work with interfacing for shape and durability, assembling curved panels, installing straps and hardware, and achieving clean, professional topstitching. The class emphasizes accuracy, patience, and techniques commonly used in structured accessory construction.</p>\r\n<p data-start="528" data-end="682">By the end of the session, each student will leave with a completed saddle bag and increased confidence tackling complex, multi-component sewing projects.</p>\r\n<p data-start="815" data-end="974"><strong data-start="815" data-end="833">Prerequisites:</strong><br data-start="833" data-end="836" />Participants must have completed <strong data-start="869" data-end="908">at least three prior sewing classes</strong> (or demonstrate equivalent experience) and be comfortable with:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-start="975" data-end="1116">\r\n 	<li data-start="975" data-end="1005">\r\n<p data-start="977" data-end="1005">Consistent seam allowances</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li data-start="1006" data-end="1039">\r\n<p data-start="1008" data-end="1039">Following multi-step patterns</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li data-start="1040" data-end="1077">\r\n<p data-start="1042" data-end="1077">Using interfacing and stabilizers</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li data-start="1078" data-end="1116">\r\n<p data-start="1080" data-end="1116">Confident sewing machine operation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIf you have taken 3 classes with us, please post them in this link:\r\n\r\nhttps://denhac.slack.com/archives/C0A1H7EJUHE/p1772500740520709','Make and Take Level 500 - Saddle Bag','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-level-500-saddle-bag','','','2026-03-02 18:26:36','2026-03-03 01:26:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59027',0,'event','',0),
(59076,1515,'2026-03-02 19:35:42','2026-03-03 02:35:42','<span style="font-weight: 400">Join Mohr to learn how to use the industrial serger. This involves threading 2 needles to produce the stitches found on the serger.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Sergers are finishing tools and used to make a variety of items. Many projects, including pants making, benefit from serger authorization. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">If you are authorized to use the serger you will be able to use it in other classes, even those where only home sewing machines are available to others. </span>','Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','serger-authorization','','','2026-03-02 19:35:42','2026-03-03 02:35:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59076',0,'event','',0),
(60069,1515,'2026-03-27 22:30:10','2026-03-28 04:30:10','<p data-path-to-node="3">If you want your clothes to look tailor-made rather than store-bought, you need to master the dart. Darts are the "architectural secret" of sewing, they are what transform flat fabric into a 3D shape that curves perfectly around the body.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">In this focused session with <b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="29">Mohr</b>, you’ll learn the technical precision required to create smooth, professional contours:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Perfect Point:</b> How to taper and finish a dart so it disappears into the garment without puckering.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Shaping &amp; Fit:</b> Understanding where and why to place darts at the bust, waist, or shoulders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Pressing Techniques:</b> Using specialized tools to "set" the curve for a high-end finish.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nSkills needed: You should be comfortable operating a sewing machine and following basic instructions. No authorizations are required for this class.','Dart Class - Garment Making','','publish','closed','closed','','dart-class-garment-making','','','2026-03-27 22:30:10','2026-03-28 04:30:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60069',0,'event','',0),
(60078,1515,'2026-03-27 22:54:51','2026-03-28 04:54:51','<p data-path-to-node="1">Join Mohr to take your sewing to the next level by drafting and sewing a custom-fit circle skirt. This project is the perfect introduction to garment-scale sewing, moving beyond small projects to wearable fashion.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="2"><b data-path-to-node="2" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Learn:</b></p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="3">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Drafting:</b> Measure and calculate the perfect waist radius.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Handling Yardage:</b> Master cutting and sewing with large volumes of fabric.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Professional Finishing:</b> Tips for clean hems on curved edges.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">Equipment &amp; Details:</b></p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="5">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Machines:</b> Use your own or ours. If already authorized, you are welcome to use the <b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="82">Industrial machines</b> or <b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="105">Sergers</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li><strong>Fabric:</strong> bring your own, expect 2 to 3 yards needed, or use our basic fabrics</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Skills needed:</strong> basic level sewing knowledge including ability to measure, cut, and use home sewing machines with minimal supervision.','Workshop - Circle Skirt','','publish','closed','closed','','workshop-circle-skirt','','','2026-03-27 22:54:51','2026-03-28 04:54:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60078',0,'event','',0),
(60085,1515,'2026-03-28 12:37:07','2026-03-28 18:37:07','<p data-path-to-node="3">The difference between a "homemade" garment and a "handmade" masterpiece is often in the sleeves. Join <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="103">Mohr</b> for a focused workshop on one of the most technical aspects of garment construction: the set-in sleeve.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Master</b></h2>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">In this session, we move beyond basic seams to tackle the three-dimensional curves of the armscye (armhole). You will learn:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Ease &amp; Alignment:</b> How to manage the extra fabric in a sleeve cap to ensure a smooth, rounded shoulder without puckers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Notch Matching:</b> The secret to perfectly aligning your sleeve with the garment body every time.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Professional Seaming:</b> Techniques for sewing curves and finishing your internal seams for comfort and durability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Skills needed:</strong> You should have a basic sewing foundation, including the ability to measure, cut, and operate a home sewing machine with minimal supervision.','Sleeve Installation - Garment Making Workshop','','publish','closed','closed','','sleeve-installation-garment-making-workshop','','','2026-03-28 12:37:07','2026-03-28 18:37:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60085',0,'event','',0),
(60087,1562,'2026-03-28 13:15:53','2026-03-28 19:15:53','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-49','','','2026-03-28 13:15:53','2026-03-28 19:15:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60087',0,'event','',0),
(60088,1562,'2026-03-28 13:17:18','2026-03-28 19:17:18','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-50','','','2026-03-30 22:59:43','2026-03-31 04:59:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60088',0,'event','',0),
(60110,1515,'2026-03-28 15:32:49','2026-03-28 21:32:49','<p data-path-to-node="2">Move beyond flat seams and learn to treat fabric as a sculptural medium! Join Mohr for a workshop focused on creating <b data-path-to-node="2" data-index-in-node="116">structural garments</b>—the art of building 3D shapes that hold their form independently of the body.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3">This technique is a game-changer for <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="37">cosplayers</b> and avant-garde designers who need to build out specific areas of a costume, such as exaggerated shoulders, structured hip fins, or rigid collars.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Master</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="5">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Soft Sculpture:</b> Techniques for padding and "bulking" areas of a garment while maintaining a wearable silhouette.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Material Manipulation:</b> Understanding how different textile properties react when forced into 3D shapes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="6"><b data-path-to-node="6" data-index-in-node="0">Class Details</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="7">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Applications:</b> Perfect for costume builds, structural fashion, and prop-making.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Authorizations:</b> No prior authorizations required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Experience Level:</b> You should be comfortable with basic machine sewing and handling thicker, non-traditional materials.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>','Garment Making / Cosplay - 3D Bow','','publish','closed','closed','','garment-making-cosplay-3d-bow','','','2026-04-18 12:27:49','2026-04-18 18:27:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60110',0,'event','',0),
(60886,1562,'2026-04-20 14:37:13','2026-04-20 20:37:13','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-51','','','2026-04-20 14:37:13','2026-04-20 20:37:13','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60886',0,'event','',0),
(61291,1515,'2026-04-30 10:46:02','2026-04-30 16:46:02','<p data-path-to-node="1">This practical, hands-on workshop is specifically designed for cosplayers who want to elevate their look from "off-the-shelf" to "custom-made." Whether you’ve purchased a full costume or individual components, this class teaches you how to tailor those pieces for a professional, form-fitting finish.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Focus</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Custom Fitting:</b> Move beyond standard sizing by learning how to adjust pre-made garments to your specific body measurements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Upgrade Techniques:</b> Transform "out of the box" cosplay parts into high-quality, custom-fit gear.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Hands-on Learning:</b> Bring your own items to the session for direct guidance and live demonstrations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Key Details</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Target Audience:</b> Ideal for "buy and modify" cosplayers looking to improve garment silhouette and comfort.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Requirement:</b> <b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="13">Bring your own items</b> (purchased cosplay or clothing) to work on during the session.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nKnow a cosplayer who could use this but isn\'t part of Denhac yet? Bring them to either of the alteration events!','Alterations for Costumes (and clothing)','','publish','closed','closed','','alterations-for-costumes-and-clothing','','','2026-04-30 10:46:02','2026-04-30 16:46:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61291',0,'event','',0),
(61293,1515,'2026-04-30 10:47:22','2026-04-30 16:47:22','<p data-path-to-node="1">This practical, hands-on workshop is specifically designed for cosplayers who want to elevate their look from "off-the-shelf" to "custom-made." Whether you’ve purchased a full costume or individual components, this class teaches you how to tailor those pieces for a professional, form-fitting finish.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Focus</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Custom Fitting:</b> Move beyond standard sizing by learning how to adjust pre-made garments to your specific body measurements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Upgrade Techniques:</b> Transform "out of the box" cosplay parts into high-quality, custom-fit gear.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Hands-on Learning:</b> Bring your own items to the session for direct guidance and live demonstrations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Key Details</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Target Audience:</b> Ideal for "buy and modify" cosplayers looking to improve garment silhouette and comfort.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Requirement:</b> <b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="13">Bring your own items</b> (purchased cosplay or clothing) to work on during the session.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nKnow a cosplayer who could use this but isn\'t part of Denhac yet? Bring them to either of the alteration events!','Alterations for Costumes (and clothing)','','publish','closed','closed','','alterations-for-costumes-and-clothing-2','','','2026-04-30 10:47:22','2026-04-30 16:47:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61293',0,'event','',0),
(61296,1515,'2026-04-30 10:50:10','2026-04-30 16:50:10','<p data-start="80" data-end="253">Join Mohr and Jamie for a measurement session that will equip you with the information needed to adjust sewing patterns to your own body measurements for future classes.</p>\r\n<p data-start="255" data-end="447"><strong data-start="255" data-end="272">What to Wear:</strong><br data-start="272" data-end="275" />Please wear the supportive garments you normally use (such as bras) and <strong data-start="347" data-end="405">skin-tight or close-fitting clothing with minimal bulk</strong>, such as leggings, yoga pants, or tights.</p>\r\n<p data-start="449" data-end="632">You will not be able to participate if you are wearing jeans, sweatpants, or other bulky clothing. If you arrive in bulky clothing, please bring something suitable to change into.</p>\r\n<p data-start="634" data-end="915">During the class, you will pair up with other participants to take full-body measurements in preparation for future classes that require them. You do not need to bring anything, we will provide all necessary tools and record your measurements so you can take them home with you.</p>','Measurement class','','publish','closed','closed','','measurement-class-2','','','2026-04-30 10:50:10','2026-04-30 16:50:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61296',0,'event','',0),
(61615,1566,'2026-05-06 21:09:47','2026-05-07 03:09:47','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-9','','','2026-05-07 10:19:15','2026-05-07 16:19:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61615',0,'event','',0),
(61790,1564,'2026-05-09 21:38:38','2026-05-10 03:38:38','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-53','','','2026-05-09 21:38:38','2026-05-10 03:38:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61790',0,'event','',0),
(64001,1564,'2026-07-06 15:01:41','2026-07-06 21:01:41','<strong>Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-3','','','2026-07-06 15:01:41','2026-07-06 21:01:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64001',0,'event','',0),
(69448,1562,'2026-10-31 12:18:02','2026-10-31 18:18:02','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-9','','','2026-10-31 12:18:02','2026-10-31 18:18:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69448',0,'event','',0);
