(53339,1569,'2025-09-27 18:31:43','2025-09-28 00:31:43','Class will include: tracing, pinning, cutting, stuffing, and sewing. You will make a pattern and complete a finished product in class.\r\nHalloween ornaments are the October class topic.\r\nThis class will not authorize you to use the industrial sewing machine, but you will learn how to get a project from start to finish. Industrial sewing authorization is not required for this class, as we\'ll be using the basic sewing machines (no authorization required).','Intro to Sewing Projects 100','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-projects-100-6','','','2025-09-27 18:31:43','2025-09-28 00:31:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53339',0,'event','',0),
(53351,1569,'2025-09-27 22:27:54','2025-09-28 04:27:54','Class will include: tracing, pinning, cutting, stuffing, and sewing. You will make a pattern and complete a finished product in class. Halloween ornaments are the October class topic. This class will not authorize you to use the industrial sewing machine, but you will learn how to get a project from start to finish. Industrial sewing authorization is not required for this class, as we\'ll be using the basic sewing machines (no authorization required).','Intro to Sewing Projects 100','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-projects-100-7','','','2025-10-10 11:32:36','2025-10-10 17:32:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53351',0,'event','',0),
(61619,1566,'2026-05-06 21:13:23','2026-05-07 03:13:23','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-17','','','2026-05-06 21:13:23','2026-05-07 03:13:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61619',0,'event','',0),
(63745,1566,'2026-06-30 08:52:33','2026-06-30 14:52:33','Completing and Passing this class will authorize you to operate the metalworking lathes we have in the metal shop. We will go over basic setup and operation of the machine as well as some basic theory on machining. It\'s not required but highly recommended you be familiar with some basic machining concepts before taking this class.\r\n\r\nThere are resources online as well as some books and manuals in the metal shop area that are good starting resources for learning about operating these machines. You are also encouraged to ask on slack in the #help-metalwork channel for advice.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Metal lathe authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','metal-lathe-authorization','','','2026-06-30 08:52:33','2026-06-30 14:52:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63745',0,'event','',0),
(63911,1566,'2026-07-03 21:05:33','2026-07-04 03:05:33','Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required\r\n\r\nWe will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld. It is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class. You must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-authorization','','','2026-07-03 21:05:33','2026-07-04 03:05:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63911',0,'event','',0),
(63915,1566,'2026-07-03 21:12:23','2026-07-04 03:12:23','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metal shop safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metal-shop-safety','','','2026-07-03 21:12:23','2026-07-04 03:12:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63915',0,'event','',0),
(65860,1566,'2026-08-20 14:59:38','2026-08-20 20:59:38','<p>Bring your painting projects and work on them with fellow denhac members! Miniatures, props, or whatever else you\'ve been meaning to paint.</p><p>Acrylic paints and brushes can be shared if needed, but bringing your own supplies is recommended.</p><p><strong>Host:</strong> <a href="https://denhac.org/member/9K9K">Helix</a></p>','Miniature/Project Painting Party','','publish','closed','closed','','miniature-project-painting-party','','','2026-08-20 14:59:38','2026-08-20 20:59:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/miniature-project-painting-party',0,'event','',0),
(66403,1566,'2026-08-31 13:12:21','2026-08-31 19:12:21','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project. This month we will have Halloween themed patterns available to attendees in addition to our normal selection.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass - Halloween Haunted House','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-halloween-haunted-house','','','2026-08-31 13:12:21','2026-08-31 19:12:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66403',0,'event','',0),
(66412,1566,'2026-08-31 13:30:02','2026-08-31 19:30:02','This talk delivers a practical overview of how quantum computing threatens modern cryptography and what security teams should be doing today to prepare. It briefly covers how current symmetric and asymmetric encryption works, then explains how quantum algorithms like Shor’s and Grover’s undermine RSA, ECC, and weaken commonly used symmetric schemes. The session examines real-world risks such as Harvest Now, Decrypt Later and Trust Now, Forge Later, helping attendees understand which systems and data are most at risk based on longevity and impact. It also introduces NIST’s post-quantum standards and their implications for PKI, TLS, and enterprise environments. The talk concludes by comparing post-quantum cryptography, hybrid approaches, and quantum key distribution, outlining practical tradeoffs and deployment challenges. Attendees leave with a clear action plan centered on crypto agility, risk assessment, and preparing infrastructure for a quantum-resilient future.<br aria-hidden="true" /><br aria-hidden="true" />Want to get involved? Check out our website at <span draggable="true"><a href="http://dc303.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dc303.org</a></span> !','DC303: Saad Baig - Post Quantum Cryptography','','publish','closed','closed','','dc303-saad-baig-post-quantum-cryptography','','','2026-08-31 13:30:02','2026-08-31 19:30:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66412',0,'event','',0),
(66413,1566,'2026-08-31 13:33:54','2026-08-31 19:33:54','This will be an interactive lab covering the reverse engineering of msfvenom’s stageless Windows x64 reverse TCP shellcode. We will cover the basics of Windows internals, x86_64 assembly code in Windows, as well as the obfuscation techniques used by the shellcode author in an attempt to hinder static analysis. To participate in the lab, you will need a fresh Windows 11 VM with 2 cpu cores, 4GB of RAM, and 64GB of disk space allocated. A script will be provided to set up the VM with the necessary software and configurations before the talk (will post a github link in discord a week or 2 before the meetup).<br aria-hidden="true" /><br aria-hidden="true" />Want to get involved? Check out our website at <span draggable="true"><a href="http://dc303.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dc303.org</a></span> !','DC303: Nick Neal - The Coroner\'s Report: A Guided Autopsy of msfvenom\'s Windows Shellcode','','publish','closed','closed','','dc303-nick-neal-the-coroners-report-a-guided-autopsy-of-msfvenoms-windows-shellcode','','','2026-08-31 13:33:54','2026-08-31 19:33:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66413',0,'event','',0),
(68765,1566,'2026-10-14 15:50:00','2026-10-14 21:50:00','Please join your fellow members and Board of Directors to discuss the happenings of denhac, where you will hear directly from the Board on the issues listed below, and engage in a Q&amp;A session. Come in and speak with others and get engaged in the things that matter most to people at denhac! We will also be providing refreshments for those attending in person.\r\n\r\nFinal agenda is yet to be determined, but below are some of the topics that have been proposed so far. Please join #board-and-members on Slack if you wish to be involved in this discussion. Final agenda will be sent out Wednesday, October 28.\r\n\r\nTopics up for discussion:\r\nFrom the Board:\r\n-What does it take to run the space\r\n-How can we make bans more transparent\r\n-How can we eliminate variability between boards for similar offenses\r\n\r\nFrom Members:\r\n-What is the board\'s responsibility to engage membership for things such as bylaw changes, both legally and culturally?\r\n-How is the membership expected to give tough feedback in ways that don\'t put the board in a defensive position?\r\n-How will some of the potential upcoming things such as paid classes and volunteers or raising membership dues affect the culture of the space. (very explicitly not in a "we should avoid doing X because the culture will change" but aiming to understand what might change)\r\n\r\nThe moderator and Board members in attendance are subject to change.\r\n\r\nModerator: @Karly\r\nBoard Members in Attendance: @Karly @dvd @Juniper @Michael Hopkins','denhac Town Hall','','publish','closed','closed','','denhac-town-hall','','','2026-10-15 15:15:28','2026-10-15 21:15:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68765',0,'event','',0),
(69027,1566,'2026-10-22 15:44:05','2026-10-22 21:44:05','','Board Meeting','','publish','closed','closed','','board-meeting','','','2026-10-22 15:44:05','2026-10-22 21:44:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69027',0,'event','',0),
(69404,1566,'2026-10-29 00:21:20','2026-10-29 06:21:20','Install of new dust collector system. The woodshop will be closed during this time.\r\n\r\nFriday 7pm - Saturday 7pm','Dust Collector Install','','publish','closed','closed','','dust-collector-install','','','2026-10-29 00:21:20','2026-10-29 06:21:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69404',0,'event','',0),
(53357,1569,'2025-09-27 22:39:08','2025-09-28 04:39:08','Learn how to draft and sew a tote bag. Class will include: pattern making, cutting, pinning, and sewing a tote bag from scratch.\r\n\r\nFeel free to bring your own fabric for this project, otherwise it will be provided for you. You do not need authorization to take this class but should be familiar with sewing or have taken the 100 level course.','Intro to Sewing Projects 200','[Optional training] Learn to sew with a machine','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-projects-200','','','2025-09-30 13:33:49','2025-09-30 19:33:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53357',0,'event','',0),
(54468,1569,'2025-10-30 16:56:12','2025-10-30 22:56:12','Come to learn simple sewing skills, make a seasonal item in class to take home with you.\r\n\r\nSkills required: None\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll learn: Tracing, cutting, pinning, sewing on machines, stuffing, and finishing a project, how to thread a sewing machine and change a bobbin\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open one week prior to class.\r\n\r\nItem: Napkins, fabric bookmarks, potentially other options\r\n\r\nTaught by Kelsey','Intro to Sewing 100','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-100','','','2025-10-30 16:56:12','2025-10-30 22:56:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54468',0,'event','',0),
(54472,1569,'2025-10-30 16:54:42','2025-10-30 22:54:42','Learn how to make items with batting\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll need: sewing machine knowledge\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll learn: sewing through multiple layers of fabric, batting, quilting, zig zag stitch, using fabric clips, using a ruler to cut fabric, seam allowance, potentially needle and foot sewing machine change\r\n\r\nItems made: pot holders, oven mitts, hot pot holders\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class.</strong>','Intro to Sewing 200','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-200','','','2025-10-30 16:54:42','2025-10-30 22:54:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54472',0,'event','',0),
(54478,1569,'2025-10-30 16:47:18','2025-10-30 22:47:18','Class requirement: Attend Intro to Sewing 200 or have experience making items separately from classes\r\n\r\nSkills needed: Understanding of seam allowance, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues including threading and changing a bobbin, ability to read a pattern, measure using rulers, and cut along ruler lines.\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: Pockets, tie installation, create a large pattern on fabric, zipper installation, use of interfacing, working with thick fabrics, sewing machine needle and foot changes\r\n\r\n<strong>Registration for this class will open one week prior to class.</strong>','Intro to Sewing 300','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-300','','','2025-10-30 16:47:18','2025-10-30 22:47:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54478',0,'event','',0),
(55414,1569,'2025-11-23 10:58:24','2025-11-23 17:58:24','Learn how to make items with batting, interfacing, zippers, or pockets depending on the class and take them home with you! Item example for this class below.\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll need: sewing machine knowledge, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues (rethread, change the bobbin)\r\n\r\nPotential Skills you’ll learn: sewing through multiple layers of fabric, batting, quilting, zig zag stitch, using fabric clips, using a ruler to cut fabric, seam allowance, potentially sewing machine needle and foot change\r\n\r\nInstructor: Kelsey\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-55416" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/how-to-make-a-flat-bottom-zip-pouch-e1763849869491-300x272.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="272" />','Intro to Sewing - Make and Take - Level 200','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-make-and-take-level-200','','','2025-11-23 10:58:24','2025-11-23 17:58:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55414',0,'event','',0),
(55440,1569,'2025-11-23 11:00:27','2025-11-23 18:00:27','Skills needed: ability to thread and hold a needle designed for hand sewing\r\n\r\nSkills obtained: ability to thread a hand needle and use it to mend a small hole in jeans\r\n\r\nYOU MUST BRING YOUR OWN JEANS – please provide jeans with small holes (quarter size or less) to work with. You are welcome to bring additional pairs for instructor look over but they will not be worked on during class.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Bucky\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to the class running.','Jean Mending - Hand Sewing Version','','publish','closed','closed','','jean-mending-hand-sewing-version','','','2025-11-23 11:00:27','2025-11-23 18:00:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55440',0,'event','',0),
(55444,1569,'2025-11-23 10:59:47','2025-11-23 17:59:47','Class requirement: <span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Attend Intro to Sewing 200 or have experience making items separately from classes.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nSkills needed: Understanding of seam allowance, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues including threading and changing a bobbin, measure using rulers, and cut along ruler lines.\r\n\r\nPotential Skills obtained: Pockets, bias tape installation, create a large pattern on fabric, zipper installation, use of interfacing and batting, working with thick fabrics, sewing machine needle and foot changes\r\n\r\nInstructor: Kelsey\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-55446" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/images.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="168" />','Intro to Sewing – Make and Take - Level 300','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-make-and-take-level-300','','','2025-11-23 10:59:47','2025-11-23 17:59:47','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55444',0,'event','',0),
(55509,1569,'2025-11-24 17:09:03','2025-11-25 00:09:03','What it says on the tin. Only those who have previously been pinged about this should sign up.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nIf you sign up without previous discussion you will not be able to attend this event.','Textiles - Train the Trainer','','publish','closed','closed','','textiles-train-the-trainer','','','2025-11-24 17:09:03','2025-11-25 00:09:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55509',0,'event','',0),
(55699,1569,'2025-11-30 20:08:46','2025-12-01 03:08:46','Make with me - come body double for your projects or drop in for assistance with what you\'re working on\r\n\r\nThis is run with Kelsey &amp; requires no advanced knowledge or pre-reqs\r\n\r\nIf you\'ve made a make and take project and want to upgrade or finish it, now is the perfect time!\r\n\r\nThis is a drop in event - please sign up to gauge future interest but if it\'s full feel free to come anyway.','Make with Me - Advanced Beginner Level Knowledge','','publish','closed','closed','','make-with-me-advanced-beginner-level-knowledge','','','2025-11-30 20:08:46','2025-12-01 03:08:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55699',0,'event','',0),
(57303,1569,'2026-01-17 19:44:12','2026-01-18 02:44:12','<span style="font-weight: 400">Come to learn simple sewing skills, make a chapstick holder in class to take home with you. You\'ll be using interfacing, and installing a clip! </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills required: None</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills you’ll learn: Cutting, pinning, sewing, finishing a project, and installing a clip. You\'ll also learn how to thread a sewing machine and change a bobbin.</span>\r\n\r\nThe pattern will be pre-cut with a variety of fabrics, if you would like a different fabric you are able to use the pattern to cut it out during the class. Written instructions will also be provided so you can follow along.\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Instructor: Kelsey </span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57305" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/chapstick-holder-keychains-300x163.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="163" />','Make and Take - Chapstick holder','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-chapstick-holder','','','2026-01-17 19:44:12','2026-01-18 02:44:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57303',0,'event','',0),
(57306,1569,'2026-01-17 19:44:09','2026-01-18 02:44:09','<span style="font-weight: 400">Learn how to make a book sleeve with interfacing, install a snap or button, use elastic, and work with multiple layers of fabric </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills you’ll need: sewing machine knowledge, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues (rethread, change the bobbin)</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Potential Skills you’ll learn: sewing through multiple layers of fabric,  using fabric clips, installing a button by hand, installing a snap by hand</span>\r\n\r\nAs a bonus skill: potentially quilting\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Instructor: Kelsey</span>\r\n\r\nExamples below:\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57308" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/DSC01709-300x200.webp" alt="" width="300" height="200" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57309" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/FPKRGSDJDOUUS7C-300x200.webp" alt="" width="300" height="200" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57310" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/FUYU8JCJDOUUS4B-200x300.webp" alt="" width="200" height="300" />','Make a take - book sleeve with button or snap','','publish','closed','closed','','make-a-take-book-sleeve-with-button-or-snap','','','2026-01-17 19:44:09','2026-01-18 02:44:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57306',0,'event','',0),
(57314,1569,'2026-01-17 19:43:56','2026-01-18 02:43:56','<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills you’ll need: basic sewing machine knowledge, ability to cut a pattern out of fabric </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Skills obtained: Learn how to add a pocket to a shirt</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Instructor: Kelsey</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Registration for this class will open one week prior to class</span>\r\n\r\nExamples below:\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57317" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/bow-tie-pocket-t-shirt-200x300.jpg" alt="" width="200" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57319" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/types-of-pockets-3-300x200.webp" alt="" width="300" height="200" />','Install pockets on shirts - make and take','','publish','closed','closed','','install-pockets-on-shirts','','','2026-02-06 11:58:32','2026-02-06 18:58:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57314',0,'event','',0),
(57322,1569,'2026-01-17 19:43:23','2026-01-18 02:43:23','<span style="font-weight: 400;">Join Kelsey to learn how to make a round pot holder, install bias tape, and a pocket and walk out with something you\'ve made yourself using materials at denhac! </span>\r\n\r\nYou will use a precut pattern to cut fabric out for this project, you will also select from a collection of premade bias tape.\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Skills you’ll need:</strong> sewing machine knowledge, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues (rethread, change the bobbin)</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Skills you’ll learn:</strong> sewing through multiple layers of fabric, batting, quilting,  using fabric clips, bias tape installation, pocket installation </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Instructor: Kelsey</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>\r\n\r\nExample below:\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57318" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Round-Potholder-Top-Photo-300x201.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="201" />','Make a round pot holder with a pocket and bias tape - ITS Level 200','','publish','closed','closed','','make-a-round-pot-holder-with-a-pocket-and-bias-tape-its-level-200','','','2026-02-06 11:33:36','2026-02-06 18:33:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57322',0,'event','',0),
(57326,1569,'2026-01-17 19:43:19','2026-01-18 02:43:19','Join Kelsey to learn how to make a simple rollup pouch that you can use for cutlery, art supplies, sewing supplies, or makeup brushes!\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills required: None</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Skills you’ll learn: Tracing, cutting, pinning, sewing on machines, finishing a project, how to thread a sewing machine and change a bobbin</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Instructor: Kelsey</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Registration for this class will open 10 days prior to class.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Examples below:</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57328" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Custom-Tool-Roll-by-Erika-Mulvenna-1800-x-1200-23-300x200.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="200" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57329" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/DIYcutleryholderwrapsewingtutorialmakeyourown-41-200x300.webp" alt="" width="200" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57330" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/IMG_2003-4-1024x683-1-300x200.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="200" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-57331" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/pencil-roll-up4-300x232.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="232" />','Rollup pouch with customized pockets - ITS Level 100','','publish','closed','closed','','rollup-pouch-with-customized-pockets-its-level-100','','','2026-01-17 19:43:19','2026-01-18 02:43:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57326',0,'event','',0),
(58068,1569,'2026-02-06 11:27:24','2026-02-06 18:27:24','Join Logan to make pot holders shaped like leaves. You can get creative with colors and fabric. Use bias tape to finish the project. Use a home sewing machine to quilt designs in the leaves.\r\n\r\nClass requirements: Intro to sewing 100, know how to thread a machine and change a bobbin, ability to cut a pattern out\r\n\r\nYou will learn: how to quilt on home sewing machines, how to navigate the needle to make unique shapes, use bias tape to finish the project, learn how to install batting\r\n\r\nInstructor: Logan\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-58070" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/IMG_2519-225x300.jpg" alt="" width="225" height="300" />','Quilted Leaf pot holders - ITS 200 - Quilting 101','','publish','closed','closed','','quilted-leaf-pot-holders-its-200-quilting-101','','','2026-02-12 17:05:24','2026-02-13 00:05:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58068',0,'event','',0),
(58071,1569,'2026-02-06 11:24:32','2026-02-06 18:24:32','Join Rory to make sustainable heating pads filled with rice that you can put in the microwave.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll use home sewing machines for this project, nothing you use will require authorizations of any type.\r\n\r\nSkills needed: Ability to cut fabric, ability to not spill rice all over the fishbowl\r\n\r\nSkills gained: confidence with home sewing machines, ability to cut a large shape and sew it together, ability to turn fabric inside out &lt;-- this is actually a huge skill you\'ll need going forward\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-58073" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/DIY-Heating-Pad-with-Rice-207x300.jpg" alt="" width="207" height="300" /> <img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-58074" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/heating-pad-8-300x225.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="225" />','Rice Heating Pad - ITS 100 - Make and take','','publish','closed','closed','','rice-heating-pad-its-100-make-and-take','','','2026-02-06 11:24:32','2026-02-06 18:24:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58071',0,'event','',0),
(59019,1569,'2026-03-01 17:19:29','2026-03-02 00:19:29','Want to raise bread using a cover you made? Or protect your food when sticking it in the fridge to marinade?\r\n\r\nJoin Kelsey for a 200 level class to make your own elastic bowl cover to take home with you.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll learn to use home sewing machines, measure and cut out a pattern, and install elastic during this class.\r\n\r\nClass registration opens up 8 days before class.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Make and Take 200 - Elastic Bowl Cover','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-200-elastic-bowl-cover','','','2026-03-01 17:19:29','2026-03-02 00:19:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59019',0,'event','',0),
(59021,1569,'2026-03-01 18:00:07','2026-03-02 01:00:07','Join Kelsey to learn how to make a round pot holder, install bias tape, and a pocket and walk out with something you\'ve made yourself using materials at denhac!  You will use a precut pattern to cut fabric out for this project, you will also select from a collection of premade bias tape.\r\n\r\n<strong>Skills you’ll need:</strong> sewing machine knowledge, ability to correct simple sewing machine issues (rethread, change the bobbin)\r\n\r\n<strong>Skills you’ll learn:</strong> sewing through multiple layers of fabric, batting, quilting,  using fabric clips, bias tape installation, pocket installation\r\n\r\nInstructor: Kelsey\r\n\r\nRegistration for this class will open 8 days prior to class.','Make &amp; Take 200 - Round Pot Holder with Bias Tape','','publish','closed','closed','','make-take-200-round-pot-holder-with-bias-tape','','','2026-03-01 18:00:07','2026-03-02 01:00:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59021',0,'event','',0),
(59025,1569,'2026-03-01 18:06:49','2026-03-02 01:06:49','Join Kelsey to make a bucket hat!\r\n\r\nThis is a 300 level course and will require you to have attended at least 2 prior classes with an instructor at denhac before attending this one.\r\n<p data-start="125" data-end="404">Ready to level up your sewing skills? In this intermediate-beginner class, participants will learn how to construct a fully lined bucket hat from start to finish. This workshop focuses on building confidence with curved seams, layering fabrics, and following multi-step patterns.</p>\r\n<p data-start="406" data-end="690">You will practice accurate cutting, seam alignment, pressing techniques, and assembling structured components like brims. By the end of the session, each participant will leave with a completed, wearable bucket hat and the skills to recreate the project at home.</p>\r\n<p data-start="692" data-end="843"><strong data-start="692" data-end="708">Skill Level:</strong> 300 Level Beginner<br data-start="730" data-end="733" />(Participants should be comfortable threading and operating a sewing machine and sewing basic straight seams.)</p>','Make &amp; Take 300 - Bucket Hat','','publish','closed','closed','','make-take-300-bucket-hat','','','2026-03-01 18:06:49','2026-03-02 01:06:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59025',0,'event','',0),
(59055,1569,'2026-03-02 19:10:10','2026-03-03 02:10:10','Join Mohr for a pressing demo showcasing our pressing tools and get assistance in pressing items you bring in.\r\n\r\nLearn about techniques used during garment making and build your knowledge base as we work through quarter one of the year.\r\n\r\nThis starts at 8PM with open house and will be going throughout the evening upon request.','Pressing Demo - Overview of how to iron clothes for garment making','','publish','closed','closed','','pressing-demo-overview-of-how-to-iron-clothes-for-garment-making','','','2026-03-02 19:10:10','2026-03-03 02:10:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59055',0,'event','',0),
(52480,1571,'2025-09-02 13:56:52','2025-09-02 19:56:52','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-5','','','2025-09-02 13:56:52','2025-09-02 19:56:52','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52480',0,'event','',0),
(52481,1571,'2025-09-02 13:59:39','2025-09-02 19:59:39','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-6','','','2025-09-02 14:00:05','2025-09-02 20:00:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52481',0,'event','',0),
(52819,1571,'2025-09-11 20:30:49','2025-09-12 02:30:49','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-27','','','2025-09-11 20:30:49','2025-09-12 02:30:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52819',0,'event','',0),
(53499,1571,'2025-10-02 08:32:56','2025-10-02 14:32:56','<strong>Only sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.</strong>\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-29','','','2025-10-02 19:57:54','2025-10-03 01:57:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53499',0,'event','',0),
(53500,1571,'2025-10-02 08:36:06','2025-10-02 14:36:06','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-7','','','2025-10-02 08:36:06','2025-10-02 14:36:06','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=53500',0,'event','',0),
