(55617,1571,'2025-11-26 23:16:47','2025-11-27 06:16:47','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-15','','','2025-11-26 23:16:47','2025-11-27 06:16:47','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=55617',0,'event','',0),
(57166,1571,'2026-01-13 12:49:22','2026-01-13 19:49:22','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-18','','','2026-01-13 12:49:22','2026-01-13 19:49:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=57166',0,'event','',0),
(58143,1571,'2026-02-07 19:02:33','2026-02-08 02:02:33','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-21','','','2026-02-07 19:02:33','2026-02-08 02:02:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58143',0,'event','',0),
(59072,1569,'2026-03-02 19:13:59','2026-03-03 02:13:59','Join Mohr for a pressing demo showcasing our pressing tools and get assistance in pressing items you bring in.\r\n\r\nLearn about techniques used during garment making and build your knowledge base as we work through quarter one of the year.\r\n\r\nThis starts at 8PM with open house and will be going throughout the evening upon request.','Pressing Demo - Overview of how to iron clothes for garment making','','publish','closed','closed','','pressing-demo-overview-of-how-to-iron-clothes-for-garment-making-2','','','2026-03-02 19:13:59','2026-03-03 02:13:59','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59072',0,'event','',0),
(59115,1569,'2026-03-03 19:39:05','2026-03-04 02:39:05','Want to save an ugly ottoman from the landfill? Turn it into a custom piece with reupholstery! Sable will guide and assist you through the entire process from tear-down to patterning to sewing and stapling over the course of 3 weeks with drop in and drop out classes.\r\n\r\nParticipant requirements:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Bring a lunch or be prepared to go buy lunch nearby on class days.</li>\r\n 	<li>We will provide an ottoman to practice with, or you can bring your own!</li>\r\n 	<li>We will help you determine how much fabric to purchase prior to the second week.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Reach out to Sable on slack if you need fabric provided or need assistance choosing fabric or determining the yardage needed for your project. Here is a <a href="https://www.kovifabrics.com/pages/yardage_calculator?srsltid=AfmBOoqZVkMcRCAqt1b-U77KQ16c0faW5jCQcBKzBkOQkVYGDYSg2yRr">fabric yardage calculator.</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>We do not have a space to store project ottomans at Denhac so you will need to take it to and from class.</li>\r\n 	<li>An up-to-date tetanus shot is recommended. This vaccine is good for 10 years.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIf you are not already authorized on the industrial sewing machines, you will be authorized before the second class.\r\n\r\n<strong>Schedule overview:</strong>\r\n3/8 Deconstruct ottoman &amp; determine fabric amount needed\r\n3/15 Pattern and begin cushion construction\r\n<strong>3/22 Reconstruct the ottoman - yay! You built a thing!</strong>\r\n\r\nThere will also be a cushion making class on the 21st taught by Mohr.','Reconstruction - Reupholstery week 3 - putting it back together','','publish','closed','closed','','reconstruction-reupholstery-week-3-putting-it-back-together','','','2026-03-03 19:39:05','2026-03-04 02:39:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59115',0,'event','',0),
(60101,1569,'2026-03-28 14:41:06','2026-03-28 20:41:06','<p data-path-to-node="3">Level up your cosplay game! Join us for a specialized garment workshop taught by a professional cosplayer where we’ll construct a classic <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="103">rounded hood and circle capelet</b>. Whether you’re preparing for a convention or just want to add some drama to your wardrobe, this class covers the fundamentals of structured hoods, linings, and decorative closures.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Master</b></h2>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">In this session, we’ll move from flat pattern to 3D garment using professional construction techniques:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Pattern Literacy:</b> Working with large-format patterns (with a look at how CNC-cut fabric pieces come together).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">The "Sandwich" Method:</b> Learn to sew a full lining for a professional, "itch-free" interior finish.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Curves &amp; Contours:</b> Managing the geometry of a circular cape and a rounded hood.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,3,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,3,0" data-index-in-node="0">Finishing Touches:</b> Installing ribbon ties and using <b data-path-to-node="6,3,0" data-index-in-node="52">Fray-Check</b> for durable, travel-ready cosplay.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="9"><b data-path-to-node="9" data-index-in-node="0">Class Details</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="10">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Instructor: Serenity </b></p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Techniques:</b> Machine construction followed by essential <b data-path-to-node="10,1,0" data-index-in-node="55">hand-sewing</b> for the final details.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Authorizations:</b> No prior authorizations required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,3,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,3,0" data-index-in-node="0">Prerequisites:</b> You should be comfortable with basic machine operation and following a simple pattern.<b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="0"></b><b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="0"></b><b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="0"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-60103" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screenshot-2025-12-27-at-3.27.39-PM-300x169.png" alt="" width="300" height="169" /></b></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>','Cosplay Essentials Workshop: The Hooded Circle Capelet','','publish','closed','closed','','cosplay-essentials-workshop-the-hooded-circle-capelet','','','2026-04-12 17:43:34','2026-04-12 23:43:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60101',0,'event','',0),
(60114,1569,'2026-03-28 15:51:27','2026-03-28 21:51:27','<p data-path-to-node="3">Construct a professional-quality six-panel ball cap from scratch! This workshop moves beyond simple flat sewing and dives into the world of <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="140">millinery and structured accessories</b>. You will learn how to manage tight curves and internal reinforcements to create a hat that looks store-bought but fits perfectly.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">Technical Skills You’ll Master</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="5">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Crown:</b> Learn the art of sewing 3D curved "gores" to create a perfectly rounded head shape.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Internal Structure:</b> Master the installation of buckram or stiffeners to give the front panels that iconic "pro" structure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Brim &amp; Sweatband:</b> Practice topstitching a curved bill and installing a comfortable inner sweatband for a clean, finished interior.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-path-to-node="6"><b data-path-to-node="6" data-index-in-node="0">Class Details</b></h2>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="7">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Authorizations:</b> No prior authorizations required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Experience Level:</b> You should be comfortable following a technical pattern and sewing precise curved edges</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>','Make and Take 300 - Ball Cap','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-300-ball-cap','','','2026-03-28 15:51:27','2026-03-28 21:51:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60114',0,'event','',0),
(60635,1569,'2026-04-12 17:40:44','2026-04-12 23:40:44','<p data-path-to-node="4">Join us in Textiles to stitch up a custom plushie to take home. We’ll guide you through using a pattern to cut your "new friend" and show you how to give them a personality with custom face pieces.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Along the way, you’ll master the basics of the sewing machine—from threading the bobbin like a pro to quick troubleshooting. You’ll learn the magic of the "flip and stuff" technique to bring your creation to life. Come for the craft, leave with a cuddle!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">This is a beginner level class, first time sewists welcome!</p>\r\n&nbsp;','Make and Take 100 - Stuffies','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-100-stuffies','','','2026-04-12 17:41:13','2026-04-12 23:41:13','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60635',0,'event','',0),
(61157,1569,'2026-04-27 19:18:48','2026-04-28 01:18:48','<p data-path-to-node="1">Learn the art of cosplay crafting with Brittany in this hands-on workshop! This session focuses on the fundamentals of sculpting and constructing custom horns using lightweight, durable EVA foam.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Key Details</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Instructor:</b> Brittany</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Core Project:</b> Custom DIY horns.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Primary Material:</b> EVA Foam.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Materials &amp; Logistics</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Convenience:</b> No need to source your own materials beforehand, all materials are provided in the class.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Purchasing:</b> EVA foam will be available for purchase directly on-site during the class for $10.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>You can bring your own if you\'d like. Ideally white or grey 4mm but if you have other colors on hand, you can use those instead.</li>\r\n 	<li>You can purchase via Venmo, a donation to the space, or cash.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">What You’ll Learn</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0">Techniques for shaping and manipulating EVA foam.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0">Construction methods to create wearable, lightweight accessories.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,2,0">Professional tips for achieving realistic or stylized horn textures.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>','EVA Foam Class - Make and take horns with a professional cosplayer','','publish','closed','closed','','eva-foam-class-make-and-take-horns-with-a-professional-cosplayer','','','2026-04-30 13:37:08','2026-04-30 19:37:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61157',0,'event','',0),
(62774,1569,'2026-06-03 18:51:07','2026-06-04 00:51:07','<p data-path-to-node="4">Join us in Textiles to stitch up a custom plushie to take home. We’ll guide you through using a pattern to cut your "new friend" and show you how to give them a personality with custom face pieces.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Along the way, you’ll master the basics of the sewing machine—from threading the bobbin like a pro to quick troubleshooting. You’ll learn the magic of the "flip and stuff" technique to bring your creation to life. Come for the craft, leave with a cuddle!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">This is a beginner level class, first time sewists welcome!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Come make friend</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-62775" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/il_1588xN.2506030802_axse-300x225.webp" alt="" width="300" height="225" /></p>','Intro to Sewing 100 - Pride Frogs','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-100-pride-frogs','','','2026-06-03 18:51:07','2026-06-04 00:51:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62774',0,'event','',0),
(63437,1569,'2026-06-20 23:11:29','2026-06-21 05:11:29','<p data-path-to-node="4">Join us in Textiles to stitch up a custom plushie to take home. We’ll guide you through using a pattern to cut your "new friend" and show you how to give them a personality with custom face pieces.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Along the way, you’ll master the basics of the sewing machine—from threading the bobbin like a pro to quick troubleshooting. You’ll learn the magic of the "flip and stuff" technique to bring your creation to life. Come for the craft, leave with a cuddle!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">This is a beginner level class, first time sewists welcome!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Come make friend</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-62775" src="https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/il_1588xN.2506030802_axse-300x225.webp" alt="" width="300" height="225" /></p>','Intro to Sewing 100 - Pride Frogs','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-sewing-100-pride-frogs-2','','','2026-06-20 23:11:29','2026-06-21 05:11:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63437',0,'event','',0),
(66431,1569,'2026-08-31 19:54:29','2026-09-01 01:54:29','Learn how to make an Jeogori, you will leave with the understanding of how to create a wrap shirt and what a dart is, how to install one, how to create a tie out of fabric, how to attach sleeves, how to create clean and presentable clothing items.\r\n\r\nYou will likely not finish this garment during the class time. You will have a better chance to do so if you cut out your pattern beforehand.\r\n\r\nTo better prepare, please review this video guide beforehand: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KOkfQ5FvCMw\r\n\r\nHere are the instructions:\r\n\r\nHere is the pattern:\r\n\r\nPlease note that you will need to be at Denhac and connected to the wifi to download the pattern. You can use the projector at 25% to correctly cut out these pieces.\r\n\r\nNote that the pattern is drafted on someone who is 5\'2" and you may need to add length, reach out in advance and we can meet to determine how much to add. For reference, my friend who is 5\'10" had to add 7 inches to the front and back to get a full coverage jeogori but the jeogori is designed to be more of a cropped wrap shirt that comes to the waist rather than the hips for the women\'s design. It is designed to come to the hips for the men\'s design.','Intermediate garment making: Jeogori','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-garment-making-jeogori','','','2026-08-31 19:54:29','2026-09-01 01:54:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66431',0,'event','',0),
(66927,1569,'2026-09-07 13:40:23','2026-09-07 19:40:23','<h2 dir="ltr">Overview</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Learn to sew from scratch by making your own glasses case — a simple, three-layer project that sews up into a tube.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What You\'ll Learn</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Threading and basic machine operation</li>\r\n 	<li>Installing interfacing</li>\r\n 	<li>Sewing straight seams to form a tube</li>\r\n 	<li>Turning and finishing a small project</li>\r\n 	<li>How to cut a pattern out using the projector</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Who This Is For</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">True beginners — this class assumes zero machine experience and teaches the fundamentals (threading, basic troubleshooting) as part of the session.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What\'s Provided / What to Bring</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li><strong>Provided:</strong> Everything — no need to bring anything extra</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Notes</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Despite including interfacing installation, this stays a true 100-level project: only 3 layers, all smaller pieces, and a straightforward tube construction — not the more complex cutting/pressing work that would push it toward 200/300.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Links</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Pattern/written tutorial: <a href="https://www.madeformermaids.com/glassescasetutorial/">https://www.madeformermaids.com/glassescasetutorial/</a></li>\r\n 	<li>Video tutorial: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zxl-Mlr-7vg">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zxl-Mlr-7vg</a></li>\r\n</ul>','Make and take - beginner - Glasses case','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-beginner-glasses-case','','','2026-09-11 20:36:42','2026-09-12 02:36:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66927',0,'event','',0),
(52537,1617,'2025-09-04 12:45:33','2025-09-04 18:45:33','I\'m installing NixOS on my laptop and getting my flake working and potential building a custom image for orange pi - Open to all members - bring your laptop and patience for when things break','NixOS Hack Session','','publish','closed','closed','','nixos-hack-session','','','2025-09-04 12:45:33','2025-09-04 18:45:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=52537',0,'event','',0),
(54546,1641,'2025-10-31 16:15:57','2025-10-31 22:15:57','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-11','','','2025-11-03 01:41:32','2025-11-03 08:41:32','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=54546',0,'event','',0),
