(58149,1656,'2026-02-07 19:08:15','2026-02-08 02:08:15','<b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b>\r\n\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-19','','','2026-02-07 19:08:15','2026-02-08 02:08:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58149',0,'event','',0),
(58152,1690,'2026-02-07 19:13:23','2026-02-08 02:13:23','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-43','','','2026-02-21 17:46:48','2026-02-22 00:46:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58152',0,'event','',0),
(58876,1686,'2026-02-26 21:49:57','2026-02-27 04:49:57','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-42','','','2026-03-16 18:21:41','2026-03-17 00:21:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58876',0,'event','',0),
(59366,1656,'2026-03-09 16:42:46','2026-03-09 22:42:46','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-20','','','2026-03-10 09:10:38','2026-03-10 15:10:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59366',0,'event','',0),
(60728,1656,'2026-04-16 11:02:09','2026-04-16 17:02:09','<blockquote><b>Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld. It is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class. You must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-22','','','2026-04-16 11:02:09','2026-04-16 17:02:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60728',0,'event','',0),
(61307,1686,'2026-04-30 12:13:19','2026-04-30 18:13:19','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @Craig','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-45','','','2026-04-30 12:13:19','2026-04-30 18:13:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61307',0,'event','',0),
(63284,1686,'2026-06-16 19:35:25','2026-06-17 01:35:25','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/laser-cutting&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZCHJVUrkGcucAEsGrtKt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nInstructor: Craig Murray','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-49','','','2026-06-16 19:35:25','2026-06-17 01:35:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63284',0,'event','',0),
(64616,1643,'2026-07-22 08:05:47','2026-07-22 14:05:47','Sewing Machine Fundamentals 101<br aria-hidden="true" />Module: Basic Machine Setup &amp; Operation\r\n\r\nCourse Description<br aria-hidden="true" />This introductory module covers the essential skills needed to operate our 7 needle embroidery machine safely and independently. No prior experience required. Students will learn standard machine setup using default settings only, no custom adjustments or troubleshooting beyond the basics.\r\n\r\nLearning Objectives<br aria-hidden="true" />By the end of this module, students will be able to:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Thread the sewing machine correctly</li>\r\n 	<li>Set up and secure fabric in the embroidery/sewing hoop</li>\r\n 	<li>Thread the machine needle</li>\r\n 	<li>Wind a bobbin</li>\r\n 	<li>Insert the bobbin case into the machine</li>\r\n 	<li>Change thread colors/types as needed</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nSkills Check<br aria-hidden="true" />Instructor stays with each student until the machine is threaded correctly and a test stitch confirms everything is working.','7 Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-3','','','2026-07-22 08:05:47','2026-07-22 14:05:47','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64616',0,'event','',0),
(65095,1686,'2026-08-03 12:27:43','2026-08-03 18:27:43','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a more broad materials list) check out the wiki.','Laser Cutter Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization','','','2026-08-03 12:27:43','2026-08-03 18:27:43','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65095',0,'event','',0),
(65655,1643,'2026-08-16 10:47:03','2026-08-16 16:47:03','This end-to-end training will impart the skills and knowledge necessary to safely design, and sew basic embroidery projects using our 7-Needle Embroidery Machine.\r\n\r\nFor more information about our textiles equipment, check out the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','7-Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-4','','','2026-08-16 11:03:37','2026-08-16 17:03:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-4',0,'event','',0),
(65761,1686,'2026-08-18 19:47:46','2026-08-19 01:47:46','Learn to use the CNC Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a more broad materials list) check out the wiki.\r\n\r\n<strong>Host:</strong> Craig','Laser Cutter Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-2','','','2026-08-19 10:45:05','2026-08-19 16:45:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/laser-cutter-authorization-2',0,'event','',0),
(66406,1668,'2026-08-31 13:14:41','2026-08-31 19:14:41','In this introductory workshop, you\'ll learn the essentials of glass cutting, foil wrapping, and soldering in order to make your very own stained glass project. This month we will have Halloween themed patterns available to attendees in addition to our normal selection.\r\n\r\nWe have the following equipment for cutting glass: hand tools, a ring saw, a glass grinder, and the beetle bits cutting system. During the workshop you will learn how to use this equipment.\r\n\r\nMaterials are provided. We have premade patterns and a pattern book, you\'re also welcome to print out a pattern or make something from scratch. You can post your design on the <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> channel on slack ahead of time to request advice.\r\n\r\nLogistical notes: Plan for your project to take about 2-3 hours of work. The more pieces your design has, the longer it will take to create. If we are not busy, walk-ins are welcome. The soldering process can create a bottleneck. Please be prepared for a wait at some workstations, depending on attendance. Consider bringing something to keep you busy if a line forms.  Join <a href="https://denhac.slack.com/archives/C08HF2H4DHN">#help-stained-glass</a> on slack for more information.\r\n\r\nThis event is for denhac members only.','Intro to Stained Glass - Halloween Haunted House','Make your own stained glass project!','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-stained-glass-halloween-haunted-house-2','','','2026-08-31 13:14:41','2026-08-31 19:14:41','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66406',0,'event','',0),
(67499,1643,'2026-09-18 19:14:16','2026-09-19 01:14:16','This end-to-end training will impart the skills and knowledge necessary to safely design, and sew basic embroidery projects using our 7-Needle Embroidery Machine.\r\n\r\nFor more information about our textiles equipment, check out the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge','7-Needle Embroidery Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','7-needle-embroidery-machine-authorization-5','','','2026-09-18 19:14:16','2026-09-19 01:14:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67499',0,'event','',0),
