(68545,1686,'2026-10-09 15:10:20','2026-10-09 21:10:20','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @Craig','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-57','','','2026-10-09 15:26:37','2026-10-09 21:26:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68545',0,'event','',0),
(59310,1690,'2026-03-07 13:12:12','2026-03-07 20:12:12','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-44','','','2026-03-07 13:12:12','2026-03-07 20:12:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59310',0,'event','',0),
(59847,1753,'2026-03-21 00:14:08','2026-03-21 06:14:08','<p data-path-to-node="3,1">Don’t let the fly zipper intimidate you anymore! Join Jamie for a hands-on workshop designed to demystify this essential sewing skill. Using premade patterns, you’ll practice cutting and installing a zipper fly from start to finish.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3,2">We provide everything you need—from fabric to zippers—so you can focus entirely on perfecting your technique. While this class uses practice materials rather than personal garments, you’ll leave with the confidence to mend, update, or include a zipper fly as you create your own pants at home.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="3,3">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="3,3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,3,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Skill Level:</b> Comfortable with basic patterns and cutting tools. No prior authorizations required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>','Zip it Up - Fly Zipper Installation','','publish','closed','closed','','zip-it-up-fly-zipper-installation','','','2026-03-23 18:59:36','2026-03-24 00:59:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59847',0,'event','',0),
(60074,1753,'2026-03-27 22:38:15','2026-03-28 04:38:15','Join Jamie to learn how to use both the industrial and home sergers.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nYou will be authorized to use all sergers once the class is complete.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nSkills needed: none, but you want lots of patience because you\'ll be threading  a couple of needles','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization-3','','','2026-03-27 22:38:15','2026-03-28 04:38:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60074',0,'event','',0),
(60112,1753,'2026-03-28 15:37:50','2026-03-28 21:37:50','<p data-start="262" data-end="505">Come join Jamie to learn how to make a simple pair of drawstring pants!</p>\r\n<p data-start="262" data-end="505">You will need your <strong data-start="301" data-end="340">hip, waist, and inseam measurements</strong> to participate. These measurements are required at sign-up. If you do not already have them, please register for the <strong data-start="458" data-end="479">Measurement Class</strong> scheduled the day before.</p>\r\n<p data-start="507" data-end="642">You will work with a <strong data-start="528" data-end="553">pre-cut pants pattern</strong>, which you will adjust and refine to match your measurements before cutting your fabric.</p>\r\n<p data-start="644" data-end="984">You may use a home sewing machine, industrial sewing machine, or serger to construct and finish your pants. Please note that <strong data-start="773" data-end="831">no machine training will be provided during this class</strong>. You must already be authorized to use industrial machines or the serger. Home sewing machines will be available and do not require prior authorization.</p>\r\n<p data-start="644" data-end="984">We will provide muslin fabric for this class, you are able to bring your own if you would like to use something else.</p>','Garment Making - Pants','','publish','closed','closed','','garment-making-pants','','','2026-03-28 15:37:50','2026-03-28 21:37:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60112',0,'event','',0),
(61246,1753,'2026-04-28 23:47:13','2026-04-29 05:47:13','Join Jamie to learn how to use both the industrial and home sergers.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nYou will be authorized to use all sergers once the class is complete.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nSkills needed: none, but you want lots of patience because you\'ll be threading  a couple of needles','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization-4','','','2026-04-28 23:53:19','2026-04-29 05:53:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61246',0,'event','',0),
(61250,1753,'2026-04-28 23:52:27','2026-04-29 05:52:27','Join Jamie to learn how to use both the industrial and home sergers.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nYou will be authorized to use all sergers once the class is complete.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nSkills needed: none, but you want lots of patience because you\'ll be threading  a couple of needles','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization-5','','','2026-04-28 23:52:27','2026-04-29 05:52:27','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61250',0,'event','',0),
(61720,1753,'2026-05-08 11:33:58','2026-05-08 17:33:58','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/metal-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw30aHX5zhonyMOZRjExxmcq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>','Introduction to Metal Shop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','introduction-to-metal-shop-safety-31','','','2026-06-03 14:20:40','2026-06-03 20:20:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61720',0,'event','',0),
