(66424,1753,'2026-08-31 19:42:37','2026-09-01 01:42:37','Want to take your sewing skills to the next level? Come join Jamie and learn how to draft a custom pair of slacks or pleated pants! We will be using your measurements to draft the pattern, then making a quick mockup to test the fit, then making adjustments to the pattern.\r\n\r\nPlease be aware, this is not a beginner class. This should not be your first sewing project and you will need to be confident with a sewing machine to get the most out of the class. If you have any doubts about whether this class is right for you, please message Jamie (https://denhac.slack.com/team/U0A3Z051RPS) on slack and he can help.','Intermediate Garment Making: Pleated Pants/Slacks','','publish','closed','closed','','intermediate-garment-making-pleated-pants-slacks','','','2026-08-31 19:42:37','2026-09-01 01:42:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66424',0,'event','',0),
(66427,1753,'2026-08-31 19:48:23','2026-09-01 01:48:23','<div class="pYfr3c">\r\n<div class="prOLdf">\r\n<div class="g53bl">\r\n<div role="heading" aria-describedby="i.desc.1668403098">Join Jamie to learn the basics of leather working by making a small holder for a lighter, chapstick, pen, or any other small item you need to carry. You\'ll learn how to cut, wet mold, punch, saddle stitch, and finish vegetable tanned leather. Please bring your own item to make a holder for.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>','Intro to Leatherworking: Lighter/Chapstick Holder','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-leatherworking-lighter-chapstick-holder','','','2026-08-31 19:48:23','2026-09-01 01:48:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66427',0,'event','',0),
(66803,1753,'2026-09-09 18:56:20','2026-09-10 00:56:20','Join us to learn how to use the home sergers. The industrial is currently a touch finicky, but if it is in good shape we will also cover the industrial serger.\r\n\r\nYou will be authorized to use all sergers once the class is complete.\r\n\r\nSkills needed: none, but you want lots of patience because you’ll be threading a couple of needles in tight spaces.','Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','serger-authorization-2','','','2026-09-11 20:56:33','2026-09-12 02:56:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66803',0,'event','',0),
(67913,1753,'2026-09-30 19:06:19','2026-10-01 01:06:19','Join Jamie to learn how to use both the industrial and home sergers.\r\n\r\nYou will be authorized to use all sergers once the class is complete.\r\n\r\nSkills needed: none, but you want lots of patience because you’ll be threading a couple of needles','Industrial Serger Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-serger-authorization-11','','','2026-09-30 19:06:19','2026-10-01 01:06:19','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67913',0,'event','',0),
(68127,1753,'2026-10-01 13:51:12','2026-10-01 19:51:12','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left;"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-25','','','2026-10-01 13:51:12','2026-10-01 19:51:12','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68127',0,'event','',0),
(68768,1753,'2026-10-14 16:04:44','2026-10-14 22:04:44','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metalshop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metalshop-safety-5','','','2026-10-15 10:17:07','2026-10-15 16:17:07','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68768',0,'event','',0),
(59382,1755,'2026-03-09 20:46:15','2026-03-10 02:46:15','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-46','','','2026-03-09 20:46:15','2026-03-10 02:46:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59382',0,'event','',0),
(59985,1755,'2026-03-25 10:38:12','2026-03-25 16:38:12','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-48','','','2026-03-25 10:38:34','2026-03-25 16:38:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=59985',0,'event','',0),
(61605,1755,'2026-05-06 17:29:30','2026-05-06 23:29:30','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Z7NYu6JokRmLMIg6nQBAM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3d Printer Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-class-52','','','2026-05-06 17:29:30','2026-05-06 23:29:30','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61605',0,'event','',0),
(62672,1755,'2026-06-01 17:37:53','2026-06-01 23:37:53','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2F3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1780783620000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2w-X5IsxvpdZOTbDuQ811y" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-2','','','2026-06-01 17:38:15','2026-06-01 23:38:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62672',0,'event','',0),
(62679,1755,'2026-06-01 17:36:14','2026-06-01 23:36:14','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-xl-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-8','','','2026-06-02 19:38:28','2026-06-03 01:38:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62679',0,'event','',0),
(62954,1755,'2026-06-07 12:37:08','2026-06-07 18:37:08','In this class, you will observe as Juniper tears down a Prusa MK4S\'s extruder and X-axis, learn what each component does and the mechanics of a 3D printer, and then collaborate with classmates to rebuild it from Prusa\'s official assembly guide. After this, you\'ll learn about how to troubleshoot the printers and run through some practice scenarios.\r\n\r\nYou will learn about:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>The three axis motors that operate the printer.</li>\r\n 	<li>Belt tensioning and lubrication procedures.</li>\r\n 	<li>The construction and intricacies/oddities of the Nextruder system.</li>\r\n 	<li>Prusa\'s official recommendations for printed replacement parts.</li>\r\n 	<li>How to run setup calibrations and self-tests.</li>\r\n 	<li>Common member complaints about the printers and how to troubleshoot them.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nAfter taking this class, you will become a trusted maintainer and expected to assist in troubleshooting and repairs when you are available.\r\n\r\nJuniper will provide food for attendees from the SIG budget.\r\n\r\nPlease only sign up for this event if you have previously spoken with Juniper about maintenance. If you haven\'t done so but are interested in this class, please DM her on Slack.','Prusa MK4S Maintenance Class (read description)','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-mk4s-maintenance-class-read-description','','','2026-06-07 12:37:08','2026-06-07 18:37:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62954',0,'event','',0),
(63575,1755,'2026-06-27 08:36:03','2026-06-27 14:36:03','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers','','','2026-06-27 08:36:03','2026-06-27 14:36:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63575',0,'event','',0),
(63576,1755,'2026-06-27 08:36:05','2026-06-27 14:36:05','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2F3d-printing&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1780783620000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2w-X5IsxvpdZOTbDuQ811y" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-4','','','2026-06-27 08:36:05','2026-06-27 14:36:05','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63576',0,'event','',0),
(64006,1755,'2026-07-06 15:33:08','2026-07-06 21:33:08','Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\nHOMEWORK: On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-4','','','2026-07-06 15:33:08','2026-07-06 21:33:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64006',0,'event','',0),
(64121,1755,'2026-07-09 08:00:52','2026-07-09 14:00:52','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-2','','','2026-07-09 17:15:45','2026-07-09 23:15:45','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64121',0,'event','',0),
(64517,1755,'2026-07-20 09:03:44','2026-07-20 15:03:44','This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only, if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.\r\n\r\nClass will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.\r\n\r\nTopics covered:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li>Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li>Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li>PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li>Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li>Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','intro-to-cad-cam','','','2026-07-20 15:57:20','2026-07-20 21:57:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64517',0,'event','',0),
(64520,1755,'2026-07-20 10:09:17','2026-07-20 16:09:17','','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization','','','2026-07-20 10:09:17','2026-07-20 16:09:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64520',0,'event','',0),
(64724,1755,'2026-07-25 10:47:10','2026-07-25 16:47:10','Come learn about Denhac\'s newest printer, the Prusa Core One+! You\'ll learn about loading and unloading, strengths and weaknesses, how it works, and general tips and tricks for how to get the most out of its capabilities. Juniper will give an overview and take questions about the printer.\r\n\r\nPlease note that this class is NOT an authorization class, and it is NOT REQUIRED in order for you to use the new printer. This is simply an elective overview for those who are curious about our new equipment and want tips for using it. However, you still need the main FDM 3D Printing Authorization in order to use ANY of our printers.','Prusa Core One+ Primer','','publish','closed','closed','','prusa-core-one-primer','','','2026-07-26 04:33:28','2026-07-26 10:33:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64724',0,'event','',0),
(65658,1755,'2026-08-16 10:52:53','2026-08-16 16:52:53','Learn to use the Prusa MK4S and Core One+ (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers check out the wiki.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-8','','','2026-08-16 10:52:53','2026-08-16 16:52:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65658',0,'event','',0),
(65661,1755,'2026-08-16 11:08:45','2026-08-16 17:08:45','This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of Prusa printers only. If you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers, this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers. This class assumes that you have some experience with 3D printing and understand slicer basics as taught in the basic FDM 3D printing authorization class.\r\n\r\nTopics covered:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Loading/unloading the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li>Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li>Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL</li>\r\n 	<li>PrusaSlicer configuration</li>\r\n 	<li>Painting objects in PrusaSlicer</li>\r\n 	<li>Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you’re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-3','','','2026-08-16 11:27:59','2026-08-16 17:27:59','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-3',0,'event','',0),
