(67778,1755,'2026-09-25 08:07:28','2026-09-25 14:07:28','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of 3D printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL/Snapmaker U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL/U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer/Snapmaker Orca configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer and Snapmaker Orca</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on multi-tool printers you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you\'re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-7','','','2026-09-25 17:38:53','2026-09-25 23:38:53','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67778',0,'event','',0),
(67787,1755,'2026-09-25 08:06:46','2026-09-25 14:06:46','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-5','','','2026-09-25 08:06:46','2026-09-25 14:06:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67787',0,'event','',0),
(58177,1768,'2026-02-08 15:33:58','2026-02-08 22:33:58','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄⌄</strong></span>\r\n\r\n<span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>BOOKINGS OPEN  1  WEEK PRIOR</strong></span></span>\r\n\r\n<strong><span style="color: #ff0000">^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^</span></strong>\r\n\r\nJoin Rory in making a custom 5x8 notebook using Japanese 4-hole stab binding.\r\n\r\nThis traditional method is great for sketchbooks, journals, guestbooks, zines, or any other blank-paper projects. You’ll leave this class with a completed project and the skills to tackle more complicated stab binding techniques.\r\n\r\nMaterials will be provided. If you would like to bring cover paper from home, please ensure it is minimum 66.7lb/180gsm weight.\r\n\r\nSkills you’ll learn: Creating templates, using an awl and curved needle, sewing pages.','Bookbinding Fundamentals: Japanese Stab Binding','','publish','closed','closed','','bookbinding-fundamentals-japanese-stab-binding','','','2026-02-08 16:01:48','2026-02-08 23:01:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58177',0,'event','',0),
(58577,1757,'2026-02-24 20:10:07','2026-02-25 03:10:07','Want to save an ugly ottoman from the landfill? Turn it into a custom piece with reupholstery! Sable will guide and assist you through the entire process from tear-down to patterning to sewing and stapling over the course of 3 weeks with drop in and drop out classes.\r\n\r\nParticipant requirements:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Bring a lunch or be prepared to go buy lunch nearby on class days.</li>\r\n 	<li>We will provide an ottoman to practice with, or you can bring your own!</li>\r\n 	<li>We will help you determine how much fabric to purchase prior to the second week.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Reach out to Sable on slack if you need fabric provided or need assistance choosing fabric or determining the yardage needed for your project. Here is a <a href="https://www.kovifabrics.com/pages/yardage_calculator?srsltid=AfmBOoqZVkMcRCAqt1b-U77KQ16c0faW5jCQcBKzBkOQkVYGDYSg2yRr">fabric yardage calculator.</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>We do not have a space to store project ottomans at Denhac so you will need to take it to and from class.</li>\r\n 	<li>An up-to-date tetanus shot is recommended. This vaccine is good for 10 years.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIf you are not already authorized on the industrial sewing machines, you will be authorized before the second class.\r\n\r\n<strong>Schedule overview:</strong>\r\n<strong>3/15 Deconstruct ottoman &amp; determine fabric amount needed</strong>\r\n3/22 Pattern and begin cushion construction\r\n3/29 Reconstruct the ottoman - yay! You built a thing!\r\n\r\nThis class is the only one that is 8 hours, subsequent classes will be 5 hours.\r\n\r\nThere will also be a cushion making class on the 21st taught by Mohr.','Deconstruct an ottoman - reupholstery class 1 - deconstruction','','publish','closed','closed','','reupholstery-from-start-to-finish-4-weeks-of-workshops','','','2026-03-08 23:39:02','2026-03-09 05:39:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58577',0,'event','',0),
(58579,1757,'2026-02-24 20:11:18','2026-02-25 03:11:18','Want to save an ugly ottoman from the landfill? Turn it into a custom piece with reupholstery! Sable will guide and assist you through the entire process from tear-down to patterning to sewing and stapling over the course of 3 weeks with drop in and drop out classes.\r\n\r\nParticipant requirements:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Bring a lunch or be prepared to go buy lunch nearby on class days.</li>\r\n 	<li>We will provide an ottoman to practice with, or you can bring your own!</li>\r\n 	<li>We will help you determine how much fabric to purchase prior to the second week.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Reach out to Sable on slack if you need fabric provided or need assistance choosing fabric or determining the yardage needed for your project. Here is a <a href="https://www.kovifabrics.com/pages/yardage_calculator?srsltid=AfmBOoqZVkMcRCAqt1b-U77KQ16c0faW5jCQcBKzBkOQkVYGDYSg2yRr">fabric yardage calculator.</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>We do not have a space to store project ottomans at Denhac so you will need to take it to and from class.</li>\r\n 	<li>An up-to-date tetanus shot is recommended. This vaccine is good for 10 years.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIf you are not already authorized on the industrial sewing machines, you will be authorized before the second class.\r\n\r\n<strong>Schedule overview:</strong>\r\n3/8 Deconstruct ottoman &amp; determine fabric amount needed\r\n<strong>3/15 Pattern and begin cushion construction</strong>\r\n3/22 Reconstruct the ottoman - yay! You built a thing!\r\n\r\nThere will also be a cushion making class on the 21st taught by Mohr.','Pattern &amp; cushion making - reupholstery class 2','','publish','closed','closed','','reupholstery-from-start-to-finish-week-2','','','2026-03-03 19:36:36','2026-03-04 02:36:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=58579',0,'event','',0),
(60067,1768,'2026-03-27 22:16:17','2026-03-28 04:16:17','Join Rory to learn how to make heat packs with rice. This will be a simple project using squares and rectangles to complete, easy to cut out and finish.\r\n\r\nAll items will be provided, including the machines!\r\n\r\n<strong>Skills needed:</strong> Absolutely none! Come and learn how to use a home sewing machine for the first time, or come just because you want to make a heat pack!','Make &amp; Take 100 - Rice Heat Pack','','publish','closed','closed','','make-take-100-rice-heat-pack','','','2026-03-27 22:16:17','2026-03-28 04:16:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60067',0,'event','',0),
(60072,1757,'2026-03-27 22:35:09','2026-03-28 04:35:09','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Sable to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-3','','','2026-03-28 14:50:20','2026-03-28 20:50:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60072',0,'event','',0),
(60076,1768,'2026-03-27 22:45:06','2026-03-28 04:45:06','<p data-path-to-node="3">Join Rory to discover <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="30">Stab Binding</b> (also known as <i data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="58">Yotsume Toji</i>), a traditional method that transforms loose sheets of paper into a beautiful, professional-looking volume.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4">It is the ultimate technique for creating custom journals, art portfolios, or binding loose-leaf sketches into a permanent collection.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6">In this hands-on session with Rory, you will master the mechanics and aesthetics of book construction:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="7">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The "Stab" Technique:</b> Learn to use an awl or punch to create clean, aligned holes through a thick stack of paper.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="7,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="7,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Decorative Stitching:</b> Master the classic four-hole stitch pattern, learning how to tension your thread for both durability and style.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nSkills needed: None! It\'s perfect for beginners, though you should be comfortable using basic measuring and punching tools.','Stab Binding - Bookbinding Class','','publish','closed','closed','','stab-binding-bookbinding-class','','','2026-04-18 12:25:50','2026-04-18 18:25:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=60076',0,'event','',0),
(61239,1757,'2026-04-28 23:34:17','2026-04-29 05:34:17','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Sable to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Master Industrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nClass Outcomes\r\n<strong>Full Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.</strong>','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-5','','','2026-04-28 23:43:40','2026-04-29 05:43:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61239',0,'event','',0),
(61288,1785,'2026-04-30 10:31:18','2026-04-30 16:31:18','<p data-path-to-node="1">In this "Make and Take" workshop, you\'ll join Danielle and transition from raw materials to a finished, functional accessory. This session focuses on practical sewing and assembly techniques to create a personalized fanny pack from scratch.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Key Project</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Goal:</b> Design and assemble a custom fanny pack.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Result:</b> A "Make and Take" experience—you walk out with a completed, ready-to-wear bag.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Skills &amp; Components</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Hardware Integration:</b> Learn how to properly attach <b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="51">webbing</b> and secure <b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="70">buckles</b> for a durable, adjustable fit.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Assembly:</b> Master the construction steps required to turn fabric and notions into a professional-looking utility bag.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Functional Design:</b> Explore the basics of spatial planning for wearable gear.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<blockquote data-path-to-node="8">\r\n<p data-path-to-node="8,0"><b data-path-to-node="8,0" data-index-in-node="0">Note:</b> This class is perfect for those looking to bridge the gap between basic crafting and functional gear-making!</p>\r\n</blockquote>','Make and Take - Intermediate Beginner - Fanny Pack','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-intermediate-beginner-fanny-pack','','','2026-04-30 10:31:18','2026-04-30 16:31:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61288',0,'event','',0),
(61313,1768,'2026-04-30 13:00:29','2026-04-30 19:00:29','Learn the fundamentals of bookbinding in this hands-on class focused on the classic single-section pamphlet stitch. This beginner-friendly method is one of the most versatile and accessible ways to bind paper, making it perfect for zines, small booklets, journals, and other creative projects.\r\n\r\n<br aria-hidden="true" />We\'ll go step-by-step through the process of folding pages, preparing your materials, and sewing your binding using a basic three-hole stitch. We’ll cover essential tools, paper selection, and simple techniques to achieve a clean, polished result.\r\n\r\n<br aria-hidden="true" />By the end of class, you’ll leave with your own completed softcover pamphlet and the skills to continue making your own bound pieces at home.\r\n\r\nSkills needed: None! It\'s perfect for beginners, though you should be comfortable using basic measuring and punching tools.','Intro to Pamphlet Binding','','publish','closed','closed','','pamphlet-binding-stab-bookbinding-class','','','2026-04-30 13:23:51','2026-04-30 19:23:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61313',0,'event','',0),
(61315,1768,'2026-04-30 13:35:19','2026-04-30 19:35:19','<p data-path-to-node="1">Build your new favorite everyday bag in this practical, skill-building workshop! This session focuses on constructing a sturdy, professional-grade tote bag featuring reinforced webbing handles and a functional exterior pocket.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Key Project Features</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Tote:</b> A spacious, durable bag designed for daily use.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">External Storage:</b> Learn the "patch pocket" technique to add an accessible exterior pocket—perfect for keys or a phone.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Structural Support:</b> Work with high-strength <b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="44">webbing</b> to create comfortable, heavy-duty handles.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Skills You’ll Learn</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Precision Topstitching:</b> Master the art of clean, visible stitches to give your bag a high-end look.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Reinforcement:</b> Learn "box-X" stitching and other methods to ensure your handles can carry a heavy load without tearing.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Pocket Alignment:</b> Discover how to center and secure pockets so they stay level and secure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,3,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,3,0" data-index-in-node="0">Boxing Corners:</b> Learn the secret to giving your bag a flat bottom so it stands up on its own.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Details</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Focus:</b> Functional sewing and hardware integration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Difficulty:</b> Suitable for those comfortable with a straight stitch who want to level up their construction skills.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Take Home:</b> A completed, custom-made tote bag ready for the grocery store, the beach, the convention, or the craft fair.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<blockquote data-path-to-node="10">\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0" data-index-in-node="0">Pro Tip:</b> This class is a fantastic "next step" for anyone who has mastered the basics and wants to start making their own durable gear!</p>\r\n</blockquote>','Tote Bag - Make and Take - Intermediate / 200','','publish','closed','closed','','tote-bag-make-and-take-intermediate-200','','','2026-05-11 21:55:24','2026-05-12 03:55:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61315',0,'event','',0),
(62773,1757,'2026-06-03 18:17:37','2026-06-04 00:17:37','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Sable to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-7','','','2026-06-03 18:17:37','2026-06-04 00:17:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62773',0,'event','',0),
(63488,1757,'2026-06-23 20:19:49','2026-06-24 02:19:49','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Sable to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these "workhorse" machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-8','','','2026-06-23 20:19:49','2026-06-24 02:19:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63488',0,'event','',0),
(65965,1757,'2026-08-22 09:09:51','2026-08-22 15:09:51','Unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n<h3>What You’ll Master</h3>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li><strong>Machine Anatomy:</strong> Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li><strong>Safe Operation:</strong> Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li><strong>Troubleshooting:</strong> How to thread, tension, and maintain these “workhorse” machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Class Outcomes</h3>\r\n<strong>Full Authorization:</strong> By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.\r\n\r\n<strong>Host:</strong> Sable','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-11','','','2026-08-24 08:49:24','2026-08-24 14:49:24','',0,'https://denhac.org/events/industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-11',0,'event','',0),
(66812,1757,'2026-09-09 18:56:16','2026-09-10 00:56:16','<p data-path-to-node="4">Start the Halloween season off right! Join us in Textiles to stitch up a simple ghost or pumpkin plushie.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">Along the way, you’ll master the basics of the sewing machine—from threading the bobbin like a pro to quick troubleshooting. You’ll learn the magic of the “flip and stuff” technique to bring your creation to life. Come for the craft, leave with a cuddle!</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">This is a beginner level class, first time sewists welcome!</p>','Make and Take 100 - Spooky Stuffies','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-100-spooky-stuffies','','','2026-09-09 18:56:16','2026-09-10 00:56:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66812',0,'event','',0),
(67791,1755,'2026-09-25 08:06:49','2026-09-25 14:06:49','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL/Snapmaker U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL/U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer/Snapmaker Orca configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer/Snapmaker Orca</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL/U1 you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you’re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-6','','','2026-09-25 08:06:49','2026-09-25 14:06:49','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67791',0,'event','',0),
(67884,1757,'2026-09-30 19:09:36','2026-10-01 01:09:36','It does exactly what it says on the tin! Join Sable to unlock the full potential of our heavy-duty equipment. If you’ve ever struggled with thick denim, leather, or multiple layers of canvas on a home machine, this is the class that changes everything.\r\n\r\n<strong>What You’ll Master</strong>\r\nIndustrial machines are built for speed and strength. In this certification session, you will learn:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Machine Anatomy: Understanding the unique motor and needle systems of our industrial fleet.</li>\r\n 	<li>Safe Operation: Mastering the foot pedal (it’s faster than you think!) and knee-lift controls.</li>\r\n 	<li>Troubleshooting: How to thread, tension, and maintain these “workhorse” machines for heavy-duty projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Class Outcomes</strong>\r\nFull Authorization: By the end of this session, you will be officially authorized to use both of our industrial sewing machines for your own projects.','Industrial Sewing Machine Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','industrial-sewing-machine-authorization-14','','','2026-09-30 19:09:36','2026-10-01 01:09:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67884',0,'event','',0),
(68495,1755,'2026-10-14 15:54:11','2026-10-14 21:54:11','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-8','','','2026-10-19 12:20:48','2026-10-19 18:20:48','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68495',0,'event','',0),
(68542,1764,'2026-10-09 15:19:21','2026-10-09 21:19:21','<pre>Bikes rock! They can be a bummer to repair though, especially if you\'re unfamiliar with how things work, or what tools you need. Come to this Skillshare to get the knowledge you need to start wrenching away!\r\n\r\nI am prepared to teach the following topics:\r\n\r\n### Fundamentals\r\n* Fixing a flat\r\n* ABC Bike safety checks\r\n* Basic bike fitting and adjustments\r\n\r\n### Basic Maintenance\r\n* Brake and shift cable replacement\r\n* Mechanical rim &amp; disk brake tuning, maintenance, and overhaul\r\n* Derailleur tuning, adjustment, and alignment\r\n\r\nAttendees: If you have a bike, please bring it! Especially if it is broken / flat etc. Feel free to bring tools if you would like, though I will be bringing a (mostly) full shop set. If you have a bike repair stand, it would be useful if you could bring that.</pre>','Bike Repair 101 - Tires, Brakes, and Derailleurs','','publish','closed','closed','','bike-repair-101-tires-brakes-and-derailleurs','','','2026-10-09 15:19:35','2026-10-09 21:19:35','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68542',0,'event','',0),
(68550,1764,'2026-10-09 15:20:39','2026-10-09 21:20:39','<pre>Does your derailleur make a weird clicking sound when you ride? Does your wheel wobble, or have a broken spoke clanking around? Do you want to switch up your gears, or *gasp*, do a fixie conversion? This is the class for you.\r\n\r\n### Overhauls &amp; Tuning\r\n* Basics of wheel repair and truing\r\n* Bottom bracket basics, overhaul, &amp; crank adjustment\r\n* Chainring replacement\r\n* Freewheel and freehub cassette service\r\n\r\nAttendees: If you have a bike, please bring it! Especially if it is broken / flat etc. Feel free to bring tools if you would like, though I will be bringing a (mostly) full shop set. If you have a bike repair stand, it would be useful if you could bring that.</pre>','Bike Repair 201 - Tuning &amp; Overhaul','','publish','closed','closed','','bike-repair-201-tuning-overhaul','','','2026-10-09 15:20:39','2026-10-09 21:20:39','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68550',0,'event','',0),
(69248,1757,'2026-10-25 10:11:28','2026-10-25 16:11:28','Do you need a last minute Halloween costume?\r\n\r\nLearn to sew a witchy hat with Jamie, following this tutorial: <a href="https://youtu.be/bwDo4R6wtu4">https://youtu.be/bwDo4R6wtu4</a>\r\n\r\nSewing machine experience is recommended for this class. Pattern and fabric are provided. Some hand sewing to finish the lining.','Make and Take 200 - Witchy Hat','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-200-witchy-hat','','','2026-10-25 10:11:28','2026-10-25 16:11:28','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69248',0,'event','',0),
(61227,1800,'2026-04-28 23:09:23','2026-04-29 05:09:23','With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-21','','','2026-04-28 23:21:14','2026-04-29 05:21:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61227',0,'event','',0),
(61299,1859,'2026-04-30 11:20:03','2026-04-30 17:20:03','<p data-path-to-node="1">Discover the meditative and tactile art of rug hooking in this comprehensive two-part workshop. This series takes you from a blank canvas to a textured masterpiece, covering everything from design theory to hands-on technique.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Session 1: The Blueprint &amp; Palette &lt;-- You are here</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Theory &amp; Inspiration:</b> An informational deep dive into the history and styles of rug hooking.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Custom Design:</b> Learn how to translate your ideas onto backing fabric. You will spend this session sketching and finalizing your own original pattern.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Color Curation:</b> Explore Carol\'s library of fibers to select the perfect yarn weights and color palettes to bring your design to life. You will leave the session with color ideas so you can purchase your own yarn, or use the yarn at Denhac.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Session 2: Hooking Technique &amp; Execution (May 20th)</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Fundamentals:</b> Master the "pull-up" technique to create consistent loops and professional-grade texture.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Instructional Guidance:</b> Get hands-on coaching on tension control, navigating curves, and filling in your pattern efficiently.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Troubleshooting:</b> Learn how to fix common mistakes and finish the edges of your piece for a durable, long-lasting result.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Part One:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="21">conceptualization and material selection</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Part Two:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="21">active crafting and technical mastery</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Take Home:</b> Your custom-designed project and the skills needed to finish it at your own pace.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<blockquote data-path-to-node="10">\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0" data-index-in-node="0">Materials Note:</b> All specialized hooks, frames, and backing materials will be provided or discussed during the first session.</p>\r\n</blockquote>','Carol\'s Hooking Class for Rugs - Part 1','','publish','closed','closed','','carols-hooking-class-for-rugs-part-1','','','2026-04-30 11:20:03','2026-04-30 17:20:03','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61299',0,'event','',0),
