ta-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Troubleshooting:</b> Learn how to fix common mistakes and finish the edges of your piece for a durable, long-lasting result.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Part One:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="21">conceptualization and material selection</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Part Two:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="21">active crafting and technical mastery</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Take Home:</b> Your custom-designed project and the skills needed to finish it at your own pace.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<blockquote data-path-to-node="10">\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0" data-index-in-node="0">Materials Note:</b> All specialized hooks, frames, and backing materials will be provided or discussed during the first session.</p>\r\n</blockquote>','Carol\'s Hooking Class for Rugs - Part 2 - Must have attended part 1','','publish','closed','closed','','carols-hooking-class-for-rugs-part-2-must-have-attended-part-1','','','2026-04-30 11:21:22','2026-04-30 17:21:22','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=61301',0,'event','',0),
(62386,1800,'2026-05-26 10:23:59','2026-05-26 16:23:59','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="color: #ff3232; text-decoration: underline;">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-22','','','2026-05-30 10:35:15','2026-05-30 16:35:15','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62386',0,'event','',0),
(63468,1800,'2026-06-22 11:34:01','2026-06-22 17:34:01','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-27','','','2026-06-22 11:34:01','2026-06-22 17:34:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63468',0,'event','',0),
(63471,1800,'2026-06-22 11:37:31','2026-06-22 17:37:31','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-27','','','2026-06-22 11:37:31','2026-06-22 17:37:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63471',0,'event','',0),
(64822,1881,'2026-07-28 05:19:13','2026-07-28 11:19:13','This is an educational, non-certification class intended to provide introductory guidance on the mechanical/chemical properties, safety, and usage of various metals and metal alloys from a crafting perspective with a focus on jewelry making.\r\n\r\nThe class consists of 30 minutes of active material with a 15 minute Q&amp;A. Free to attend for all members.','Jewelry Class: Materials for Makers - Metals','','publish','closed','closed','','jewelry-class-materials-for-makers-metals','','','2026-08-04 10:53:40','2026-08-04 16:53:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64822',0,'event','',0),
(64825,1881,'2026-07-28 09:35:17','2026-07-28 15:35:17','This is an educational, non-certification class intended to provide introductory guidance on the physical/chemical properties, safety, and usage of various rocks, minerals, and gemstones from a crafting perspective with a focus on jewelry making.\r\n\r\nThe class consists of 30 minutes of active material with a 15 minute Q&amp;A. Free to attend for all members.','Jewelry Class: Materials for Makers - Gems/Stones','','publish','closed','closed','','jewelry-class-materials-for-makers-gems-stones','','','2026-07-28 09:35:17','2026-07-28 15:35:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64825',0,'event','',0),
(65036,1800,'2026-08-01 13:59:08','2026-08-01 19:59:08','This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and complete your homework before the class by reading the woodshop wiki page and all woodshop tool wiki pages. This class takes 2-3 hours depending on the number of attendees and experience.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThis class includes:\r\n\r\nRouter Table\r\n\r\nLaguna Band Saw\r\n\r\nJet Drum Sander\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe table saw/planer/jointer/miter saw will not be covered and are part of Woodshop A.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-29','','','2026-08-24 08:50:18','2026-08-24 14:50:18','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65036',0,'event','',0),
(65045,1800,'2026-08-01 16:22:33','2026-08-01 22:22:33','This training will authorize you to use 4 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and complete your homework before the class by reading the woodshop wiki page and all woodshop tool wiki pages. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience.\r\n\r\nThis class includes:\r\nDewalt compound sliding miter saw\r\nSaw Stop table saw\r\nPowermatic jointer\r\nGrizzly Planer\r\n\r\nThe router table/bandsaw/drum sander will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-29','','','2026-08-01 16:22:33','2026-08-01 22:22:33','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65045',0,'event','',0),
(66185,1800,'2026-08-26 23:18:16','2026-08-27 05:18:16','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-31','','','2026-08-31 16:47:47','2026-08-31 22:47:47','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66185',0,'event','',0),
(66587,1859,'2026-09-01 21:57:37','2026-09-02 03:57:37','<p data-path-to-node="1">Discover the meditative and tactile art of rug hooking in this comprehensive two-part workshop. This series takes you from a blank canvas to a textured masterpiece, covering everything from design theory to hands-on technique.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="2" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="3"><b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="0">Section 1: The Blueprint &amp; Palette </b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="4">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Theory &amp; Inspiration:</b> An informational deep dive into the history and styles of rug hooking.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Custom Design:</b> Learn how to translate your ideas onto backing fabric. You will spend this session sketching and finalizing your own original pattern.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="4,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="4,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Color Curation:</b> Explore Carol\'s library of fibers to select the perfect yarn weights and color palettes to bring your design to life. You will leave the session with color ideas so you can purchase your own yarn, or use the yarn at Denhac.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="5"><b data-path-to-node="5" data-index-in-node="0">Section 2: Hooking Technique &amp; Execution </b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Fundamentals:</b> Master the "pull-up" technique to create consistent loops and professional-grade texture.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Instructional Guidance:</b> Get hands-on coaching on tension control, navigating curves, and filling in your pattern efficiently.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Troubleshooting:</b> Learn how to fix common mistakes and finish the edges of your piece for a durable, long-lasting result.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr data-path-to-node="7" />\r\n\r\n<h3 data-path-to-node="8"><b data-path-to-node="8" data-index-in-node="0">Workshop Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="9">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Section One:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,0,0" data-index-in-node="21">conceptualization and material selection</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Section Two:</b> Focused on <b data-path-to-node="9,1,0" data-index-in-node="21">active crafting and technical mastery</b>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="9,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="9,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Take Home:</b> Your custom-designed project and the skills needed to finish it at your own pace.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<blockquote data-path-to-node="10">\r\n<p data-path-to-node="10,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0" data-index-in-node="0">Materials Note:</b> All specialized hooks, frames, and backing materials will be provided or discussed during the first session.</p>\r\n</blockquote>','Carol\'s Hooking Class for Rugs','','publish','closed','closed','','carols-hooking-class-for-rugs','','','2026-09-01 21:57:37','2026-09-02 03:57:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66587',0,'event','',0),
(67352,1899,'2026-09-15 17:21:00','2026-09-15 23:21:00','Help out, check in with projects, and have fun! No experience necessary. Come when you can, leave when you want.\r\n\r\nThanks! <img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f6e0-fe0f.png" alt=":hammer_and_wrench:" aria-label="hammer and wrench emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":hammer_and_wrench:" /><img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f383.png" alt=":jack_o_lantern:" aria-label="jack o lantern emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":jack_o_lantern:" />','Haunted House Club Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-club-office-hours-7','','','2026-09-15 17:22:21','2026-09-15 23:22:21','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67352',0,'event','',0),
(67353,1899,'2026-09-15 17:21:33','2026-09-15 23:21:33','Help out, check in with projects, and have fun! No experience necessary. Come when you can, leave when you want.\r\n\r\nThanks! <img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f6e0-fe0f.png" alt=":hammer_and_wrench:" aria-label="hammer and wrench emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":hammer_and_wrench:" /><img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f383.png" alt=":jack_o_lantern:" aria-label="jack o lantern emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":jack_o_lantern:" />','Haunted House Club Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-club-office-hours-8','','','2026-09-15 17:22:08','2026-09-15 23:22:08','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67353',0,'event','',0),
(67354,1899,'2026-09-15 17:21:54','2026-09-15 23:21:54','Help out, check in with projects, and have fun! No experience necessary. Come when you can, leave when you want.\r\n\r\nThanks! <img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f6e0-fe0f.png" alt=":hammer_and_wrench:" aria-label="hammer and wrench emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":hammer_and_wrench:" /><img src="https://a.slack-edge.com/production-standard-emoji-assets/16.0/google-medium/1f383.png" alt=":jack_o_lantern:" aria-label="jack o lantern emoji" data-stringify-emoji=":jack_o_lantern:" />','Haunted House Club Office Hours','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-club-office-hours-9','','','2026-09-15 17:21:54','2026-09-15 23:21:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67354',0,'event','',0),
(68208,1800,'2026-10-02 06:26:16','2026-10-02 12:26:16','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-35','','','2026-10-02 06:26:16','2026-10-02 12:26:16','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68208',0,'event','',0),
(68216,1800,'2026-10-02 06:28:55','2026-10-02 12:28:55','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-35','','','2026-10-02 06:28:55','2026-10-02 12:28:55','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68216',0,'event','',0),
(68658,1785,'2026-10-12 08:48:42','2026-10-12 14:48:42','<div id="Tj9Y4e" class="KP7TGc RjsPE" data-observe-id="u59cif" data-is-migration-recent="false">\r\n<div class="ua2Qrb">\r\n<div id="ResponsesView" class="rxsFue gmvbEd">\r\n<div class="nMw83b" data-observe-id="w6TSZ">\r\n<div id="i44">\r\n<div class="csgrRe">\r\n<div class="uMXdLb">\r\n<div class="RH5hzf RLS9Fe">\r\n<div class="lrKTG">\r\n<div class="o3Dpx" role="list">\r\n<div class="Qr7Oae" role="listitem">\r\n<div class="OxAavc NVbRL" data-item-id="1668403098">\r\n<div class="Ih4Dzb">\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Girls, this is feel-good-in-a-bra Fall.</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Bra shopping can stink and leave you deflated after not feeling good in anything, sending you back to your ole reliable sports bra- you’re not alone! Ever considered sewing your own bra to get the perfect look and fit? If not, now you have!</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Danielle will share what she has learned on her ~1 year journey making her own bras. Join her to learn the basics to kickstart your own adventure making a bra that FITS your girls and personality!</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Skill level: BEGINNER*</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">*We will NOT be touching a sewing machine in this class. However, intermediate experience sewing is HIGHLY recommended if planning to sew a bra after this class. Know your own line between taking on a challenge and setting yourself up for frustration.</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">In this class you will:</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-see that bra sewing is not actually very hard</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-take your measurements used for size selection of bra patterns</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-learn basic terminology</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-learn the fabric/notion names, use cases, and where to purchase them.</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Danielle will bring examples of each to see and feel</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-Get a free wired bra pattern and sew-along resources to start at home(or at Denhac!)</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-Make a paper bra for fitting</div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">-the first hands-on step to making your bra!</div>\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest "></div>\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Description of the event, feel free to just drop some bullet points instead of a full description and I can do the rest ">Please bring a laptop. Questions? Message Danielle on slack: @Danielle Heeb or post in #help-textiles</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class="Qr7Oae" role="listitem">\r\n<div class="OxAavc NVbRL" data-item-id="958949322">\r\n<div class="xMZTse Ih4Dzb">\r\n<div tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-describedby="c381" aria-label="What is the date and time"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class="Qr7Oae" role="listitem">\r\n<div class="OxAavc NVbRL" data-item-id="85882132">\r\n<div class="pYfr3c">\r\n<div class="prOLdf">\r\n<div class="g53bl">\r\n<div class="cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE" role="heading" aria-describedby="i.desc.85882132"><span class="M7eMe">Items needed</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class="Ih4Dzb">\r\n<div class="q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-label="Items needed">Laptop (used to find then download your size bra pattern)</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class="Qr7Oae" role="listitem">\r\n<div class="OxAavc" data-other-input="qSV85" data-other-hidden="MfYA1e" data-item-id="1034285363">\r\n<div class="pYfr3c">\r\n<div class="prOLdf">\r\n<div class="g53bl">\r\n<div id="c384" class="cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE" role="heading" aria-describedby="i.desc.1034285363"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>','Sew a bra that FITS!','','publish','closed','closed','','sew-a-bra-that-fits','','','2026-10-12 09:00:56','2026-10-12 15:00:56','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68658',0,'event','',0),
(68661,1864,'2026-10-12 08:53:34','2026-10-12 14:53:34','In this class you will learn the basics of crochet and start making a hat. We will cover the following stitches/techniques:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>- chain stitch</li>\r\n 	<li>- yarn over</li>\r\n 	<li>- single crochet</li>\r\n 	<li>- half double crochet</li>\r\n 	<li>- slip stitch</li>\r\n 	<li>- reading crochet patterns</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nYou will not finish your hat during class, but we will go over how to finish it by yourself.\r\n\r\nI\'m following this tutorial (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ufCgyVbmWkI) that you will also be able to reference.','Learn to Crochet a Beanie','','publish','closed','closed','','learn-to-crochet-a-beanie','','','2026-10-12 08:53:34','2026-10-12 14:53:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68661',0,'event','',0),
(68767,1899,'2026-10-14 15:58:44','2026-10-14 21:58:44','','Haunted House Postmortem - 2026','','publish','closed','closed','','haunted-house-postmortem-2026','','','2026-10-14 15:58:44','2026-10-14 21:58:44','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68767',0,'event','',0),
(62393,1932,'2026-05-26 10:49:25','2026-05-26 16:49:25','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-25','','','2026-05-26 10:49:25','2026-05-26 16:49:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62393',0,'event','',0),
(62976,1949,'2026-06-07 22:11:23','2026-06-08 04:11:23','<span style="color: #ff0000"><strong>Event Bookings Opens 7 days prior to class.</strong></span>\r\n\r\nOnly sign up for this class <em>after</em> you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.\r\n\r\nLearn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/cnc&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFti8EPPxpAeN3kX3Lq_2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\n<strong>HOMEWORK:</strong> <strong>On the</strong><strong> wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class.</strong> <strong>Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. <b data-stringify-type="bold">If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.</b></strong>','CNC Router Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization-class-57','','','2026-06-07 22:11:23','2026-06-08 04:11:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=62976',0,'event','',0),
(63467,1932,'2026-06-22 11:31:36','2026-06-22 17:31:36','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-26','','','2026-06-22 11:31:36','2026-06-22 17:31:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63467',0,'event','',0),
(63469,1932,'2026-06-22 11:36:09','2026-06-22 17:36:09','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-26','','','2026-06-22 11:36:09','2026-06-22 17:36:09','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63469',0,'event','',0),
(63958,2003,'2026-07-04 23:51:34','2026-07-05 05:51:34','Learn how to make a simple knot bag with Jackie!\r\n\r\nBeginners welcome! You will learn the basics of threading and using a domestic sewing machine, measuring and cutting fabric, and sewing a simple bag with a lining.\r\n\r\nHere is a link to the video tutorial we will follow together in class: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY1ubz3xa22/?igsh=MWxpaXZwd25mdnd1bw%3D%3D','Make and Take 100 - Knot Bag','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-100-knot-bag','','','2026-07-04 23:51:34','2026-07-05 05:51:34','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=63958',0,'event','',0),
(64095,2004,'2026-07-08 08:36:07','2026-07-08 14:36:07','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-5','','','2026-07-08 08:57:20','2026-07-08 14:57:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64095',0,'event','',0),
(64123,2004,'2026-07-09 00:45:31','2026-07-09 06:45:31','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-6','','','2026-07-09 00:45:31','2026-07-09 06:45:31','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64123',0,'event','',0),
(64125,2004,'2026-07-09 00:51:29','2026-07-09 06:51:29','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printer Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printer-authorization-7','','','2026-07-09 00:51:29','2026-07-09 06:51:29','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=64125',0,'event','',0),
(65189,2003,'2026-08-06 08:37:40','2026-08-06 14:37:40','Make an apron perfectly suited to your needs! Jackie will help you make a simple apron which you can customize through fabric choice, pockets, trim, etc.\r\n\r\nDomestic sewing machine experience is recommended but not required. You\'ll learn how to measure and cut out a pattern, sew simple pockets, finish edges, and more.','Make and Take 200 - Aprons','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-200-aprons','','','2026-08-06 08:37:40','2026-08-06 14:37:40','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65189',0,'event','',0),
(65491,1949,'2026-08-12 15:06:37','2026-08-12 21:06:37','Only sign up for this class after you\'ve completed the homework section of the wiki.<br aria-hidden="true" />Learn to use the CNC Routers and get authorized to use them. The CNC Routers are capable of machining almost any material because it uses a spinning end mill to selectively remove stock material until you\'re left with your final part. These machines are most commonly used on sheets of plywood, hardwood, polycarbonate, acrylic, and aluminum.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge. To learn more about our CNC Machines read the wiki.\r\n\r\nHOMEWORK: On the wiki page is a Homework section, you must watch the homework videos and familiarize yourself with everything before showing up to class. Although you can still take the class, you will need to know how to do CAD and CAM using Fusion 360 or some other workflow before you\'ll have any files to run on these machines. If you’ve never used a CNC machine then it is highly recommended that you sign up for a CAD/CAM class or request one in the #compuer-aided-design channel before signing up for this CNC authorization.','CNC Router Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','cnc-router-authorization','','','2026-08-12 15:06:37','2026-08-12 21:06:37','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65491',0,'event','',0),
(66174,1932,'2026-08-26 23:09:02','2026-08-27 05:09:02','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-34','','','2026-08-27 10:20:36','2026-08-27 16:20:36','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66174',0,'event','',0),
(66192,1932,'2026-08-26 23:56:42','2026-08-27 05:56:42','<strong>New in September:</strong> With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-33','','','2026-08-26 23:58:20','2026-08-27 05:58:20','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66192',0,'event','',0),
(66371,2004,'2026-08-30 17:00:02','2026-08-30 23:00:02','Bring your painting projects and work on them with fellow denhac members! All skill level are welcome. No experience required. Great opportunity to share techniques and bounce ideas off each other.\r\n\r\nNothing to paint? No problem! Models will be available to paint, as well as paints and materials can be shared.\r\n\r\n<strong>Host:</strong> <a href="https://denhac.org/member/9K9K">Helix</a>','Miniature/Project Painting Party','','publish','closed','closed','','miniature-project-painting-party-2','','','2026-08-30 17:00:02','2026-08-30 23:00:02','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66371',0,'event','',0),
(66377,2004,'2026-08-30 17:06:42','2026-08-30 23:06:42','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the Large Format 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-2','','','2026-08-30 17:06:42','2026-08-30 23:06:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66377',0,'event','',0),
(66590,1909,'2026-09-01 22:00:24','2026-09-02 04:00:24','<p data-path-to-node="3">Unlock the potential of precision cutting! Join <b data-path-to-node="3" data-index-in-node="48">Xavier</b> for a hands-on introduction to our Cricut ecosystem. Whether you want to create custom vinyl decals, heat-transfer apparel, or intricate paper crafts, this class is your starting point for "push-button" perfection.</p>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="5">In this session, we’ll bridge the gap between your screen and the cutting mat:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-path-to-node="6">\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Design Space Basics:</b> Navigate the software to create, upload, and manipulate simple shapes and text.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Material Selection:</b> Learn which blades and mats to use for vinyl, cardstock, and more.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<p data-path-to-node="6,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">The "Final Print":</b> From "weeding" your design to the final application, you’ll walk through the entire production process.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nYou will leave this class with a complete project and the knowledge of how to replicate what you\'ve learned.\r\n\r\n<strong>No authorizations needed for this class.</strong> You will need to know how to navigate a computer using a mouse and keyboard.','Cricut 100 - Intro to Cricut','','publish','closed','closed','','cricut-100-intro-to-cricut','','','2026-09-09 19:01:01','2026-09-10 01:01:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66590',0,'event','',0),
(66922,2003,'2026-09-07 13:19:16','2026-09-07 19:19:16','<h2 dir="ltr">Overview</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Join Jackie to make a spooky-season collar with a spiderweb motif, including how to complete unique cuts, make your own tie, install interfacing, and turn the piece right-side out.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What You\'ll Learn</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Creating a fabric tie</li>\r\n 	<li>Installing interfacing</li>\r\n 	<li>Cutting in curved lines</li>\r\n 	<li>Turning a sewn piece inside out (right-side out) cleanly</li>\r\n 	<li>Straight-stitching on contrasting fabric to make a web design pop</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Who This Is For</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Best suited for students who already know their way around the machine, intermediate beginner level, the tie is essentially self-made bias tape, which means precise cutting and a lot of pressing, plus interfacing installation.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What\'s Provided / What to Bring</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li><strong>Provided:</strong> denhac\'s fabric stock is available to use for this class</li>\r\n 	<li><strong>Bring:</strong> Optional — a non-stretch, tightly woven fabric (like cotton poplin) works best so the web stitching stays crisp; pick a fabric/thread combo with enough contrast that the web pattern is visible. If you want a spider embellishment, bring one of your own (a plastic ring spider, a bead-and-pipe-cleaner spider, or a spider brooch) — denhac won\'t have these on hand.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Before You Arrive</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Watch the tutorial we\'ll be following: [see link below]</li>\r\n 	<li>Suggested machine settings if you want to test your machine beforehand: tension 5, stitch length 3, straight stitch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Links</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Pattern: Will be linked shortly</li>\r\n 	<li>Instructions/tutorial video: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcwevcHhMbg/?igsi=Mno5NTd3M293OG5t">https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcwevcHhMbg/?igsi=Mno5NTd3M293OG5t</a></li>\r\n</ul>','Make and take - intermediate beginner - Halloween Spider-Web Collar','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-intermediate-beginner-halloween-spider-web-collar','','','2026-10-12 22:30:10','2026-10-13 04:30:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66922',0,'event','',0),
(66924,2003,'2026-09-07 13:25:04','2026-09-07 19:25:04','<h2 dir="ltr">Overview</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Make a fully-lined tote bag you can customize through fabric choice, pockets, and trim.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What You\'ll Learn</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>Measuring and cutting out a pattern</li>\r\n 	<li>Sewing simple pockets</li>\r\n 	<li>Finishing edges</li>\r\n 	<li>Assembling a lined bag</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Who This Is For</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Beginners welcome — domestic sewing machine experience is recommended but not required.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What\'s Provided / What to Bring</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li><strong>Provided:</strong> denhac\'s fabric stock is available to use for this class</li>\r\n 	<li><strong>Bring:</strong> Optional — bring your own fabric if you want a specific color/print not in the shop\'s stock</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir="ltr"></p>','Make and take - beginner - Tote bag','','publish','closed','closed','','make-and-take-beginner-tote-bag','','','2026-09-07 13:25:04','2026-09-07 19:25:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66924',0,'event','',0),
(68220,1932,'2026-10-02 06:30:08','2026-10-02 12:30:08','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-38','','','2026-10-03 11:52:50','2026-10-03 17:52:50','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68220',0,'event','',0),
(68355,2004,'2026-10-06 06:46:10','2026-10-06 12:46:10','<div class="p-rich_text_section">This class is for upgrading authorization from using the existing fleet of printers only, <strong>if you do not have a prior authorization to use the 3D printers this class is not for you, and we will not authorize you for either set of printers.</strong> Class will take ~1 hour or so. It assumes you have some experience with 3D printing, and understand slicer basics as taught in the 3D FDM printing classes.Topics covered:</div>\r\n<ul class="p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested" data-stringify-type="unordered-list" data-list-tree="true" data-indent="0" data-border="0">\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Loading/unloading the Prusa XL/Snapmaker U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Installing/cleaning the build plate</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Understanding where menu items are on the Prusa XL/U1</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">PrusaSlicer/Snapmaker Orca configuration</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Painting objects in PrusaSlicer/Snapmaker Orca</li>\r\n 	<li data-stringify-indent="0" data-stringify-border="0">Peculiarities when printing on the Prusa XL/U1 you should keep in mind</li>\r\n</ul>','Multi-tool printing upgrade class (Only sign up if you’re authorized on basic 3D Printers)','','publish','closed','closed','','multi-tool-printing-upgrade-class-only-sign-up-if-youre-authorized-on-basic-3d-printers-8','','','2026-10-06 06:46:10','2026-10-06 12:46:10','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68355',0,'event','',0),
(69331,1899,'2026-10-27 14:19:46','2026-10-27 20:19:46','All materials will be provided.\r\n<p style="text-align: center;">Pumpkin carving/painting, tee shirt painting, and tee shirt bleaching.</p>','Spooky Make and Take - Haunted House Club','','publish','closed','closed','','spooky-make-and-take-haunted-house-club','','','2026-10-27 14:21:26','2026-10-27 20:21:26','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69331',0,'event','',0);
