(65090,2089,'2026-08-03 10:59:54','2026-08-03 16:59:54','This training will authorize you to use 4 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and complete your homework before the class by reading the woodshop wiki page and all woodshop tool wiki pages. This class takes ~3 hours depending on the number of attendees and experience.\r\n\r\nThis class includes:\r\n\r\nDewalt compound sliding miter saw\r\n\r\nSaw Stop table saw\r\n\r\nPowermatic jointer\r\n\r\nGrizzly Planer\r\n\r\nThe router table/bandsaw/drum sander will not be covered in this class, and are part of Woodshop B.\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization “A”','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-33','','','2026-08-03 10:59:54','2026-08-03 16:59:54','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=65090',0,'event','',0),
(66482,2036,'2026-09-01 07:01:51','2026-09-01 13:01:51','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="presentation" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-6','','','2026-09-01 07:01:51','2026-09-01 13:01:51','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=66482',0,'event','',0),
(67184,2006,'2026-09-11 21:07:11','2026-09-12 03:07:11','<h2 dir="ltr">Overview</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Bead your own Christmas ornament by hand-sewing beads in a pattern around a glass ball.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What You\'ll Learn</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li>How to read and follow a beading pattern</li>\r\n 	<li>Technique for sewing/wrapping beads around a curved glass surface</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Who This Is For</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Beginners with no prior beading experience,  this is a hand technique, not machine-based.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">What\'s Provided / What to Bring</h2>\r\n<ul dir="ltr">\r\n 	<li><strong>Provided:</strong> Beading patterns will be provided</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir="ltr">Notes</h2>\r\n<p dir="ltr">Goal for the class is to complete/learn the pattern, not necessarily leave with a fully finished ornament, similar in spirit to other make-and-takes where finishing isn\'t guaranteed in-session.</p>','Beading with Eric! Make and take','','publish','closed','closed','','beading-with-eric-make-and-take','','','2026-09-11 21:07:11','2026-09-12 03:07:11','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=67184',0,'event','',0),
(67240,728,'2026-09-13 09:24:02','2026-09-13 15:24:02','','denhac-ai-sig-logo-01','','inherit','closed','closed','','wp-attachment-wp-attachment-denhac-ai-sig-logo-01','','','2026-09-13 09:24:21','2026-09-13 15:24:21','',56101,'https://denhac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/denhac-ai-sig-logo-01.jpg',0,'attachment','',0),
(68133,1686,'2026-10-01 13:55:57','2026-10-01 19:55:57','Learn to use the CNC CO2 Lasers and get authorized to use them. The laser cutters emit a high power infrared beam of light, reflect it off the mirrors on the gantry of the machine, and into your material encased by a stream of high pressure air to both ignite and extinguish a fire that precisely burns through material. These machines are perfect for engraving images onto and cutting precise and accurate shapes from flat sheets of material especially wood, leather, fabric, paper, acrylic, and more.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our Lasers (including a broader materials list) <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/laser-cutter-ultra-secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read the wiki</a>.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no charge.\r\n\r\nTeacher: @Craig','Laser Cutter Authorization Class','','trash','closed','closed','','laser-cutter-authorization-class-56__trashed','','','2026-10-09 15:15:38','2026-10-09 21:15:38','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68133',0,'event','',0),
(68205,2089,'2026-10-02 06:31:06','2026-10-02 12:31:06','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nNew in September: With the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings. These classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible.\r\n\r\nThis training will authorize you to use 3 major woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools. Register for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://denhac.org/wiki/category/equipment/wood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;usd=2&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hiqe9ZjxtZNT3fbPQtPoh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class takes ~3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Saw Stop table saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Powermatic jointer</li>\r\n 	<li>Dewalt planer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>The router table will not be covered in this class, and is now part of Woodshop B.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','Woodshop Authorization "A"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-a-39','','','2026-10-02 06:31:06','2026-10-02 12:31:06','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68205',0,'event','',0),
(68211,2089,'2026-10-02 06:27:23','2026-10-02 12:27:23','<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline"><span style="color: #ff3232;text-decoration: underline">Bookings open 7 days prior to event.</span></span></strong>\r\n\r\nWith the addition of the band saw to the training-required list, we\'re breaking up the "General Woodshop Authorization Class" into two classes "Woodshop A" and "Woodshop B", and merging in bandsaw and drum sander trainings.\r\n\r\nThese classes cover different equipment and do not build on each other, so the order in which you take them does not matter. We hope this new format will make classes shorter and more digestible. This training will authorize you to use 3 woodworking power tools. This training is mandatory for all denhac members before you\'re allowed to use these tools.\r\n\r\nRegister for this training and <strong>complete your homework</strong> <strong>before the class by reading <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdenhac.org%2Fwiki%2Fcategory%2Fequipment%2Fwood-working&amp;sa=D&amp;source=calendar&amp;ust=1777774200000000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wDo4x_6MjMy37owJZcE-C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the woodshop wiki page</a> and all woodshop tool wiki pages</strong>. This class will probably take 2-3 hours depending on number of attendees and experience. This class includes:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Router Table</li>\r\n 	<li>Band Saw</li>\r\n 	<li>Drum Sander</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>This class is offered to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</strong>','Woodshop Authorization "B"','','publish','closed','closed','','woodshop-authorization-b-36','','','2026-10-02 06:27:23','2026-10-02 12:27:23','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68211',0,'event','',0),
(68358,2004,'2026-10-06 06:47:14','2026-10-06 12:47:14','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-7','','','2026-10-06 06:47:14','2026-10-06 12:47:14','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68358',0,'event','',0),
(68361,2036,'2026-10-06 06:49:04','2026-10-06 12:49:04','<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">Please <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki page</a> for the grizzly mill before signing up for this class!</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>Learn to use the Grizzly Manual Milling Machine and get authorized to use it. This machine is good for milling metals as hard as steel, but the work piece must be moved by hand (unlike a CNC Milling Machine), making curves and intricate parts a bit more difficult to machine.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_1746005445.712789" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="listitem" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="1746005445.712789">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__background p-message_pane_message__message c-message_kit__message" role="presentation" data-qa="message_container" data-qa-unprocessed="false" data-qa-placeholder="false">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__hover" role="document" data-qa-hover="true">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__actions c-message_kit__actions--default">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__gutter__right" role="presentation" data-qa="message_content">\r\n<div class="c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text">\r\n<div class="c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text" data-qa="message-text">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer" data-qa="block-kit-renderer">\r\n<div class="p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_block" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="p-rich_text_section">We will meet in the classroom for ~1 hour going over basics of machining and then 2 hours out in the metal shop for machine overview and skills test. Please wear appropriate attire.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>To learn more about the Grizzly Manual Mill, <a href="https://denhac.org/wiki/grizzly-mill">read the wiki</a>.</div>\r\n<div id="message-list_bottomSpacer" class="c-virtual_list__item" role="presentation" data-qa="virtual-list-item" data-item-key="bottomSpacer"></div>','Milling Machine Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','milling-machine-authorization-class-7','','','2026-10-06 22:59:42','2026-10-07 04:59:42','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68361',0,'event','',0),
(68950,2116,'2026-10-19 12:23:48','2026-10-19 18:23:48','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metalshop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metalshop-safety-6','','','2026-10-19 12:24:17','2026-10-19 18:24:17','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=68950',0,'event','',0),
(69451,2111,'2026-10-31 12:19:01','2026-10-31 18:19:01','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-10','','','2026-10-31 12:19:01','2026-10-31 18:19:01','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69451',0,'event','',0),
(69457,2004,'2026-10-31 12:21:04','2026-10-31 18:21:04','Learn to use the Prusa Mk4S and Core One (Our fleet of desktop FDM 3d printers) and get authorized to use them. FDM printing uses a plastic filament fed into a heated nozzle like a hot glue gun to deposit plastic until your part is complete. These machines are great for rapid prototyping with PLA, PETG, and TPU.\r\n\r\nThis class does not authorize users to use the multi-tool 3d printers, but this class is a prerequisite for the advanced workshop that will teach you how to use them. This class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about our 3d printers read the wiki.','FDM 3D Printing Authorization','','publish','closed','closed','','fdm-3d-printing-authorization-12','','','2026-10-31 12:21:04','2026-10-31 18:21:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69457',0,'event','',0),
(69467,2213,'2026-10-31 12:29:25','2026-10-31 18:29:25','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left;"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-26','','','2026-10-31 12:29:25','2026-10-31 18:29:25','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69467',0,'event','',0),
(69470,2213,'2026-10-31 12:30:04','2026-10-31 18:30:04','<blockquote>\r\n<p style="text-align: left;"><b data-stringify-type="bold">Metal Shop Safety Authorization Required</b></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nCompleting and passing this class will authorize you to operate the TIG welder in the metal shop. We will discuss safe operation of the machine, the welding process, and what to look for in an ideal weld.\r\n\r\nIt is required to take the metal shop safety course prior to the TIG welding class.\r\n\r\nYou must wear appropriate clothing to the class. All clothing MUST be made from natural fibers. Closed-toe shoes, preferably resistant to metal chips / slag. Optimal: boots with long pants covering the tops. No loose clothing or accessories, tie up hair. Protect yourself from the UV light TIG produces! Recommended to wear long sleeve shirts and use sunscreen on exposed skin. All other PPE will be provided.\r\n\r\nThis class is available to denhac members only, and at no additional charge.','TIG Welder Authorization Class','','publish','closed','closed','','tig-welder-authorization-class-27','','','2026-10-31 12:30:04','2026-10-31 18:30:04','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69470',0,'event','',0),
(69473,2116,'2026-10-31 12:37:46','2026-10-31 18:37:46','This will cover the angle grinders, bench grinders, grizzly band saw, and the drill press.\r\n\r\nPlease do not wear loose clothing. Jeans and a T-shirt with closed toed shoes are best, hair needs to be pulled back. We have an assortment of used Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) but it is best to bring your own if you have it. This includes PPE like safety glasses, hearing protection, and gloves. Tank tops and v neckline shirts shouldn\'t be worn for the class\r\n\r\nThis class is available to all denhac members, and at no additional charge.\r\n\r\nPlease be punctual. Members arriving late may be required to reschedule for a later class due to missed material.\r\n\r\nTo learn more about the metalshop, read the wiki','Metalshop Safety','','publish','closed','closed','','metalshop-safety-9','','','2026-10-31 12:37:46','2026-10-31 18:37:46','',0,'https://denhac.org/?post_type=event&p=69473',0,'event','',0),
